{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:08:04.308Z","ordinal":112410,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a7bf-24d4-7360-91c0-22424b067bae","call_id":"call_94f3d9c741ad4612a03383339b029a30","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #402 is at `bd7fb1cf`, and its visible Linux, test-matrix, JS/TS, Cloudflare, and CodeQL checks pass; Entire Gates is still pending. The PR body remains stale: it describes head `8520d9c8`, RC2, and qualification as pending.\\n\\nThe local exact-head suite recorded one fixture-only failure because its wrapper lacked two environment variables configured in CI. The final SUITE claim remains held. I relayed that the owner should refresh the PR body before marking it ready or releasing it; I made no changes.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**APPROVED.** Commit `2dbe565b` stays within the authorized two-file scope. The checker now rejects generic `Error: Cannot find module` as infrastructure failure while retaining recognition of TS and Rust diagnostics. The added tests cover those cases and fail closed when the checker is unavailable.\\n\\nNo tests were run. Minor wording caveat: the mocked “candidate syntax failures” test verifies fail-closed behavior during checker unavailability; it does not demonstrate an actual syntax diagnostic.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audit sent to the release owner. The exact 05913af5 source gate is still running; after it passes, the live provider matrix is next, but the GATEWAY claim remains held by the RC15 E5 worktree. The qualification record still points to older commits and needs refresh after candidate-bound evidence is complete.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a7bc-bec1-76c3-8e8c-1894005f2121","create_time":1793815684.308643}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
