{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:08:16.003Z","ordinal":112414,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a7bc-bec1-76c3-8e8c-1894005f2121","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeb748a68f481a38fac057c6c2e7224","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The original v1.1.0 version cannot be published: it was declared failed and versions are immutable. I’m continuing the previously selected path of qualifying its full roadmap for v1.1.2.\n\nOn `bd7fb1cf`, GitHub CI and CodeQL pass, and CI uploaded a Linux package artifact. The owner’s local `make test` ended with one fixture-configuration failure (2,371 passed, 1 failed, 5 skipped); the corresponding CI jobs passed with the required fixture configured. I recorded the result, but the `SUITE` claim remains with `claude-code`, so I did not rerun it.\n\nPR #402 is still a draft. Its description is stale, the release documents are uncommitted and still have inaccurate shipped/gate wording, and the independent audit says the “Entire Gates” check is pending. The remaining review limitations are documented in the draft; the audit’s corrections were sent to the release coordinator. No tag or release files have been published.\n\n[Release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md) · [Qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md)\n\n**Next:** the release owner must address the fixture-only local failure or explicitly classify it against the green CI evidence, correct and commit the release documentation, refresh PR #402, and complete the remaining owner-only release steps."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793815690474,"completed_at_ms":1793815696003}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:08:16.223Z","ordinal":112415,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeb748a68f481a38fac057c6c2e7224","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The original v1.1.0 version cannot be published: it was declared failed and versions are immutable. I’m continuing the previously selected path of qualifying its full roadmap for v1.1.2.\n\nOn `bd7fb1cf`, GitHub CI and CodeQL pass, and CI uploaded a Linux package artifact. The owner’s local `make test` ended with one fixture-configuration failure (2,371 passed, 1 failed, 5 skipped); the corresponding CI jobs passed with the required fixture configured. I recorded the result, but the `SUITE` claim remains with `claude-code`, so I did not rerun it.\n\nPR #402 is still a draft. Its description is stale, the release documents are uncommitted and still have inaccurate shipped/gate wording, and the independent audit says the “Entire Gates” check is pending. The remaining review limitations are documented in the draft; the audit’s corrections were sent to the release coordinator. No tag or release files have been published.\n\n[Release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md) · [Qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md)\n\n**Next:** the release owner must address the fixture-only local failure or explicitly classify it against the green CI evidence, correct and commit the release documentation, refresh PR #402, and complete the remaining owner-only release steps.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a7bc-bec1-76c3-8e8c-1894005f2121","create_time":1793815690.4138749,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeb748a68f481a38fac057c6c2e7224","turn_id":"01a1a7bc-bec1-76c3-8e8c-1894005f2121","role":"assistant"},