{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:15:57.543Z","ordinal":112640,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a7c6-5d67-7e52-9fc2-54d6e73ed847","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for release-document accuracy. The source review items are acknowledged, and the `2dbe565b` diagnostic fix is present at exact PR head `bd7fb1cf`. I did not edit files or run tests/builds.\n\n1. **The docs say the release has shipped, but publication is still pending.** The current PR #402 is open at `bd7fb1cf`; GitHub reports no `v1.1.2` release, and the qualification checklist leaves the tag and publication unchecked. Change “v1.1.2 ships” / “Stable release … shipped” in [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3) and [release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:3) to distinguish the owner’s decision to ship with limitations from actual publication.\n\n2. **The exact-head gate is referenced but absent, and the release summary overstates the local result.** The qualification record links to `#final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf` at line 3, but contains no corresponding section. The release notes say the exact source head passed the full local suite at line 71; the reported `bd7fb1cf` local run had one failure, `eval_version_probe_storage`, because its CI fixture variables were missing. Record that result and the separate CI result instead of calling the local run fully green. The CI status text at [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:65) is also stale: current checks on `bd7fb1cf` pass for CodeQL and the named CI jobs; Entire Gates remains pending.\n\n3. **The cache limitation is overstated.** The release note says the server-kind cache “never expires or invalidates” at [v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:46). At exact head, readable discovery overwrites the cached kind, including with `unknown` ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1208)); stale identity is retained on unavailable, 404, or missing-model paths. Describe the lack of expiry and those retention paths specifically. The resulting stale `X-Task-Class` risk is real.\n\n4. **Clarify the matrix-provenance limitation.** The release notes say any clean repository at the claimed commit passes ([v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:49)), while the runner checks Git `HEAD` and cleanliness, then checks installed provenance against the same commit and pinned archive digest ([tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:359), [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:403)). If the remaining limitation is that this does not prove the archive was built reproducibly from that source tree, state that directly; the current wording obscures what is and is not bound."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a7c6-5d20-72a3-8d30-1c60208ce567","create_time":1793816157.5431259,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3826}}
