b1cf + uncommitted release docs: CHANGES_REQUESTED. Required: remove shipped/stable assertions; fix/remove missing #final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf anchor; report local make test accurately (2371 pass, 1 fixture-env failure, 5 skipped) and distinguish green exact-head GitHub jobs from pending Entire; refresh qualification checklist/status; narrow server-kind cache wording (readable discovery overwrites, stale kind retained on unavailable/404/not-listed paths); clarify archive digest is not proven reproducibly bound to verified checkout. Other listed limitations directionally accurate. PR #402 still draft/open, no tag/release. Docs remain claimed by claude-code; no edits made.\n2026-11-04T18:23:43Z RELEASE SUITE claude-code: final exact-head gate on bd7fb1cf complete. make build exit 0; make test exit 2 = cargo tests 254+1+4+1 pass, npm test 2377 tests / 2371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped (sole failure eval_version_probe_storage: NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT/NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT unset in my wrapper); make aborted there so test-scope-procs.sh and security_gates.sh did not run in it - I ran them separately: test-scope-procs exit 0, security_gates exit 0; eval_version_probe_storage rerun alone with /mnt/nexus-eval-ci + /opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime: 1/1 pass. Logs /tmp/rg-final-*.log. Per the owner, this was the one final gate; the rerun was one file. SUITE free.\n2026-11-04T18:25:41Z PUSH claude-code: PR402 head 40d553b5 = bd7fb1cf + docs-only commit (release notes + qualification record; git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' empty; security_gates.sh passed on this head). SUITE released.\n2026-11-04T18:31:24Z PUSH claude-code: PR402 head fafbf6d5: docs-only corrections after the independent docs review (WP-1107 scope stated as vLLM-only strict schemas, CHANGELOG.md, review table, limitations). security_gates passed; SUITE released.\n2026-11-04T18:31:44Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW claude-code (reviewer agent, not the author): release docs + version bump bd7fb1cf..40d553b5 = REQUEST CHANGES, all corrections applied in fafbf6d5 (docs only): HIGH WP-1107 delivered in reduced scope (strict schemas on the vLLM path only; llama.cpp/Ollama keep native schemas; no grammar/format constraint; hybrid grammars not implemented); CHANGELOG.md; limitations wording; review table; G1.1-5 wording. Numbers/hashes/version bump verified correct. Full text on PR402.\n2026-11-04T20:27:10Z CLAIM claude-code: FILE_cli_src_agent.ts FILE_cli_test_step_loop.test.ts on v1/v112-release for the owner-approved fix of Entire trail 145 HIGH finding (01M6KXTK2G0S): in --step mode the parallel read_file branch in agent.ts runs endStep();continue and bypasses the STEP_PAUSED check. Plan: regression test RED first, minimal fix, focused tests, then ONE new exact-head gate. Owner decision 2026-11-04 ~19:00 UTC: 'Fix the HIGH, rerun the gate'.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md.released-20261103T025719Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2.md\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":82364}},"started_at_ms":1793824049855,"completed_at_ms":1793824049856}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:27:30.147Z","ordinal":112752,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3a7ecd4e-d3db-44b3-8d6e-26bb65b9a433","process_id":"76481","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commits/fafbf6d598372f12c045cd08ab623b0c95f884ae/check-runs --jq '.check_runs[] | select(.name == \"Entire Gates\") | {status,conclusion,started_at,completed_at,details_url,output}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commits/fafbf6d598372f12c045cd08ab623b0c95f884ae/check-runs --jq '.check_runs[] | select(.name == \"Entire Gates\") | {status,conclusion,started_at,completed_at,details_url,output}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"completed_at\":\"2026-11-04T19:22:30Z\",\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"details_url\":\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/145/changes/nexus-code/140\",\"output\":{\"annotations_count\":0,\"annotations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/check-runs/126777524056/annotations\",\"summary\":\"- ❌ **Approvals**: failed — No reviewers have approved this trail\\n- ✅ **Checks**: passed — CI checks have passed\\n- ❌ **Findings**: failed — Unresolved findings: 1 high severity\\n- ✅ **Up to date**: passed — Up to date\\n\\n[Trail #140 on Entire](https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/145/changes/nexus-code/140)\",\"text\":null,\"title\":\"2 blocking gates not passing\"},\"started_at\":\"2026-11-04T18:31:29Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":472226807}},"started_at_ms":1793824049674,"completed_at_ms":1793824050147}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:27:30.605Z","ordinal":112753,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8aae7076-f54a-4a76-b8ea-3249ba7578ae","process_id":"44944","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short --branch; git log -4 --oneline --decorate; sed -n '1,80p' docs/releases/v1.1.2.md; sed -n '1,85p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; rg -n 'final exact|final-head|bd7fb|fafbf6|2371|eval_version_probe|Entire Gates|cache|archive digest|checklist|stable|ships' docs/releases/v1.1.2.md docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short --branch; git log -4 --oneline --decorate; sed -n '1,80p' docs/releases/v1.1.2.md; sed -n '1,85p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; rg -n 'final exact|final-head|bd7fb|fafbf6|2371|eval_version_probe|Entire Gates|cache|archive digest|checklist|stable|ships' docs/releases/v1.1.2.md docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/v112-release...origin/v1/v112-release [ahead 1]\nc5ceb2e5 (HEAD -> v1/v112-release) test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\nfafbf6d5 (origin/v1/v112-release) docs(release): correct WP-1107 scope and the review record\n40d553b5 docs(release): v1.1.2 release notes and qualification record\nbd7fb1cf chore(release): bump to 1.1.2\n# Nexus Code v1.1.2\n\n**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.2, which ships **with known limitations** that the owner accepted explicitly. They are listed in full below, and the [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) carries the evidence and the open items. The tag is created after the release pull request merges; these notes describe the source that is tagged.\n\nv1.1.2 delivers the WP-1101 to WP-1108 roadmap that was originally planned for v1.1.0, with WP-1107 delivered in reduced form (see below). The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files, and v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. Version numbers are immutable, so the roadmap work is assigned to v1.1.2. No `v1.1.2-rc.*` tag was ever published; the candidates that carried those names are superseded.\n\n## What is in this release\n\n- **WP-1101, local OpenTelemetry tracing.** GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tool dispatch and compaction, written locally with payload-free attributes. Trace output is confined to the approved trace directory.\n- **WP-1102, flight-recorder credential redaction.** Credential redaction across traces, CLI errors and debug journals.\n- **WP-1103, versioned evaluation datasets.** Datasets with separate examples and oracles and regression and benchmark splits; candidate prompts do not carry oracle paths or commands.\n- **WP-1104, standalone `nexus eval`.** A packaged command with dataset selection, run count, an isolated home and structured score output. It runs outside the repository checkout.\n- **WP-1105, deterministic code evaluators.** AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary and JSON-repair evaluators and tool-call syntax telemetry (`toolCallSyntax`). **The evaluators are a library: no dataset task uses them yet.** See the limitations below.\n- **WP-1106, single-step loop mode.** `--step`, and `/step` in the REPL and the TUI, pause after one agent turn for operator confirmation.\n- **WP-1107, bounded tool schemas (reduced scope).** A bounded schema compiler for the four harness tools, and strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**. llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas: no grammar or format constraint is sent for them, and the hybrid reasoning grammars from the roadmap are not implemented. The 99.5% valid-tool-call target was **not measured** against live providers; see below.\n- **WP-1108, dependency modernisation.** The pending Dependabot updates were triaged and merged. `cargo deny` is clean, there are no deprecated npm packages, and a CycloneDX SBOM is generated.\n- **Non-progress recovery.** A bounded recovery state machine for repeated unproductive tool calls, with state-based same-step progress and unique tool-call ids ([#398](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398)).\n- **Specialist orchestration and independent review.** Specialist roles with tool allow-lists, an evidence-based review boundary for operation units, and redaction of credential-named keys in review evidence ([#396](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/396), [#401](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/401)).\n\n## Fixed\n\n### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n\nWhen a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n\nResume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\n\n- Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\n- Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` carries two messages and asserts that each appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\n\n### Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\n\nThe v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n\n## Known limitations (owner waiver)\n\nIndependent reviewers examined the release source and returned REQUEST CHANGES on the WP-1105 evaluator work and on the WP-1107 provider work. The owner decided to ship v1.1.2 with the findings below open, and to fix only one of them (the `typecheck_clean` diagnostic pattern, commit `2dbe565b`). Nothing in this list has been fixed in this release. The review reports are on [PR #402](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402).\n\n### Not measured\n\n- **Constrained decoding, gate G1.1-4: NOT MET, NOT MEASURED.** The target is at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. Strict function schemas are connected on the vLLM request path and tested locally with mock servers; llama.cpp and Ollama requests do not use them. No measurement against live llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama endpoints was made, because the shared gateway resource was held by another release stream. Do not read this release as having met that target.\n- **Task quality.** The benchmark fixture checks execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving or provider quality.\n\n### Provider handling (WP-1107)\n\n- **The server-kind cache has no expiry or invalidation.** A readable model-list refresh overwrites the cached kind. When a refresh is unavailable (503, bad JSON, dropped connection, 404 or the model not listed), the previous kind is retained, including its strict flag. If the server on that endpoint is replaced and then answers that way, the stale kind stays (the cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint, so a fresh client for the same endpoint inherits it), and a retained gateway kind sends the `X-Task-Class` header to the non-gateway server that replaced it on the same endpoint. The rule that standalone local servers do not receive `X-Task-Class` (REQ-PRV-109) therefore holds on the success path and for non-gateway kinds, not in that replacement case.\n- **Null normalisation covers well-formed native tool calls only.** Calls that needed JSON repair, and text-mode tool calls, still reach read tracking with `null` optional fields. The normaliser also strips an explicit `null` from every optional property of every tool for all providers, including properties whose schema allows null (measured on a synthetic tool; real MCP tools were not checked).\n- **Request counting can turn off.** After a transient `/version` failure, or a 404 or missing-model refresh, a retained vLLM kind no longer matches the advertised source, so the agent probably reports that request counting is unavailable.\n- **Matrix provenance is not bound to the checkout content.** The provider-matrix runner verifies the installed archive digest and that a clean checkout is at the claimed commit, but it does not prove the archive was built from that checkout: any clean repository at the claimed commit passes. A matrix result is evidence about the archive only if the archive digest is pinned by the person reading it.\n- **Ollama identity.** A transient `/api/version` failure on a successful refresh still drops the kind to unknown.\n\n### Code evaluators (WP-1105)\n\n- **Fail-open overlay (rated HIGH by the reviewer; the only HIGH finding still open).** Build and typecheck run in the baseline workspace with only candidate edits to `.ts`, `.mts`, `.cts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, `.jsx`, `.rs` and `.py` files overlaid. Edits to any other file (`.go`, `.c`, `.json` and so on) are invisible to the build, so a change in one of those files that breaks the build can pass. Honest changes to such inputs, for example a new JSON module, can fail.\n- **Shadowing.** A candidate can still shadow the checker through `node_modules` or an in-repo build helper, because those files are overlaid as source.\n- **Large workspaces.** The runner takes two full workspace snapshots even for build-only tasks. A workspace with a very large `node_modules` is refused (5 second traversal deadline, 50,000 entries).\n- **No resource limits on evaluator commands** (memory, process count, disk); in-process parsers have no timeout (a 65 MB TypeScript file blocked for about 63 seconds); a command path that resolves outside the workspace through a symlink or `..` runs (the command comes from trusted configuration; low exposure); `typecheck_clean` reports a benign line shift in a diagnostic as new.\n- **`typecheck_clean` recognises only coded diagnostics** (`error TS1234:` or `error[E0123]:`). Checkers that print other formats fail closed whenever the baseline already has errors, and identical recognised configuration errors on both sides (for example TS5057) still pass.\n- **Build configuration edits are ignored.** Because the baseline configuration is pinned, a candidate's edits to `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` and similar files are silently ignored by build and `typecheck_clean`, without a report.\n- **Other.** `node --check` exits 0 for a `.js` file written with ESM syntax even when it contains a syntax error (for example `export const a = ;`); a dangling symlink at an overlaid path fails closed with `EEXIST`, and so does a candidate symlink with a source extension; the pinned workspace is created under the system temporary directory, not the configured workspace root; `spec.candidate.cwd` is silently overridden by the pinned root; `--pretty` compiler output defeats the TypeScript diagnostic pattern (fails closed); legacy text-mode tool calls are not counted by the `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; the evaluator README is partly stale.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\nUnchanged from v1.1.1: Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer, Node.js 22 or newer, and an OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint (local or an explicitly selected provider). The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nOperation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No migration runs, and v1.1.1 can read records written by v1.1.2.\n\n## Qualification\n\nThe [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) states what was run, on which commit, with which result, and what was not run. In short: on the release source head `bd7fb1cf`, `make build` passed, the Rust tests passed, the CLI suite passed 2,371 of 2,377 tests with 5 skipped and one failure that comes from a CI fixture variable missing in the local wrapper (the file passed alone when run with the fixtures), and the terminal process-scope and security gates passed when run separately. The exact-head GitHub checks other than the Entire approval gate passed. Independent review of the WP-1105 and WP-1107 work was not an ACCEPT; its findings are the limitations above. No release package for the final stable version was built or acceptance-tested before the tag; the published archive is built by the release workflow.\n# Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\n\n**Status as of 2026-11-04: v1.1.2 ships with known limitations that the owner accepted explicitly.** The release source head is `bd7fb1cf` on `v1/v112-release` (PR #402). Its sources are the integration branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration` through codex-root's `2dbe565b`, plus current `main`, plus the version bump from `1.1.2-rc.2` to `1.1.2`. The exact-head gate on `bd7fb1cf` is recorded in the [final exact-head gate](#final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf) section. Later commits on that PR change only documentation files (`docs/` and `CHANGELOG.md`).\n\n**What this record does not claim.** Independent reviewers returned REQUEST CHANGES on the WP-1105 evaluator work and on the WP-1107 provider work; the owner waived the listed findings and fixed only one of them. Gate G1.1-4 (at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints) was **not measured** and is **not met**. No release package for the final stable version was built or installed by this record: the `rc.2` archive below was built from an earlier source (`c198a33f`), is unpublished, and does not qualify `v1.1.2`. The published archive is built by the release workflow on the tag.\n\nThe v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. No `v1.1.2-rc.*` tag was ever published; the RC1 and RC2 archives named in this record are superseded local artifacts.\n\n## Independent review record and owner waiver\n\nReviews were done by separate reviewer agents that did not write the code. They are posted on [PR #402](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402).\n\n| Scope | Reviewed range | Verdict | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1107 provider work | `5fde750a` (parent `3eea888a`) | REQUEST CHANGES | A HIGH defect (null optional arguments rejected by the Rust core under vLLM strict mode), the task-class header on failed handshakes, matrix-runner provenance, and weak vLLM identity. Fixed in `b032791e` and `0d506762`, except as listed below. |\n| WP-1107 delta | `7f915894..b032791e` | REQUEST CHANGES | The HIGH null-argument defect, the matrix-runner provenance bypasses and the vLLM identity check were fixed. The task-class header leak was closed; kind loss on an unreadable model list was not. |\n| WP-1107 delta | `b032791e..0d506762` | REQUEST CHANGES (borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS) | The matrix runner is fixed (source commit checked against a clean checkout, archive digest required). Kind retention, null normalisation and the transient `/version` case are only partly fixed. Open items are in the limitations below. |\n| WP-1105 evaluators | `5fde750a` | REQUEST CHANGES | Three MEDIUM findings: `typecheck_clean` could pass without measuring anything, build and typecheck ran the candidate's modified build configuration, and `syntax_ast` failed honest runs that delete or edit non-source files. Addressed in `0d506762`, except as listed below. |\n| WP-1105 evaluators | `0d506762` | REQUEST CHANGES | Vacuous `typecheck_clean` pass fixed; build-config pinning partly fixed; a fail-open overlay allow-list and other items open. |\n| Short final review | `0d506762..c198a33f` | REQUEST CHANGES, one new finding | The `typecheck_clean` diagnostic pattern accepted Node's `Error: Cannot find module` and brought back the vacuous pass. The owner had codex-root fix it in `2dbe565b`. The symlink-overlay fix, the sidecar `workspace_name` restore and the gateway-replacement test were found correct. |\n\nReviews that codex-root commissioned on its own commits are not independent reviews of this release and are not counted here. The fix in `2dbe565b` was reviewed only by codex-root's reviewer. The version bump was not separately reviewed. A reviewer requested changes to an earlier draft of these documents, and a further independent review of the final text requested the corrections now applied.\n\n**Owner waiver (2026-11-04).** The owner decided to ship v1.1.2 with the findings under \"Known limitations\" open, and to fix only the `typecheck_clean` pattern. The limitations are repeated in the [release notes](v1.1.2.md).\n\n## Known limitations (owner waiver)\n\nSee [v1.1.2.md](v1.1.2.md#known-limitations-owner-waiver) for the full list. In short: the 99.5% constrained-decoding target was never measured against live providers; the server-kind cache has no expiry and can send `X-Task-Class` to a replaced non-gateway server; null normalisation misses repaired and text-mode tool calls; the code evaluators overlay only some file types onto the baseline workspace (so edits to other files are invisible to build and typecheck), can be shadowed through `node_modules` and build helpers, refuse very large workspaces, and have no resource limits. The evaluators are not used by any dataset task yet.\n\n\n## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\n\nThe approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\n\n| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions connected; PR #396 review fixes present. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating connected. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | The roadmap records this item as cut. | Cut on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | The roadmap records this item as cut; recovery behavior is supplied by PR #398. | Cut on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | The roadmap says this is not yet connected to request latency. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | The roadmap says the comparative harness entry point is not yet connected. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 7 — CERI | The roadmap says the `nexus eval` entry point is not yet connected. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n\n## Work-package status\n\n| Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence details |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Lifecycle instrumentation integrated in commit `97945557`, extending the existing local recorder. Public worktree-backed turns emit exactly one turn span; all four direct model request sites, tool dispatch, and compaction paths are traced with payload-free attributes. | **SOURCE PASSED** | The exact c198a33f suite passed 2,369 tests, 0 failed, 5 skipped; log SHA-256 `69452dedecae7e6396c91d8a397a301d80393b610849cffdc83f1b5a7eba7b45`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. Installed trace capture on the final stable artifact remains pending. |\n| WP-1102 — Flight recorder credential redaction | Zero-leak sanitization across traces, CLI errors, and debug journals. | Integrated in commit `9c1926e1`. Comprehensive regex + token redactor applied across all flight recorder sinks. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/*_redaction.test.ts` (22/22 passed across all sinks and adversarial fixtures). |\n| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | The c198a33f archive acceptance fixture invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and checked that hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. An uncontended rerun produced the same evidence digest. | **PACKAGE BOUNDARY PASS** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Candidate evidence: [`acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `ddaa6915da0808b8a95ac115c54a076411351c45229af7538ffc0236e59dad7c`. It records six requests, no missing/skipped tasks, four regression checks passing and two failing. Hidden validators are false by design; this fixture measures execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving quality or provider quality. The final stable archive must receive its own acceptance run. |\n| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | The c198a33f archive was installed through the production installer and its package-runtime acceptance passed 5/5 in an uncontended rerun. | **PACKAGE RUNTIME PASS — c198a33f RC2** | `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` log SHA-256 `045f31fa6c0d85f132c37d49134f62e03c61ad839fdaab52c1da2b42ffba94d1`; the test used isolated HOME and the exact archive. Repeat against the final stable archive. |\n| WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`; codex-root fixed review findings through `2dbe565b` (symlink overlay, Rust diagnostics, coded-diagnostic pattern). | **SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED** | `code_evaluators.test.ts` passes on the final head (see the final gate). Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#code-evaluators-wp-1105): fail-open overlay for non-listed file types, shadowing through `node_modules` and build helpers, snapshot limits, no resource limits. The evaluators are not used by any dataset task yet. |\n| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. Commits through `0d506762` connect strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**; llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint), and the hybrid reasoning grammars in the roadmap are not implemented. The owner-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **REDUCED SCOPE DELIVERED; SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX NOT MEASURED** | Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#provider-handling-wp-1107): no expiry for the server-kind cache, `X-Task-Class` can reach a replaced non-gateway server, null normalisation gaps, request counting can turn off, matrix provenance not bound to checkout content. G1.1-4 was not measured. |\n| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n\n## Release-gate status\n\n| Gate | Required proof | Current evidence | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction and path-safety tests are part of the suites that passed on the release source head. | **SOURCE TESTS PASS; installed trace capture on a final artifact not collected** |\n| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | c198a33f archive evidence records six requests and no hidden validator path or command in captured prompts; package-runtime acceptance passed in the uncontended rerun. | **PACKAGE BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\n| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | c198a33f package-runtime suite passed 5/5, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS ON RC2; stable artifact pending** |\n| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Strict function schemas are connected on the vLLM request path only and tested locally against mock servers. The shared `GATEWAY` claim was held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric was collected. | **NOT MET — NOT MEASURED** |\n| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | On `bd7fb1cf`: `make build` and the Rust and CLI suites passed as recorded above (one fixture-variable failure rerun alone), the security lifecycle gates passed, and the CodeQL check passed (the alert count was not queried). For the earlier `c198a33f` source, two independent package builds were byte-identical, a 141-component CycloneDX SBOM validated, the installer test passed and the package-runtime suite passed 5/5. | **SOURCE AND SECURITY GATES PASS ON THE RELEASE HEAD; PACKAGE EVIDENCE IS FOR EARLIER SOURCE; RELEASE-LEVEL PTY EVIDENCE NOT COLLECTED** |\n\n## Final exact-head gate (bd7fb1cf)\n\nSource head `bd7fb1cf1b3b6a2a991cb88bcab8fd295fb4ec67` (`v1/v112-release`, PR #402). It was gated once, in a fresh detached worktree with its own `npm ci`, the evaluator scanner helper at mode 0644, the Rust toolchain on `PATH`, an isolated home and no other test or build process on the host. The run started 2026-11-04 17:02 UTC.\n\n| Step | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `make build` (release core and CLI) | exit 0; the release terminal binary and `cli/dist` artifacts were present | log SHA-256 `56e0285af45ade7f3af0a403a69ea79278e1b99eeafdf501de2fc4048282e847` |\n| `make test`: `cargo test` | passed: 43 + 254 + 1 + 4 + 1 tests, 0 failed | in the log below |\n| `make test`: `npm test` (CLI suite) | 2,377 tests, 237 suites: **2,371 passed, 1 failed, 5 skipped** | log SHA-256 `8d3adba582258b176c5d68a4d8159b81de489a4ff3ea83dcc97dd7b0f499b448` |\n| `make test` as a whole | **make exit 2** (the failing recipe exited 1): `make` stopped at the failing `npm test`, so the terminal process-scope step and the security gates did not run inside it | |\n| The one failure | `eval_version_probe_storage`: \"the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem\". It needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT`, which CI sets and the gate wrapper did not. | |\n| Rerun of that file alone, with the fixtures (`/mnt/nexus-eval-ci`, `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`) | 1 of 1 passed | log SHA-256 `42f15fb17372d996adfbf4623a039068e8f50d4613220eb59c00dd8b410219f8` |\n| `scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh` (run separately) | exit 0: scope measurement fixtures passed | log SHA-256 `021c66fd6984b5a774f914446677cc4523e01fe46cb09838a9a5472de93912f2` |\n| `scripts/security_gates.sh` (run separately) | exit 0: all security lifecycle gates passed | log SHA-256 `a9ebd74bcb62e98376fa5a1779172f815a0a80ec23af0b26b3c72e8732391180` |\n\nThe five skipped tests were: three package acceptance tests that need `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE`, `NEXUS_PACKAGE_INSTALL_ROOT`, `NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_EVIDENCE_PATH` or `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT`; `checkpoint gc disables configured hooks added immediately before ref deletion` (needs Git 2.55 or later); and `shell =1 still requires provenance when config.env says =0` (a trusted `gh` is installed on the host).\n\nSo there was no single clean `make test` run on this head: the local run failed on a fixture variable, and the missing steps and the failing file were run separately. A rerun of the whole suite with the fixtures set was not done.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:3:**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.2, which ships **with known limitations** that the owner accepted explicitly. They are listed in full below, and the [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) carries the evidence and the open items. The tag is created after the release pull request merges; these notes describe the source that is tagged.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:46:- **The server-kind cache has no expiry or invalidation.** A readable model-list refresh overwrites the cached kind. When a refresh is unavailable (503, bad JSON, dropped connection, 404 or the model not listed), the previous kind is retained, including its strict flag. If the server on that endpoint is replaced and then answers that way, the stale kind stays (the cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint, so a fresh client for the same endpoint inherits it), and a retained gateway kind sends the `X-Task-Class` header to the non-gateway server that replaced it on the same endpoint. The rule that standalone local servers do not receive `X-Task-Class` (REQ-PRV-109) therefore holds on the success path and for non-gateway kinds, not in that replacement case.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:49:- **Matrix provenance is not bound to the checkout content.** The provider-matrix runner verifies the installed archive digest and that a clean checkout is at the claimed commit, but it does not prove the archive was built from that checkout: any clean repository at the claimed commit passes. A matrix result is evidence about the archive only if the archive digest is pinned by the person reading it.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2.md:72:The [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) states what was run, on which commit, with which result, and what was not run. In short: on the release source head `bd7fb1cf`, `make build` passed, the Rust tests passed, the CLI suite passed 2,371 of 2,377 tests with 5 skipped and one failure that comes from a CI fixture variable missing in the local wrapper (the file passed alone when run with the fixtures), and the terminal process-scope and security gates passed when run separately. The exact-head GitHub checks other than the Entire approval gate passed. Independent review of the WP-1105 and WP-1107 work was not an ACCEPT; its findings are the limitations above. No release package for the final stable version was built or acceptance-tested before the tag; the published archive is built by the release workflow.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3:**Status as of 2026-11-04: v1.1.2 ships with known limitations that the owner accepted explicitly.** The release source head is `bd7fb1cf` on `v1/v112-release` (PR #402). Its sources are the integration branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration` through codex-root's `2dbe565b`, plus current `main`, plus the version bump from `1.1.2-rc.2` to `1.1.2`. The exact-head gate on `bd7fb1cf` is recorded in the [final exact-head gate](#final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf) section. Later commits on that PR change only documentation files (`docs/` and `CHANGELOG.md`).\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:5:**What this record does not claim.** Independent reviewers returned REQUEST CHANGES on the WP-1105 evaluator work and on the WP-1107 provider work; the owner waived the listed findings and fixed only one of them. Gate G1.1-4 (at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints) was **not measured** and is **not met**. No release package for the final stable version was built or installed by this record: the `rc.2` archive below was built from an earlier source (`c198a33f`), is unpublished, and does not qualify `v1.1.2`. The published archive is built by the release workflow on the tag.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:17:| WP-1107 delta | `b032791e..0d506762` | REQUEST CHANGES (borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS) | The matrix runner is fixed (source commit checked against a clean checkout, archive digest required). Kind retention, null normalisation and the transient `/version` case are only partly fixed. Open items are in the limitations below. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:28:See [v1.1.2.md](v1.1.2.md#known-limitations-owner-waiver) for the full list. In short: the 99.5% constrained-decoding target was never measured against live providers; the server-kind cache has no expiry and can send `X-Task-Class` to a replaced non-gateway server; null normalisation misses repaired and text-mode tool calls; the code evaluators overlay only some file types onto the baseline workspace (so edits to other files are invisible to build and typecheck), can be shadowed through `node_modules` and build helpers, refuse very large workspaces, and have no resource limits. The evaluators are not used by any dataset task yet.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:49:| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Lifecycle instrumentation integrated in commit `97945557`, extending the existing local recorder. Public worktree-backed turns emit exactly one turn span; all four direct model request sites, tool dispatch, and compaction paths are traced with payload-free attributes. | **SOURCE PASSED** | The exact c198a33f suite passed 2,369 tests, 0 failed, 5 skipped; log SHA-256 `69452dedecae7e6396c91d8a397a301d80393b610849cffdc83f1b5a7eba7b45`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. Installed trace capture on the final stable artifact remains pending. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:51:| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | The c198a33f archive acceptance fixture invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and checked that hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. An uncontended rerun produced the same evidence digest. | **PACKAGE BOUNDARY PASS** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Candidate evidence: [`acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `ddaa6915da0808b8a95ac115c54a076411351c45229af7538ffc0236e59dad7c`. It records six requests, no missing/skipped tasks, four regression checks passing and two failing. Hidden validators are false by design; this fixture measures execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving quality or provider quality. The final stable archive must receive its own acceptance run. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:52:| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | The c198a33f archive was installed through the production installer and its package-runtime acceptance passed 5/5 in an uncontended rerun. | **PACKAGE RUNTIME PASS — c198a33f RC2** | `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` log SHA-256 `045f31fa6c0d85f132c37d49134f62e03c61ad839fdaab52c1da2b42ffba94d1`; the test used isolated HOME and the exact archive. Repeat against the final stable archive. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:55:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. Commits through `0d506762` connect strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**; llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint), and the hybrid reasoning grammars in the roadmap are not implemented. The owner-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **REDUCED SCOPE DELIVERED; SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX NOT MEASURED** | Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#provider-handling-wp-1107): no expiry for the server-kind cache, `X-Task-Class` can reach a replaced non-gateway server, null normalisation gaps, request counting can turn off, matrix provenance not bound to checkout content. G1.1-4 was not measured. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:64:| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | c198a33f package-runtime suite passed 5/5, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS ON RC2; stable artifact pending** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:66:| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | On `bd7fb1cf`: `make build` and the Rust and CLI suites passed as recorded above (one fixture-variable failure rerun alone), the security lifecycle gates passed, and the CodeQL check passed (the alert count was not queried). For the earlier `c198a33f` source, two independent package builds were byte-identical, a 141-component CycloneDX SBOM validated, the installer test passed and the package-runtime suite passed 5/5. | **SOURCE AND SECURITY GATES PASS ON THE RELEASE HEAD; PACKAGE EVIDENCE IS FOR EARLIER SOURCE; RELEASE-LEVEL PTY EVIDENCE NOT COLLECTED** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:68:## Final exact-head gate (bd7fb1cf)\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:70:Source head `bd7fb1cf1b3b6a2a991cb88bcab8fd295fb4ec67` (`v1/v112-release`, PR #402). It was gated once, in a fresh detached worktree with its own `npm ci`, the evaluator scanner helper at mode 0644, the Rust toolchain on `PATH`, an isolated home and no other test or build process on the host. The run started 2026-11-04 17:02 UTC.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:78:| The one failure | `eval_version_probe_storage`: \"the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem\". It needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT`, which CI sets and the gate wrapper did not. | |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:87:**GitHub checks on `bd7fb1cf`.** `CodeQL`, `javascript-typescript`, `cloudflare-experiment (22)` and `(24)`, `test-matrix (22)` and `(24)` and `linux-x86_64` passed; `CodeRabbit` reported its review as skipped. `Entire Gates` waited for owner approval. The release workflow additionally runs the evaluator toolchain, the capped-tmpfs fixtures and the packaging steps on the tag.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:89:**Docs-only follow-up commits.** Commits after `bd7fb1cf` on PR #402 change only documentation files (`docs/` and `CHANGELOG.md`); `git diff --stat bd7fb1cf <head> -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'` is empty for the merged head.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:91:**Not done in this record.** No release package for the final stable version was built here, installed, or acceptance-tested (the package rows below are for earlier source). The supported-provider matrix (G1.1-4) was not run. Release-level PTY evidence and installed trace capture on the final artifact were not collected.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:125:  - **Installer:** local HTTP-feed installation passed archive checksum, package manifest, binary self-test, and compatibility checks. The installed launcher and TUI report `1.1.2-rc.2`; `.provenance.json` binds the installed tree to this archive digest. GitHub attestation verification was disabled because this local candidate is unpublished.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:143:- **Installed-candidate evidence:** [`acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json), SHA-256 `d6244199b00dc1ef722f08e8cdeb585f35a9215f869a1125b8e5e06b3ba98f0d`. The uncontended rerun regenerated byte-identical evidence: six requests, one per public benchmark task, no hidden validator path or command in prompts. Four regression checks passed and two failed; hidden validators are false by design, so this is execution and prompt-boundary evidence, not task-solving quality. This RC2 evidence does not qualify the final stable archive.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:145:## Release checklist\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:147:- [x] WP-1101 to WP-1108 source changes, including the WP-1107 and WP-1105 review remediations, are present through codex-root's `2dbe565b`, merged with current `main` and version-bumped to `1.1.2` (`bd7fb1cf`).\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:148:- [x] Release source head `bd7fb1cf`: build, Rust tests, CLI suite (one fixture-variable failure, rerun alone and passed), terminal process-scope fixtures and security gates, as recorded in the final exact-head gate section.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:149:- [x] Exact-head GitHub checks other than the Entire approval gate passed on `bd7fb1cf`.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:152:- [ ] Not done: a package for the final stable version was not built, installed or acceptance-tested before the tag; the release workflow builds the published archive.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":913623595}},"started_at_ms":1793824049690,"completed_at_ms":1793824050605}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:27:31.890Z","ordinal":112754,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a83e-d2b2-7570-bc4a-b9e98c8d04c1","call_id":"call_904d04bdb1634d57b176387763be8d1b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"entire\":\"{\\\"completed_at\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T19:22:30Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"failure\\\",\\\"details_url\\\":\\\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/145/changes/nexus-code/140\\\",\\\"output\\\":{\\\"annotations_count\\\":0,\\\"annotations_url\\\":\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/check-runs/126777524056/annotations\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"- ❌ **Approvals**: failed — No reviewers have approved this trail\\\\n- ✅ **Checks**: passed — CI checks have passed\\\\n- ❌ **Findings**: failed — Unresolved findings: 1 high severity\\\\n- ✅ **Up to date**: passed — Up to date\\\\n\\\\n[Trail #140 on Entire](https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/145/changes/nexus-code/140)\\\",\\\"text\\\":null,\\\"title\\\":\\\"2 blocking gates not passing\\\"},\\\"started_at\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T18:31:29Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}\\n\",\"docs\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10419)\\nTotal output lines: 189\\n\\n## v1/v112-release...origin/v1/v112-release [ahead 1]\\nc5ceb2e5 (HEAD -> v1/v112-release) test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\\nfafbf6d5 (origin/v1/v112-release) docs(release): correct WP-1107 scope and the review record\\n40d553b5 docs(release): v1.1.2 release notes and qualification record\\nbd7fb1cf chore(release): bump to 1.1.2\\n# Nexus Code v1.1.2\\n\\n**Maturity:** Release notes for Nexus Code v1.1.2, which ships **with known limitations** that the owner accepted explicitly. They are listed in full below, and the [qualification record](v1.1.2-qualification.md) carries the evidence and the open items. The tag is created after the release pull request merges; these notes describe the source that is tagged.\\n\\nv1.1.2 delivers the WP-1101 to WP-1108 roadmap that was originally planned for v1.1.0, with WP-1107 delivered in reduced form (see below). The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files, and v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. Version numbers are immutable, so the roadmap work is assigned to v1.1.2. No `v1.1.2-rc.*` tag was ever published; the candidates that carried those names are superseded.\\n\\n## What is in this release\\n\\n- **WP-1101, local OpenTelemetry tracing.** GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tool dispatch and compaction, written locally with payload-free attributes. Trace output is confined to the approved trace directory.\\n- **WP-1102, flight-recorder credential redaction.** Credential redaction across traces, CLI errors and debug journals.\\n- **WP-1103, versioned evaluation datasets.** Datasets with separate examples and oracles and regression and benchmark splits; candidate prompts do not carry oracle paths or commands.\\n- **WP-1104, standalone `nexus eval`.** A packaged command with dataset selection, run count, an isolated home and structured score output. It runs outside the repository checkout.\\n- **WP-1105, deterministic code evaluators.** AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary and JSON-repair evaluators and tool-call syntax telemetry (`toolCallSyntax`). **The evaluators are a library: no dataset task uses them yet.** See the limitations below.\\n- **WP-1106, single-step loop mode.** `--step`, and `/step` in the REPL and the TUI, pause after one agent turn for operator confirmation.\\n- **WP-1107, bounded tool schemas (reduced scope).** A bounded schema compiler for the four harness tools, and strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**. llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas: no grammar or format constraint is sent for them, and the hybrid reasoning grammars from the roadmap are not implemented. The 99.5% valid-tool-call target was **not measured** against live providers; see below.\\n- **WP-1108, dependency modernisation.** The pending Dependabot updates were triaged and merged. `cargo deny` is clean, there are no deprecated npm packages, and a CycloneDX SBOM is generated.\\n- **Non-progress recovery.** A bounded recovery state machine for repeated unproductive tool calls, with state-based same-step progress and unique tool-call ids ([#398](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398)).\\n- **Specialist orchestration and independent review.** Specialist roles with tool allow-lists, an evidence-based review boundary for operation units, and redaction of credential-named keys in review evidence ([#396](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/396), [#401](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/401)).\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\\n\\nWhen a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\\n\\nResume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\\n\\n- Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\\n- Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` carries two messages and asserts that each appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\\n\\n### Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\\n\\nThe v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \\\"at most once\\\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\\n\\n## Known limitations (owner waiver)\\n\\nIndependent reviewers examined the release source and returned REQUEST CHANGES on the WP-1105 evaluator work and on the WP-1107 provider work. The owner decided to ship v1.1.2 with the findings below open, and to fix only one of them (the `typecheck_clean` diagnostic pattern, commit `2dbe565b`). Nothing in this list has been fixed in this release. The review reports are on [PR #402](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402).\\n\\n### Not measured\\n\\n- **Constrained decoding, gate G1.1-4: NOT MET, NOT MEASURED.** The target is at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. Strict function schemas are connected on the vLLM request path and tested locally with mock servers; llama.cpp and Ollama requests do not use them. No measurement against live llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama endpoints was made, because the shared gateway resource was held by another release stream. Do not read this release as having met that target.\\n- **Task quality.** The benchmark fixture checks execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving or provider quality.\\n\\n### Provider handling (WP-1107)\\n\\n- **The server-kind cache has no expiry or invalidation.** A readable model-list refresh overwrites the cached kind. When a refresh is unavailable (503, bad JSON, dropped connection, 404 or the model not listed), the previous kind is retained, including its strict flag. If the server on that endpoint is replaced and then answers that way, the stale kind stays (the cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint, so a fresh client for the same endpoint inherits it), and a retained gateway kind sends the `X-Task-Class` header to the non-gateway server that replaced it on the same endpoint. The rule that standalone local servers do not receive `X-Task-Class` (REQ-PRV-109) therefore holds on the success path and for non-gateway kinds, not in that replacement case.\\n- **Null normalisation covers well-formed native tool calls only.** Calls that needed JSON repair, and text-mode tool calls, still reach read tracking with `null` optional fields. The normaliser also strips an explicit `null` from every optional property of every tool for all providers, including properties whose schema allows null (measured on a synthetic tool; real MCP tools were not checked).\\n- **Request counting can turn off.** After a transient `/version` failure, or a 404 or missing-model refresh, a retained vLLM kind no longer matches the advertised source, so the agent probably reports that request counting is unavailable.\\n- **Matrix provenance is not bound to the checkout content.** The provider-matrix runner verifies the installed archive digest and that a clean checkout is at the claimed commit, but it does not prove the archive was built from that checkout: any clean repository at the claimed commit passes. A matrix result is evidence about the archive only if the archive digest is pinned by the person reading it.\\n- **Ollama identity.** A transient `/api/version` failure on a successful refresh still drops the kind to un…6419 tokens truncated…es. | **SOURCE PASSED** | The exact c198a33f suite passed 2,369 tests, 0 failed, 5 skipped; log SHA-256 `69452dedecae7e6396c91d8a397a301d80393b610849cffdc83f1b5a7eba7b45`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. Installed trace capture on the final stable artifact remains pending. |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:51:| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | The c198a33f archive acceptance fixture invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and checked that hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. An uncontended rerun produced the same evidence digest. | **PACKAGE BOUNDARY PASS** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Candidate evidence: [`acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `ddaa6915da0808b8a95ac115c54a076411351c45229af7538ffc0236e59dad7c`. It records six requests, no missing/skipped tasks, four regression checks passing and two failing. Hidden validators are false by design; this fixture measures execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving quality or provider quality. The final stable archive must receive its own acceptance run. |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:52:| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | The c198a33f archive was installed through the production installer and its package-runtime acceptance passed 5/5 in an uncontended rerun. | **PACKAGE RUNTIME PASS — c198a33f RC2** | `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` log SHA-256 `045f31fa6c0d85f132c37d49134f62e03c61ad839fdaab52c1da2b42ffba94d1`; the test used isolated HOME and the exact archive. Repeat against the final stable archive. |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:55:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. Commits through `0d506762` connect strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**; llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint), and the hybrid reasoning grammars in the roadmap are not implemented. The owner-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **REDUCED SCOPE DELIVERED; SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX NOT MEASURED** | Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#provider-handling-wp-1107): no expiry for the server-kind cache, `X-Task-Class` can reach a replaced non-gateway server, null normalisation gaps, request counting can turn off, matrix provenance not bound to checkout content. G1.1-4 was not measured. |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:64:| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | c198a33f package-runtime suite passed 5/5, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS ON RC2; stable artifact pending** |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:66:| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | On `bd7fb1cf`: `make build` and the Rust and CLI suites passed as recorded above (one fixture-variable failure rerun alone), the security lifecycle gates passed, and the CodeQL check passed (the alert count was not queried). For the earlier `c198a33f` source, two independent package builds were byte-identical, a 141-component CycloneDX SBOM validated, the installer test passed and the package-runtime suite passed 5/5. | **SOURCE AND SECURITY GATES PASS ON THE RELEASE HEAD; PACKAGE EVIDENCE IS FOR EARLIER SOURCE; RELEASE-LEVEL PTY EVIDENCE NOT COLLECTED** |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:68:## Final exact-head gate (bd7fb1cf)\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:70:Source head `bd7fb1cf1b3b6a2a991cb88bcab8fd295fb4ec67` (`v1/v112-release`, PR #402). It was gated once, in a fresh detached worktree with its own `npm ci`, the evaluator scanner helper at mode 0644, the Rust toolchain on `PATH`, an isolated home and no other test or build process on the host. The run started 2026-11-04 17:02 UTC.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:78:| The one failure | `eval_version_probe_storage`: \\\"the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem\\\". It needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT`, which CI sets and the gate wrapper did not. | |\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:87:**GitHub checks on `bd7fb1cf`.** `CodeQL`, `javascript-typescript`, `cloudflare-experiment (22)` and `(24)`, `test-matrix (22)` and `(24)` and `linux-x86_64` passed; `CodeRabbit` reported its review as skipped. `Entire Gates` waited for owner approval. The release workflow additionally runs the evaluator toolchain, the capped-tmpfs fixtures and the packaging steps on the tag.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:89:**Docs-only follow-up commits.** Commits after `bd7fb1cf` on PR #402 change only documentation files (`docs/` and `CHANGELOG.md`); `git diff --stat bd7fb1cf <head> -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'` is empty for the merged head.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:91:**Not done in this record.** No release package for the final stable version was built here, installed, or acceptance-tested (the package rows below are for earlier source). The supported-provider matrix (G1.1-4) was not run. Release-level PTY evidence and installed trace capture on the final artifact were not collected.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:125:  - **Installer:** local HTTP-feed installation passed archive checksum, package manifest, binary self-test, and compatibility checks. The installed launcher and TUI report `1.1.2-rc.2`; `.provenance.json` binds the installed tree to this archive digest. GitHub attestation verification was disabled because this local candidate is unpublished.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:143:- **Installed-candidate evidence:** [`acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-ddaa6915da08-installed.json), SHA-256 `d6244199b00dc1ef722f08e8cdeb585f35a9215f869a1125b8e5e06b3ba98f0d`. The uncontended rerun regenerated byte-identical evidence: six requests, one per public benchmark task, no hidden validator path or command in prompts. Four regression checks passed and two failed; hidden validators are false by design, so this is execution and prompt-boundary evidence, not task-solving quality. This RC2 evidence does not qualify the final stable archive.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:145:## Release checklist\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:147:- [x] WP-1101 to WP-1108 source changes, including the WP-1107 and WP-1105 review remediations, are present through codex-root's `2dbe565b`, merged with current `main` and version-bumped to `1.1.2` (`bd7fb1cf`).\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:148:- [x] Release source head `bd7fb1cf`: build, Rust tests, CLI suite (one fixture-variable failure, rerun alone and passed), terminal process-scope fixtures and security gates, as recorded in the final exact-head gate section.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:149:- [x] Exact-head GitHub checks other than the Entire approval gate passed on `bd7fb1cf`.\\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:152:- [ ] Not done: a package for the final stable version was not built, installed or acceptance-tested before the tag; the release workflow builds the published archive.\\n\",\"reviews\":{\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABV0bFMg\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"body\":\"\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security\",\"name\":\"github-advanced-security\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4\",\"id\":null}}]},\"claims\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1030)\\nTotal output lines: 11\\n\\n2026-11-04T17:02:30Z CLAIM SUITE claude-code: v1.1.2 final exact-head gate on bd7fb1cf (worktree ~/nexus-wt/rg-final; v1/v112-release = c198a33f + 2dbe565b + main + version bump 1.1.2): make build, make test (cargo test + npm test + security_gates), terminal process-scope. Logs /tmp/rg-final-*.log. Please no test or build processes on this host meanwhile (a contended run is worthless).\\n2026-11-04 18:02:03 UTC SUITE RESULT claude-code bd7fb1cf exact make test exited 1: 2377 tests, 2371 pass, 1 fail, 5 skipped; sole failure test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts because NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT are unset in local wrapper. Both vars are configured in CI workflow; exact-head GitHub linux-x86_64 and test-matrix jobs succeeded. Log SHA-256 8d3adba582258b176c5d68a4d8159b81de489a4ff3ea83dcc97dd7b0f499b448. Suite processes have exited; do not release claude-code claim or rerun without owner direction.\\n2026-11-04 18:16:20 UTC INDEPENDENT_REVIEW review_delta exact bd7fb1cf + uncommitted release docs: CHANGES_REQUESTED. Required: remove shipped/stable assertions; fix/remove missing #final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf anchor; report local make test accurately (2371 pass, 1 fixture-env failure, 5 skipped) and distinguish green exact-head GitHub jobs from pending Entire; refresh qualification checklist/status; narrow server-kind cache wording (readable discovery overwrites, stale kind retained on unavailable/404/not-listed paths); clarify archive digest is not proven reproducibly bound to verified checkout. Other listed limitations directionally accurat…230 tokens truncated…cord; git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' empty; security_gates.sh passed on this head). SUITE released.\\n2026-11-04T18:31:24Z PUSH claude-code: PR402 head fafbf6d5: docs-only corrections after the independent docs review (WP-1107 scope stated as vLLM-only strict schemas, CHANGELOG.md, review table, limitations). security_gates passed; SUITE released.\\n2026-11-04T18:31:44Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW claude-code (reviewer agent, not the author)