ty; security_gates.sh passed on this head). SUITE released.\n2026-11-04T18:31:24Z PUSH claude-code: PR402 head fafbf6d5: docs-only corrections after the independent docs review (WP-1107 scope stated as vLLM-only strict schemas, CHANGELOG.md, review table, limitations). security_gates passed; SUITE released.\n2026-11-04T18:31:44Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW claude-code (reviewer agent, not the author): release docs + version bump bd7fb1cf..40d553b5 = REQUEST CHANGES, all corrections applied in fafbf6d5 (docs only): HIGH WP-1107 delivered in reduced scope (strict schemas on the vLLM path only; llama.cpp/Ollama keep native schemas; no grammar/format constraint; hybrid grammars not implemented); CHANGELOG.md; limitations wording; review table; G1.1-5 wording. Numbers/hashes/version bump verified correct. Full text on PR402.\n2026-11-04T20:27:10Z CLAIM claude-code: FILE_cli_src_agent.ts FILE_cli_test_step_loop.test.ts on v1/v112-release for the owner-approved fix of Entire trail 145 HIGH finding (01M6KXTK2G0S): in --step mode the parallel read_file branch in agent.ts runs endStep();continue and bypasses the STEP_PAUSED check. Plan: regression test RED first, minimal fix, focused tests, then ONE new exact-head gate. Owner decision 2026-11-04 ~19:00 UTC: 'Fix the HIGH, rerun the gate'.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":934916653}},"started_at_ms":1793824071322,"completed_at_ms":1793824072258}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:27:53.688Z","ordinal":112763,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a83f-27d8-7570-8d88-6d4fb660c6ff","call_id":"call_1df374383ec240faa3bd3cbbe3ead453","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 6.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4803)\nTotal output lines: 101\n\n## v1/v112-release...origin/v1/v112-release [ahead 1]\nc5ceb2e5 (HEAD -> v1/v112-release) test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\nfafbf6d5 (origin/v1/v112-release) docs(release): correct WP-1107 scope and the review record\n40d553b5 docs(release): v1.1.2 release notes and qualification record\nc5ceb2e5 test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\n cli/test/step_loop.test.ts | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)\ncommit c5ceb2e5609e4a1ac9fa5bb187933f9dfa753750\nAuthor:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nAuthorDate: Wed Nov 4 20:27:22 2026 +0000\nCommit:     Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\nCommitDate: Wed Nov 4 20:27:22 2026 +0000\n\n    test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\n    \n    RED: the parallel-read branch ends the step with endStep();continue and skips\n    the STEP_PAUSED check, so a second provider request and the later edit run.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M6M3XBSEVBKJ1CTFJC4NA3RB\n\ndiff --git a/cli/test/step_loop.test.ts b/cli/test/step_loop.test.ts\nindex 8d4a4d6c..10fe0051 100644\n--- a/cli/test/step_loop.test.ts\n+++ b/cli/test/step_loop.test.ts\n@@ -80,6 +80,44 @@ describe(\"WP-1106: Single-step agent loop mode\", () => {\n     }\n   });\n \n+  test(\"AC1b: --step pauses after a cycle whose tool calls are parallel reads\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n+    const home = makeHome();\n+    const repo = makeRepo({ \"a.txt\": \"alpha\\n\", \"b.txt\": \"beta\\n\" });\n+    trustWorkspace(home, repo);\n+    const prevHome = process.env.HOME;\n+    process.env.HOME = home;\n+\n+    const gw = await startGateway((n) => {\n+      if (n === 1) {\n+        return {\n+          kind: \"tools\",\n+          calls: [\n+            { name: \"read_file\", args: { path: \"a.txt\" } },\n+            { name: \"read_file\", args: { path: \"b.txt\" } },\n+          ],\n+        };\n+      }\n+      return write(\"after-reads.txt\", \"must not exist\\n\");\n+    });\n+\n+    const app = new ApplicationCore(cfg(gw.url, repo));\n+    try {\n+      const result = await app.runTask(\"Read both files, then write a file\", { step: true });\n+\n+      assert.equal(gw.requests.length, 1, \"a parallel-read cycle must still end the step: only 1 provider request\");\n+      assert.ok(!fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, \"after-reads.txt\")), \"the edit after the reads must not run in the same --step\");\n+      assert.equal(result.turn.reason, \"STEP_PAUSED\");\n+      assert.equal(result.turn.stepPaused, true);\n+      assert.equal(result.turn.steps.used, 1);\n+    } finally {\n+      app.shutdown();\n+      await gw.close();\n+      process.env.HOME = prevHome;\n+      fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+      fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+    }\n+  });\n+\n   test(\"AC2: /step advances the current objective by exactly one cycle\", { timeout: 60_000 }, async () => {\n     const home = makeHome();\n     const repo = makeRepo();\n 190803  1-15:00:51 Sl   node -e const f=require('fs'),p=require('path'),o=require('os');const h=o.homedir();const C=process.env.CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR||p.join(h,'.claude');const E=process.env.CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT||process.env.PLUGIN_ROOT||'';const d=process.cwd();const S=n=>{const q=n.split('-')[0].split('.');return[parseInt(q[0],10)||0,parseInt(q[1],10)||0,parseInt(q[2],10)||0]};const W=(a,b)=>{const x=S(a),y=S(b);return(y[0]-x[0])||(y[1]-x[1])||(y[2]-x