{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:28:07.570Z","ordinal":112770,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aeb9549f04081a3a63cbf8184146c8a","usage":{"input_tokens":217724,"cached_input_tokens":212096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":693,"reasoning_output_tokens":676,"total_tokens":218417},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":839077,"cached_input_tokens":632576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3141,"reasoning_output_tokens":1874,"total_tokens":842218},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2308653224,"cached_input_tokens":2291392256,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4220682,"reasoning_output_tokens":2025291,"total_tokens":2312873906}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:28:08.742Z","ordinal":112771,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a83f-62a6-7623-8d0c-31133aa968b2","call_id":"call_1abd9105319747fe8d72f5a5ddc2ca25","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Relayed review_delta’s `CHANGES_REQUESTED` verdict and all five required documentation corrections to the release coordinator. I made no edits.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for release-document accuracy. The source review items are acknowledged, and the `2dbe565b` diagnostic fix is present at exact PR head `bd7fb1cf`. I did not edit files or run tests/builds.\\n\\n1. **The docs say the release has shipped, but publication is still pending.** The current PR #402 is open at `bd7fb1cf`; GitHub reports no `v1.1.2` release, and the qualification checklist leaves the tag and publication unchecked. Change “v1.1.2 ships” / “Stable release … shipped” in [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3) and [release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:3) to distinguish the owner’s decision to ship with limitations from actual publication.\\n\\n2. **The exact-head gate is referenced but absent, and the release summary overstates the local result.** The qualification record links to `#final-exact-head-gate-bd7fb1cf` at line 3, but contains no corresponding section. The release notes say the exact source head passed the full local suite at line 71; the reported `bd7fb1cf` local run had one failure, `eval_version_probe_storage`, because its CI fixture variables were missing. Record that result and the separate CI result instead of calling the local run fully green. The CI status text at [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:65) is also stale: current checks on `bd7fb1cf` pass for CodeQL and the named CI jobs; Entire Gates remains pending.\\n\\n3. **The cache limitation is overstated.** The release note says the server-kind cache “never expires or invalidates” at [v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:46). At exact head, readable discovery overwrites the cached kind, including with `unknown` ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1208)); stale identity is retained on unavailable, 404, or missing-model paths. Describe the lack of expiry and those retention paths specifically. The resulting stale `X-Task-Class` risk is real.\\n\\n4. **Clarify the matrix-provenance limitation.** The release notes say any clean repository at the claimed commit passes ([v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:49)), while the runner checks Git `HEAD` and cleanliness, then checks installed provenance against the same commit and pinned archive digest ([tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:359), [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:403)). If the remaining limitation is that this does not prove the archive was built reproducibly from that source tree, state that directly; the current wording obscures what is and is not bound.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audit sent to the release owner. The exact 05913af5 source gate is still running; after it passes, the live provider matrix is next, but the GATEWAY claim remains held by the RC15 E5 worktree. The qualification record still points to older commits and needs refresh after candidate-bound evidence is complete.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793824088.7427096}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
