{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:31:33.323Z","ordinal":112872,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a842-81cb-7f20-a193-957d2d801061","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED overall; source fix approved.** I reviewed local HEAD `822c08fb`, the test-first commit `c5ceb2e5`, and release docs at `fafbf6d5`. I did not run tests or builds.\n\nThe regression test is meaningful: `c5ceb2e5` adds it without changing source, and asserts one provider request, no later file write, `STEP_PAUSED`, and one step used. The subsequent six-line source fix in [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:6262) checks the parallel-read path after results are saved and before `endStep(); continue`, matching the sequential path’s pause behavior. It also avoids replacing interruption, inference, or persistence failures. The known pause-overrides-stagnation limitation remains; it is documented in [v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:72).\n\nThe release record needs another update before it describes this exact head. At `fafbf6d5`, [the qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3) identifies `bd7fb1cf` as the source head and says later commits are docs-only. Local HEAD is now `822c08fb`, with the test and source commits after that record. The recorded gate therefore does not qualify the current head. Update the head/gate account after the exact-head run completes; it is currently running separately."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793824293.3230193,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3841}}
