{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:47:12.768Z","ordinal":113177,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a850-d780-7e42-8e55-40ad54b9421f","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...810 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-04 8:47pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (19,974t read) | 132,974t work | 85% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2267 WP-1107 Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments — Scope Conflict Resolution and Implementation Verification (Nov 2, 1:45 PM)\n### Nov 4, 2026\n30866 5:43p ○ eval_version_probe_storage Test Requires CI Environment Variables — Expected to Fail Locally\n30867 5:44p ○ Local Final Gate Script Does Not Set CI tmpfs Env Vars — Confirmed Expected Failure Pattern\n30868 \" ✓ PR #402 Gate Note Posted — eval_version_probe_storage Local Failure Explained\n30869 \" ○ Local Final Gate Stall Resolved — Test Log Resumed, D-State Worker Process Exited\n30870 5:45p ✓ Work State Updated — eval_version_probe_storage Fixture Issue and Gate Progress Recorded\n30871 \" ○ CI Run 1461 — Both test-matrix Jobs Complete, linux-x86_64 Now In Progress at CLI Suite Step\n30872 5:48p ○ CI Run 1461 on bd7fb1cf — All test-matrix and cloudflare Jobs Complete, linux-x86_64 at Package Step\n30873 5:49p ○ Local Final Gate Log Contains Harness \"TURN ENDED - UNVERIFIED\" Marker at 1094 Passes\n30874 5:51p ○ v1.1.2 Release Work State — Full Gate Sequence and Remaining Open Items Confirmed\n30875 5:52p ○ WP-1107 R2 Review at b032791e — Full Finding Details Confirmed from Claims Log\n30876 \" ○ CI linux-x86_64 — First package-linux.sh Build Passed, Now Running Reproducibility Second Build\n30877 \" ○ v1.1.2 Qualification Doc — WP-1107 Live Provider Matrix and WP-1105 Evaluator Gate Status Confirmed\n30878 \" ⚖ Release Strategy — Ship v1.1.2 With Known Limitations, Audit Release Docs Before Publishing\n30879 5:53p ○ CI linux-x86_64 — Reproducibility and All Verification Steps Passed, Now at Installer Smoke Test\n30880 \" ✓ Release Notes and Qualification Doc Updated with Known Limitations — Uncommitted in v112-release Worktree\n30881 5:54p ✓ v1.1.2 Qualification Doc Rewritten — Full Independent Review Record, Known Limitations, and Open Gate Items Documented\n30884 5:55p ○ CI Run 1461 on bd7fb1cf — All Five Jobs Passed, linux-x86_64 Package Build Complete\n30885 5:59p ○ release_gate_audit Agent Sent Doc Corrections to Coordinator\n30886 6:01p ○ Local Final Gate make test Failed — Assertion Error at 1184 Passes\n30887 \" ○ Local Final Gate Complete — 2371 Pass, 1 Fail (eval_version_probe_storage CI-Only)\n30888 \" ○ eval_version_probe_storage CI-Only Failure Confirmed — NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and RUNTIME_ROOT Required\n30889 6:02p ✓ Local Final Gate Result Logged to Claims Log — Awaiting Owner Direction\n30890 6:03p ○ v1.1.2 Release Blockers Identified — PR Body Stale, Docs Need Corrections Before Tag\n30892 6:06p ○ Active Agent Directory — Only \"CloudyGate\" (codex-cli/gpt-6) Active in nexus-code Project\n30893 6:07p ○ WP-1107 R2 Delta Review — Four Findings Status After b032791e\n30894 6:08p ✓ Work State Updated — CI Artifact Digest and Gate Job Status Recorded\n30895 \" ○ Active Agent Status — release_gate_audit, review_delta, and roadmap_next Completed\n30896 \" ○ PR #402 Body Confirmed Stale — Describes 8520d9c8 and RC2, Head Is Now bd7fb1cf\n30897 \" ○ v112-release Worktree State — Two Release Docs Uncommitted, Claims Log Final Gate Result Confirmed\n30898 6:09p ○ PR #402 Check Suite on bd7fb1cf — All Pass Except Entire Gates Still Pending\n30899 \" ○ Entire Gates Detail — Blocked on No Reviewers Approved, Pending Because PR Is Draft\n30900 6:10p ✓ Independent Release Review of bd7fb1cf Requested from review_delta\n30903 \" ○ Claims Registry — SUITE and Doc File Claims Still Held by claude-code\n30922 6:13p ○ eval_version_probe_storage Test — Requires CI-Mounted tmpfs and Separate Evaluator UID, Correctly CI-Only\n30931 6:14p ○ WP-1107 R2 Delta Review — Four Finding Statuses After b032791e\n30932 \" ✓ Independent Review of bd7fb1cf Returned CHANGES_REQUESTED — Blocking Items Recorded in Work State\n30933 6:16p ○ PR #402 Body Confirmed Stale — Describes c198a33f/8520d9c8, Head Is Now bd7fb1cf\n30934 6:17p ◆ New Agent \"AzureMeadow\" (codex-app/gpt-6) Spawned for v1.1.2 Release Gate Follow-Up\n30935 6:18p ✓ Release Goal Status Set to Blocked — Awaiting Doc Corrections and Reviewer Approval\nS2306 v1.1.2 Release Gate Status Briefing — Independent Review CHANGES_REQUESTED, Goal Formally Blocked (Nov 4, 6:18 PM)\n30959 8:27p ○ PR #402 Updated — No Longer Draft, Body Refreshed to Reflect bd7fb1cf Head\n30960 \" ○ PR #402 CI All Green Except Entire Gates (Fail) — Checks on fafbf6d5\n30961 \" ○ Entire Trail 145 HIGH Finding — Step-Mode Bypass Bug in agent.ts Claimed for Fix\n30962 \" ○ Entire Gates Failure Details — Two Blocking Gates: No Approvals + 1 High Finding Unresolved\n30963 \" ○ v112-release Worktree Has Uncommitted Step-Mode Fix Test — One Commit Ahead of Origin\n30964 \" ◆ Step-Mode Parallel Read Fix — RED Regression Test Committed, SUITE Claimed for GREEN + Gate\n30965 8:28p ● Step-Mode Parallel Read Pause Bug Fixed — GREEN Committed, Second Exact-Head Gate Running on 822c08fb\n30975 8:29p ○ Second Exact-Head Gate Running on 822c08fb — 105 CLI Tests Passed, Build Complete, Release Docs Modified\n30976 8:30p ✓ Release Docs Updated with Additional Known Limitations from Entire Review — WP-1106 TUI, Eval CLI, Tracing, Tool Grammar, Redaction\n30979 8:31p ○ review_delta Independent Review of 822c08fb — Source Fix APPROVED, Docs CHANGES_REQUESTED\n30982 8:35p ○ Second Gate — Context Limit Changed to 65536 at Step 2 — New Test Suite Starting\n\nAccess 133k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793825232.7683103,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
