{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:47:47.339Z","ordinal":113209,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a851-5e8b-7dd0-8635-6cbfd6a44add","call_id":"call_1a4b32b51d984f7f94e9d978834586ca","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Relayed review_delta’s `CHANGES_REQUESTED` verdict and all five required documentation corrections to the release coordinator. I made no edits.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUESTED overall; source fix approved.** I reviewed local HEAD `822c08fb`, the test-first commit `c5ceb2e5`, and release docs at `fafbf6d5`. I did not run tests or builds.\\n\\nThe regression test is meaningful: `c5ceb2e5` adds it without changing source, and asserts one provider request, no later file write, `STEP_PAUSED`, and one step used. The subsequent six-line source fix in [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:6262) checks the parallel-read path after results are saved and before `endStep(); continue`, matching the sequential path’s pause behavior. It also avoids replacing interruption, inference, or persistence failures. The known pause-overrides-stagnation limitation remains; it is documented in [v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:72).\\n\\nThe release record needs another update before it describes this exact head. At `fafbf6d5`, [the qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3) identifies `bd7fb1cf` as the source head and says later commits are docs-only. Local HEAD is now `822c08fb`, with the test and source commits after that record. The recorded gate therefore does not qualify the current head. Update the head/gate account after the exact-head run completes; it is currently running separately.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audit sent to the release owner. The exact 05913af5 source gate is still running; after it passes, the live provider matrix is next, but the GATEWAY claim remains held by the RC15 E5 worktree. The qualification record still points to older commits and needs refresh after candidate-bound evidence is complete.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793825267.3392704}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
