{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:52:37.165Z","ordinal":113365,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a855-caad-7d00-9321-8f8bec282c00","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**Disposition: partial fixes; the remaining WP-1107 findings need fresh independent review.** I inspected the changes in `0d506762` and `05913af5` and their current code paths. No tests or builds were run.\n\n- **Provider-kind rediscovery — partially addressed.** `0d506762` retains the previous kind when `/models` is unavailable, returns 404, or omits the selected model; a readable generic result can replace it with `unknown` ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1174), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1208)). That protects previously verified identity during transient failures, but leaves the reported stale-gateway risk when a replacement server responds through those failure paths. No expiry or endpoint-generation check was added. `05913af5` does not change this code.\n\n- **Null normalization and read tracking — partially addressed.** The new helper derives optional fields from tool schemas and is applied to returned native tool calls and again at dispatch ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:43), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1449), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1607), [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:4889)). But tracking still observes the original call arguments ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:5797)), and structurally repaired write/exec calls return before dispatch normalization ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:4866)). The helper also removes explicit `null` from every optional property, even when the schema allows null ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:47)). The finding is not fully closed; `05913af5` does not touch this path.\n\n- **Transient vLLM `/version` failure — partially addressed.** The cache keeps `vllm` after the version probe fails ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1197)). However, only a successful probe sets `advertised.via = \"vllm\"`. Request-count admission checks the advertisement’s `tokenize`/`via` fields ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:2965)), so a retained kind does not by itself preserve request-count capability. The regression test verifies retained identity and strict schema, but not request-count admission ([client_tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts:119)). Still open; `05913af5` does not change it.\n\n- **Matrix source/archive pinning — the self-attestation gap is closed; build provenance remains limited.** `0d506762` requires a clean checkout whose `HEAD` matches `sourceCommit`, requires an archive SHA-256, and checks installed provenance and files against the verified archive ([tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:359), [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:403), [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:427)). Its tests cover mismatched self-attested commits, dirty checkouts, and missing archive pins ([tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs:201)). The runner still does not establish that the archive was reproducibly built from that checkout. `05913af5` does not change matrix code.\n\n`05913af5` adds evaluator and provider tests, but makes no WP-1107 changes in `client.ts`, `agent.ts`, or the matrix runner. The provider-kind retention, observation normalization, and vLLM request-count behavior therefore remain candidates for fresh independent review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793825557.1650379,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3880}}
