{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:58:03.291Z","ordinal":113531,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeb9c582e3481a3be90cf5fb41f8114","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The review reconciliation narrows the remaining work. The checked-in follow-ups already address the initial rediscovery retention and matrix forgery reports, but three provider gaps remain: tracking can still see unnormalized arguments on some paths, nullable schema fields are stripped, and a failed vLLM `/version` probe may still lose request-count admission. The evaluator’s F2 isolation issue also remains. I’m holding off on touching claimed release files or starting another test run while the owner’s full gate is active."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793825880220,"completed_at_ms":1793825883291}}
