{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:00:53.847Z","ordinal":113587,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a85d-5ed6-7570-9d8e-ca697d5459cc","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED before implementation.** The proposed work targets the right areas, but the cache rule and argument-normalization boundary need sharper acceptance criteria. The existing [WP-1107 plan](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:41) currently says gateway task-class routing survives unavailable rediscovery; that conflicts with the requirement to prevent a stale gateway identity from leaking `X-Task-Class`.\n\n### WP-1107 argument parsing and normalization\n\nMake one canonical parsed call—arguments plus repair status—and use it for dispatch, read tracking, observation keys, and stored assistant history. Right now dispatch normalizes a local `args` value, while tracking uses the original call arguments ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:4889), [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:5797)). Structural-repair write/exec calls also return before dispatch normalization ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:4866)). The client-side normalizer only handles JSON `tool_calls`; it does not establish one canonical representation for text-mode calls.\n\nSpecify that optional `null` is removed only when the declared property schema does **not** allow null. Cover supported nullability forms (`type: [\"string\", \"null\"]`, `anyOf`/`oneOf`, and `enum`/`const` if those forms are supported). Required fields should not be silently removed.\n\nSuggested files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`; tests in `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts` or a new parser-focused test, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, and `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`.\n\nAdd tests for native and repaired/text-mode calls; explicit nullable versus non-nullable optional properties; and equal normalized arguments across Rust dispatch, read tracking, observation identity, and persisted history. Include a repair-required write/exec case to preserve its existing fail-closed behavior.\n\n### WP-1107 provider identity and cache\n\nSeparate cached provider kind from permission to send routing headers. A safe rule to test is:\n\n- On successful contradictory or generic discovery, replace or clear the cached kind.\n- On an unavailable refresh, preserve the last verified kind only for the same endpoint/model and a bounded freshness window; expire it afterward.\n- Suppress `X-Task-Class` whenever the current discovery is unavailable or ambiguous. Re-enable it only after a fresh positive gateway handshake or explicit operator override.\n- On a successful vLLM owner-marker response with a transient `/version` failure, preserve the previously verified vLLM advertisement/token-count source for that same endpoint/model. On model absence or identity mismatch, clear it.\n\nThis lets the client retain vLLM counting during a transient version-probe failure without allowing a stale gateway cache to authorize the header. The current cache is endpoint-only ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1161)); routing headers read that cache directly ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:841)). Spell out cache key, expiry, and the difference between transport adaptation and header authorization in the plan.\n\nAdd tests for gateway → unavailable/404 replacement (no header while stale), fresh gateway recovery, gateway → positive non-gateway replacement, endpoint/model changes, vLLM `/version` failure retaining request counting, and expiry. Existing tests cover parts of discovery and strict adaptation, but the current version-outage test does not assert request-count behavior ([client_tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts:119)).\n\n### WP-1105 F2 overlay\n\nFail closed when any candidate change that could affect build/typecheck is excluded from the overlay. Do not silently run the baseline configuration and report a pass. Define the excluded-input policy explicitly, including manifests, compiler/build configuration, `node_modules`, and in-repository build helpers; make checker/dependency inputs immutable to candidate changes.\n\nSuggested files: `eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs`, `eval/evaluators/code/command.mjs` if sandbox mounts need tightening, `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts`, and `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1105-PLAN.md`.\n\nAdd tests proving changed config, `node_modules` checker files, and build-helper files fail before command invocation, while a supported source edit still reaches the evaluator and is detected. Also test added, modified, and deleted excluded paths.\n\nKeep the three areas in separate chunks with exact file claims. Do not count mock-provider tests as G1.1-4 evidence; that gate still requires the exact installed candidate’s live provider matrix. No tests or builds were run for this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793826053.8468783,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3890}}
