{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:04:15.609Z","ordinal":113682,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a860-72f9-7103-909a-c8fe87b59fed","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED.** The criteria are mostly binary and can be split into the proposed slices, but the cache policy needs a stronger header-safety rule, and the nullability acceptance needs a defined rejection path.\n\n### WP-1107-A: canonical arguments\n\nAdd `cli/src/parser.ts` and its tests to the claimed files. The current parser repairs arguments in `parseModelResponse`, while the client normalizer and agent dispatch perform separate processing. Use one canonical call record at both main and subagent parse sites, and use it for dispatch, observation keys/read tracking, and stored assistant history. Keep raw syntax/repair classification available for `toolCallSyntax`.\n\nFor required fields containing null, specify how schema-invalid calls are rejected before dispatch; the current parser does not validate arguments against the tool schema. Also clarify that the existing fail-closed rule rejects **structurally repaired** write/exec calls, rather than implying all syntax repairs are denied.\n\nSuggested tests: native and text/repair calls yield the same canonical arguments across dispatch, tracking, identity, and history; allowed-null forms remain intact; disallowed optional nulls are removed; required nulls are rejected; structurally repaired write/exec calls still have no side effects.\n\n### WP-1107-B: provider identity\n\nA five-minute endpoint/model cache can still be inherited by a newly created client after the endpoint has been replaced. Separate cached provider adaptation/counting from authorization to send `X-Task-Class`: require a fresh positive gateway handshake for that header, and suppress it after an unavailable or ambiguous refresh until verified again (unless explicitly overridden). State that unknown or expired identity cannot enable provider-specific adaptation.\n\nAdd tests for a new client inheriting a recent static cache, a failed refresh after gateway discovery, explicit override, changed endpoint/model, vLLM counting during a transient `/version` outage, cache expiry, and recovery. The existing plan’s “gateway task class survives unavailable rediscovery” criterion should be changed because it conflicts with preventing stale cross-provider header leakage.\n\n### WP-1105-F2: evaluator overlay\n\nThis slice is testable. Specify that **every** changed path outside the supported source overlay—added, modified, or deleted—fails before the evaluator command runs. Define the exact path classes for build helpers and checker/dependency inputs so candidates cannot shadow them. Test those paths alongside a supported source-only change.\n\nThe relevant paths are `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts` (or another existing parser test file), `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`, `eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs`, and `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts`. Update the WP plan and release limitation records under claims. Keep the three slices separate; no tests or builds were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793826255.609067,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3896}}
