{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:05:49.600Z","ordinal":113729,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a861-e21f-7232-85f3-1cd422a44374","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**Not yet approved.** The revised criteria resolve the header-leak concern by separating per-client header authorization from the bounded provider cache. Add two explicit cases before implementation:\n\n1. **Cold vLLM probe failure:** Without a prior successful owner-marker-plus-version handshake inside the five-minute window, a transient `/version` failure must leave the provider unknown and disable strict adaptation/counting. Retention should require both that prior verified handshake and a current matching `owned_by: vllm` model entry. Add a test for cold failure as well as warm failure and expiry.\n\n2. **Dependency immutability during execution:** Failing before invocation when candidate changes touch `node_modules` or build helpers prevents static shadowing, but clarify whether those protected inputs must also remain read-only while the evaluator command runs. If so, include a regression proving the command cannot modify the checker/dependency paths; otherwise narrow the contract to candidate changes detected before invocation.\n\nThe argument-record and excluded-path criteria are otherwise testable, provided the canonical record reaches both main and subagent paths and the tests compare dispatch, tracking, identity, and stored history. No tests or builds were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793826349.599527,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3901}}
