{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:07:22.900Z","ordinal":113776,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a863-4e94-7572-9111-643b8cd36096","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**APPROVED WITH ONE SCOPE CONDITION.** The revised WP-1107 criteria close the cache and nullability gaps: only a prior successful vLLM handshake can be retained through a matching-catalog `/version` outage, and task-class headers require fresh positive gateway verification for that client.\n\nFor WP-1105-F2, the read-only execution requirement needs these implementation files explicitly in the plan and claims: `eval/evaluators/code/command.mjs`, `build.mjs`, and `typecheck_clean.mjs`, alongside `runner.mjs` and `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts`. The build and typecheck wrappers must pass protected paths through to the command runner; the runner must reject unsafe or symlinked protected paths. The existing [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/isolate.mjs:760) already supports read-only mounts, so it need not change unless the implementation finds a gap.\n\nThe malicious-command regression should show that a write to a protected sentinel fails and leaves it unchanged, while a permitted build-output write succeeds. Tests should use the isolated command path, not just a mock runner.\n\nNo tests or builds were run; exact file claims and SUITE release remain prerequisites."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a83e-2c55-7f73-bb41-4b9fa47da4c8","create_time":1793826442.9001448,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3905}}
