d two failing. Hidden validators are false by design; this fixture measures execution and prompt boundaries, not task-solving quality or provider quality. The final stable archive must receive its own acceptance run. |\n | WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | The c198a33f archive was installed through the production installer and its package-runtime acceptance passed 5/5 in an uncontended rerun. | **PACKAGE RUNTIME PASS — c198a33f RC2** | `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` log SHA-256 `045f31fa6c0d85f132c37d49134f62e03c61ad839fdaab52c1da2b42ffba94d1`; the test used isolated HOME and the exact archive. Repeat against the final stable archive. |\n | WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`; codex-root fixed review findings through `2dbe565b` (symlink overlay, Rust diagnostics, coded-diagnostic pattern). | **SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED** | `code_evaluators.test.ts` passes on the final head (see the final gate). Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#code-evaluators-wp-1105): fail-open overlay for non-listed file types, shadowing through `node_modules` and build helpers, snapshot limits, no resource limits. The evaluators are not used by any dataset task yet. |\n-| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n+| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. Entire's automated review of PR #402 found a HIGH defect (the parallel `read_file` path skipped the pause); it was reproduced and fixed in `822c08fb` with a regression test (`AC1b`) that failed first. | **SOURCE PASSES; ONE HIGH FIXED; MEDIUM FINDINGS OPEN (TUI /step) — OWNER-ACCEPTED LIMITATIONS** | `step_loop.test.ts` passes 9/9 on the fixed head. The REPL `/step` test does not exercise the real command, and the TUI `/step` handler has no test. Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#single-step-mode-and-the-tui-wp-1106). |\n | WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. Commits through `0d506762` connect strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**; llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint), and the hybrid reasoning grammars in the roadmap are not implemented. The owner-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **REDUCED SCOPE DELIVERED; SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX NOT MEASURED** | Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#provider-handling-wp-1107): no expiry for the server-kind cache, `X-Task-Class` can reach a replaced non-gateway server, null normalisation gaps, request counting can turn off, matrix provenance not bound to checkout content. G1.1-4 was not measured. |\n | WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n \ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\nindex 42c1e6fe..5541df54 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\n@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ v1.1.2 delivers the WP-1101 to WP-1108 roadmap that was originally planned for v\n \n ## Fixed\n \n+### `--step` now pauses after a cycle of parallel `read_file` calls\n+\n+In `--step` mode, when the model returned two or more `read_file` calls in one turn, the parallel-read path ended the step without applying the single-step pause, so the run could issue further model requests and execute later edits before returning. The parallel path now pauses exactly like the sequential path. A regression test (`AC1b` in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts`) was written first and failed before the fix. This was found by Entire's automated review of PR #402 and reproduced.\n+\n ### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n \n When a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n@@ -59,6 +63,27 @@ Independent reviewers examined the release source and returned REQUEST CHANGES o\n - **Build configuration edits are ignored.** Because the baseline configuration is pinned, a candidate's edits to `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` and similar files are silently ignored by build and `typecheck_clean`, without a report.\n - **Other.** `node --check` exits 0 for a `.js` file written with ESM syntax even when it contains a syntax error (for example `export const a = ;`); a dangling symlink at an overlaid path fails closed with `EEXIST`, and so does a candidate symlink with a source extension; the pinned workspace is created under the system temporary directory, not the configured workspace root; `spec.candidate.cwd` is silently overridden by the pinned root; `--pretty` compiler output defeats the TypeScript diagnostic pattern (fails closed); legacy text-mode tool calls are not counted by the `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; the evaluator README is partly stale.\n \n+### Single-step mode and the TUI (WP-1106)\n+\n+These come from Entire's automated review of PR #402. They were not reproduced one by one by the release owner; the `--step` pause fix above was.\n+\n+- **The TUI `/step` command calls the turn runner directly.** It creates no rollback checkpoint, so a later `/undo` can discard the preceding turn's work along with the step; it emits no live tool events and saves no session; and a blocked turn is reported as \"Step completed\".\n+- **`/step` cannot be cancelled** from the TUI while its cycle runs (the command is not marked cancellable).\n+- **A stagnation stop is overwritten by the step pause**, and the pause skips the end-of-step bookkeeping, so stagnation detection does not advance across `/step` calls.\n+- **Test coverage is thin.** The REPL `/step` test does not drive the real command, and the TUI `/step` handler has no test.\n+\n+### Evaluation CLI and datasets (WP-1103, WP-1104, WP-1105)\n+\n+- **`--isolated-home` is honoured only when `eval` is the first argument.** With a global option in front (for example `nexus -e URL eval --dataset d --isolated-home`) the flag is accepted and ignored, and the run uses the operator's real home and configuration. Put `eval` first.\n+- **`diff_boundary` can reject a valid patch** for a non-hardened task that has hidden tests: the runner stages them into the candidate workspace before the comparison, so they count as agent changes.\n+- **Two sources of truth.** `eval/datasets/core-v1/tasks/*` copies `eval/tasks/*`, and the evaluator runtime file list exists in two places that already differ.\n+\n+### Other\n+\n+- **Tracing:** the OTLP instrumentation scope version is hard-coded to `1.1.0`, so trace records carry the wrong instrumentation version.\n+- **Tool grammar:** the GBNF compiler (`generateToolArgumentsGbnf`, `generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars`) has no runtime caller; only the tool allow-list is used. It ships with its own tests only.\n+- **Redaction layers:** sidecar text is redacted per field and again per event, which corrupted workspace paths badly enough to need an exception for `session.state`; file paths and diffs in other events are redacted twice with no such exception. Four identical diagnostic-redaction helpers exist in the CLI, and the REPL step error path skips redaction. Null stripping for optional tool arguments is also done twice.\n+\n ## Runtime requirements\n \n Unchanged from v1.1.1: Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer, Node.js 22 or newer, and an OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint (local or an explicitly selected provider). The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime.\n20261103022909Z ACQUIRE FILE_cli_src_slash_session_commands.ts wp-1106-step-tui-sync\n20261103023405Z RELEASE FILE_cli_src_slash_catalog.ts wp-1106-step-tui-sync\n20261103023405Z RELEASE FILE_cli_src_slash_session_commands.ts wp-1106-step-tui-sync\n20261103023443Z ACQUIRE WP-1108 wp-1108-dependency-modernization\n20261103023509Z RELEASE WP-1108 wp-1108-dependency-modernization\n20261103023554Z RELEASE_STALE FILE_cli_test_evaluator_diagnostic_redaction.test.ts\n20261103023554Z RELEASE_STALE FILE_cli_test_provider_cli_diagnostic_redaction.test.ts\n20261103023657Z ACQUIRE WP-1102 wp-1102-integration\n20261103023829Z RELEASE WP-1102 wp-1102-integration\n20261103T025719Z RELEASE FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md antigravity v1.1.2 qualification record updated and committed at 7e3b170b\n2026-11-03T20:21:55Z CLAIM SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 focused RED and exact candidate gates\n2026-11-04T03:38:02.687760+00:00 CLAIM FILE_cli_src_agent.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 remediation\n2026-11-04T03:38:02.687760+00:00 CLAIM FILE_cli_test_vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 remediation\n2026-11-04T03:38:02.687760+00:00 CLAIM FILE_cli_test_task_class.test.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 remediation\n2026-11-04T03:38:02.687760+00:00 CLAIM FILE_docs_LOCAL_SERVERS.md owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 remediation\n2026-11-04T03:40:33.768781+00:00 CLAIM SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 AC7 focused RED test\n2026-11-04T03:46:03.618476+00:00 RELEASE SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=WP-1107 AC7 focused RED observed Rust null rejection; green real RPC execution PASS\n2026-11-04T03:48:50.036778+00:00 CLAIM SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 AC8 focused RED tests\n2026-11-04T03:55:25.267967+00:00 RELEASE SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=AC8 focused task_class suite green 8/8; no active runner\n2026-11-04T04:01:36.986797+00:00 RELEASE FILE_cli_test_server_context_discovery.test.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=read-only compatibility fixtures already satisfy owner+version; no edits planned\n2026-11-04T04:01:36.986797+00:00 RELEASE FILE_cli_test_tokens.test.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=read-only compatibility fixtures already satisfy owner+version; no edits planned\n2026-11-04T04:01:36.986797+00:00 RELEASE FILE_cli_test_standalone_profiles.test.ts owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=read-only compatibility fixtures already satisfy owner+version; no edits planned\n2026-11-04T04:02:09.246982+00:00 CLAIM SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 AC10 focused RED tests\n2026-11-04T04:03:37.364879+00:00 RELEASE SUITE owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration outcome=AC10 focused 29/29 and compatibility 26/26 PASS; no active runner\n2026-11-04T15:09:42Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_NOTE candidate=2a94f62e branch=v1/v112-wp1104-integration reviewer=antigravity tsc=PASS focused=19/20_pass_3_skip remaining_failure=env(review-worktree node_modules symlink outside sandbox runtime allowlist) verdict=NO_DEFECT_FOUND_FOCUSED_ONLY superseded_by=eb6884df/PR402\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828015.7308078}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
