{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:37:25.914Z","ordinal":114543,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a87e-d199-7b93-9d35-92bad0db6543","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**Read-only follow-up: CHANGES_REQUESTED on the current plan wording; the remaining findings are real and the proposed fixes are testable.** Reviewed `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release` at `822c08fb`. I made no edits and ran no tests.\n\n- **Provider rediscovery:** [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1161) retains identity by endpoint on unavailable, 404, or missing-model discovery, while [routingHeaders](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:841) uses that shared cache to authorize `X-Task-Class`. The cache also drives strict-schema adaptation and `/tokenize` routing ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:1342)). The plan’s AC1 still says a gateway header “survives unavailable rediscovery” ([WP-1105-PLAN.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1105-PLAN.md:45)); that conflicts with preventing a stale gateway header after same-endpoint replacement. Separate **bounded provider adaptation/counting retention** from **per-client gateway-header authorization**: keep adaptation only for the same normalized endpoint and model, within the five-minute window after positive verification; disable the header on any unavailable or ambiguous refresh until a fresh positive gateway handshake or explicit override. For warm vLLM, retain strict adaptation and counting through `/version` failure only with prior positive owner-plus-version verification, a current matching vLLM model entry, and an unexpired cache. Test warm/cold vLLM, model mismatch/change, expiry/recovery, unavailable gateway refresh, new client inheriting shared cache, and explicit override.\n\n- **Canonical arguments:** The helper at [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:42) removes null from all optional top-level properties without checking whether the schema permits null, and client-side normalization covers returned native `tool_calls` only ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/client.ts:58)). Text-mode calls are parsed later at both main and subagent entry points ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:6100), [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:6979)). Dispatch normalizes a local `args` value, but tracking still uses the original `call.function.arguments` ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:5788)); observation keys and history also derive from the unnormalized call ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:3167), [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/src/agent.ts:6143)). The plan’s client-boundary AC4 is therefore too narrow ([WP-1105-PLAN.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1105-PLAN.md:49)). Normalize once after parsing at both agent entry points into a canonical call record, then use its args for dispatch, read tracking, observation identity, and persisted history. Preserve syntax/repair classification; reject disallowed required null before dispatch; remove optional null only when the schema establishes that null is disallowed, preserving nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` cases. Test native, text, and repaired calls; dispatch/tracking/key/history agreement; nullable and required null; and write/exec structural-repair denial.\n\n**Claims and handoff:** `cli/src/agent.ts` is actively claimed by `claude-code` for the `--step` fix, and the `SUITE` claim is held for the exact-head gate. Do not edit or validate until those owners release the relevant claim/lane. The matrix test file is claimed by `codex-root` with a stale heartbeat; ask its owner to confirm/release it before claiming that file. Claim the remaining client/parser and focused test files atomically before implementation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828245.9139576,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3964}}
