{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:38:55.029Z","ordinal":114589,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba5ed88c081a3be58526c9fc4b3c3","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ve confirmed the existing plan needs two distinct contracts: cached provider behavior may preserve strict adaptation/counting briefly, while task-class headers require fresh, client-specific gateway confirmation; and argument normalization must happen once before both dispatch and observation. I’m revising the claimed plan to make those boundaries and the matrix integrity checks testable before asking for another plan review."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793828333567,"completed_at_ms":1793828335029}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:38:55.032Z","ordinal":114590,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba5ed88c081a3be58526c9fc4b3c3","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’ve confirmed the existing plan needs two distinct contracts: cached provider behavior may preserve strict adaptation/counting briefly, while task-class headers require fresh, client-specific gateway confirmation; and argument normalization must happen once before both dispatch and observation. I’m revising the claimed plan to make those boundaries and the matrix integrity checks testable before asking for another plan review.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828333.536583,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba5ed88c081a3be58526c9fc4b3c3","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1a880-2db8-7a83-9b85-f5bad7e3229c","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3966}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:39:14.976Z","ordinal":114591,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aeba5ef028c81a388bfb6bd8711420f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_5bd8754437424e689c1667c09883d316","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC8:** Without an explicit operator override, `X-Task-Class` is sent only for a positively identified gateway. First-time unknown discovery and a failed standalone handshake suppress it; a failed `/models` refresh retains a prior positive gateway identity only for the same endpoint URL; changing endpoint or receiving a successful but generic catalog clears that prior identity. Tests: `task class is suppressed without a positive gateway handshake`; `failed rediscovery retains gateway identity only for the same endpoint`; `successful generic rediscovery clears prior gateway identity`.\\n+- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a successful mismatching catalog clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` is sent only after a fresh positive gateway handshake by that client or an explicit operator override; unavailable/ambiguous refresh suppresses it until fresh verification. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation with matching model`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\\n@@\\n - **AC13:** Before matrix inference, every installed package file (apart from the installer-owned provenance record) must match the verified archive snapshot's exact file set and SHA-256 digests; a matching but forged provenance record cannot make a modified installed runtime qualify. Test `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance` asserts rejection before any provider/client call and before evidence output is written.\\n+- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema forbids null; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, while schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `native text and repaired tool calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\\n+- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted inputs: the declared source commit must equal the immutable candidate revision supplied by the qualification invocation, and archive SHA-256 must be required and match the exact archive copied into the private verified snapshot. A self-written provenance/source record cannot override either value. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\\n@@\\n-1. Normalize strict-mode optional nulls — files: `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\\n-2. Preserve endpoint identity and gate task-class headers — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`; tests: all three AC8 tests.\\n+1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\\n+2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests.\\n@@\\n-4. Snapshot, verify, and bind matrix runtime bytes — files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`; tests: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`; `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance`.\\n+4. Snapshot, verify, and bind matrix runtime bytes and evidence identity — files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`; tests: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`; `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance`; all AC15 tests.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828335.0119023}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:39:15.008Z","ordinal":114592,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-a9ff667f-f8eb-4c69-baeb-81b442fab075","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -75,3 +75,3 @@\n - **AC7:** In a real `write_file` and `run_command` dispatch through the Rust RPC bridge, vLLM strict-mode `null` values for originally optional `write_file.overwrite`, `run_command.background`, and `run_command.timeout_secs` are omitted before deserialization; required fields and non-null optional values are preserved, and both executors succeed. Test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n-- **AC8:** Without an explicit operator override, `X-Task-Class` is sent only for a positively identified gateway. First-time unknown discovery and a failed standalone handshake suppress it; a failed `/models` refresh retains a prior positive gateway identity only for the same endpoint URL; changing endpoint or receiving a successful but generic catalog clears that prior identity. Tests: `task class is suppressed without a positive gateway handshake`; `failed rediscovery retains gateway identity only for the same endpoint`; `successful generic rediscovery clears prior gateway identity`.\n+- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a successful mismatching catalog clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` is sent only after a fresh positive gateway handshake by that client or an explicit operator override; unavailable/ambiguous refresh suppresses it until fresh verification. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation with matching model`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\n - **AC9:** The matrix copies the archive into a private snapshot, verifies archive digest, installer provenance, manifest contents, exact file set and every file digest without following symlinks, then imports only from that same verified snapshot. A deterministic substitution of the installed runtime after snapshot verification and before import cannot affect the measured code. Test: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`.\n@@ -81,2 +81,4 @@\n - **AC13:** Before matrix inference, every installed package file (apart from the installer-owned provenance record) must match the verified archive snapshot's exact file set and SHA-256 digests; a matching but forged provenance record cannot make a modified installed runtime qualify. Test `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance` asserts rejection before any provider/client call and before evidence output is written.\n+- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema forbids null; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, while schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `native text and repaired tool calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\n+- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted inputs: the declared source commit must equal the immutable candidate revision supplied by the qualification invocation, and archive SHA-256 must be required and match the exact archive copied into the private verified snapshot. A self-written provenance/source record cannot override either value. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\n \n@@ -92,6 +94,6 @@\n \n-1. Normalize strict-mode optional nulls — files: `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n-2. Preserve endpoint identity and gate task-class headers — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`; tests: all three AC8 tests.\n+1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n+2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests.\n 3. Require positive vLLM identity — files: `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`; tests: both AC10 tests plus existing context/token-counting and standalone-profile regressions in the full suite.\n-4. Snapshot, verify, and bind matrix runtime bytes — files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`; tests: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`; `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance`.\n+4. Snapshot, verify, and bind matrix runtime bytes and evidence identity — files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`; tests: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`; `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance`; all AC15 tests.\n 5. Complete optional and unknown-name dispatch boundaries — files: `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`; tests: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge` (shell cases); `unknown special-name tools do not enter nullable argument normalization` (ordinary unknown receipt/result through terminal reporting).\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793828355006,"completed_at_ms":1793828355008}}
