mp;utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&amp;utm_content=402\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">CodeRabbit</a>! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&amp;url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">X</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Mastodon</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&amp;text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Reddit</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&amp;mini=true&amp;title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&amp;summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">LinkedIn</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#discussion_r4460235650\",\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace\\n\\nThis information exposed to the user depends on [stack trace information](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/security/code-scanning/52)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"name\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4\",\"id\":62310815},\"id\":4460235650,\"pull_request_review_id\":5759223090,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"line\":94,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":\"eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\",\"body_html\":\"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This information exposed to the user depends on <a href=\\\"1\\\">stack trace information</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/security/code-scanning/52\\\">Show more details</a></p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#pullrequestreview-5759223090\",\"body\":\"\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"name\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4\",\"id\":62310815},\"id\":5759223090,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"updated_at\":null,\"review\":\"COMMENTED\",\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6620818765\",\"body\":\"Independent review of commit 5fde750a (WP-1107 provider-specific tool schemas; parent 3eea888a; not yet on any PR): **REQUEST CHANGES**.\\n\\nFocused tests pass (client_tool_grammar 16, provider_capabilities 12, server_context_discovery 17, standalone_profiles 5, tokens 4, task_class 5, tool_grammar 4, tool_grammar_matrix 10, client_robustness 9, eval matrix test 10; tsc clean). The findings below are not caught by them.\\n\\n**HIGH - vLLM strict mode breaks write_file and run_command at execution.** `tool_grammar_provider.ts` turns every optional parameter into a required nullable one, so a strict-mode model emits `overwrite:null` / `background:null`. The Rust core declares plain `bool` fields (`file_ops.rs:37`, `runner.rs:19`) and rejects them: `Invalid write_file arguments: invalid type: null, expected a boolean` (reviewer built the core from this commit and called `executeTool`; `timeout_secs`, `shell`, `cwd` nulls succeeded). Nothing strips nulls before dispatch. The matrix cannot catch it: it accepts any call that satisfies the adapted schema, which allows null. Fix: strip nulls for fields that were optional before adaptation (client/dispatch path), or make the core accept null; add an end-to-end test through the real executor.\\n\\n**MEDIUM - REQ-PRV-109 (no X-Task-Class to standalone local servers unless configured) holds only on the success path.** A failed handshake now demotes the kind to `unknown`, and `routingHeaders()` sends the header for unknown. Reproduced at head but not at base: llama.cpp marker with /props 404; Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404; vLLM with /version 404; `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0`; and a periodic rediscovery where /models returns 500 resets a known kind to unknown. Fix: decide the header from the catalog-level kind, and keep the previous kind when rediscovery is unavailable. `task_class.test.ts` is unchanged and covers only success.\\n\\n**MEDIUM - the matrix runner does not enforce \\\"only the verified installed candidate\\\".** It trusts a self-attested `.provenance.json` inside the caller-supplied installRoot. Reproduced: a forged provenance file + hand-written lib/cli/dist + unrelated archive is accepted (passed:true); a symlinked `lib` outside installRoot is run (no realpath); swapping the symlink after the provenance read runs the swapped runtime (TOCTOU). The RED/GREEN test is real but guards a cosmetic check (`Object.hasOwn(options,\\\"runtime\\\")`, an option that is never consumed). Fix: realpath installRoot, verify MANIFEST.sha256 and the archive-to-install link, verify once and import from the same resolved path.\\n\\n**MEDIUM-LOW - vLLM identity is weak.** Any catalog entry with `max_model_len`/`context_length` plus a /version route is classified vllm and gets `strict:true`; requiring `owned_by: vllm` would be stricter.\\n\\nLow/nits: plan AC4 test names do not exist; `identityCached` is dead; docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md not updated; adaptToolDefinitionsForServer throws on an optional array/object param (unreachable today); Ollama /api/show `model` mismatch demotes to unknown.\\n\\nFixture changes (Q1): the three old assertions that fail against the new source (Ollama via 'catalog' vs 'ollama', vLLM extra GET /version, tokens 404) are legitimate updates to the new identity rule; standalone_profiles is strengthened; no weakening found. Coverage lost: nothing asserts context discovery for a vLLM catalog without /version.\\n\\nNot verified: live vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama servers or vLLM strict acceptance; full npm test / make test (only the final7 log counts were read); TUI /model e2e; packaged installer layout.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6620818765,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T02:22:51Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T02:22:51Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of commit <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b\\\"><tt>5fde750</tt></a> (WP-1107 provider-specific tool schemas; parent <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/3eea888abbf20b4b63c75c2b554debd67038f5a1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/3eea888abbf20b4b63c75c2b554debd67038f5a1\\\"><tt>3eea888</tt></a>; not yet on any PR): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Focused tests pass (client_tool_grammar 16, provider_capabilities 12, server_context_discovery 17, standalone_profiles 5, tokens 4, task_class 5, tool_grammar 4, tool_grammar_matrix 10, client_robustness 9, eval matrix test 10; tsc clean). The findings below are not caught by them.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>HIGH - vLLM strict mode breaks write_file and run_command at execution.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tool_grammar_provider.ts</code> turns every optional parameter into a required nullable one, so a strict-mode model emits <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">overwrite:null</code> / <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">background:null</code>. The Rust core declares plain <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bool</code> fields (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">file_ops.rs:37</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runner.rs:19</code>) and rejects them: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Invalid write_file arguments: invalid type: null, expected a boolean</code> (reviewer built the core from this commit and called <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">executeTool</code>; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">timeout_secs</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">shell</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cwd</code> nulls succeeded). Nothing strips nulls before dispatch. The matrix cannot catch it: it accepts any call that satisfies the adapted schema, which allows null. Fix: strip nulls for fields that were optional before adaptation (client/dispatch path), or make the core accept null; add an end-to-end test through the real executor.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM - REQ-PRV-109 (no X-Task-Class to standalone local servers unless configured) holds only on the success path.</strong> A failed handshake now demotes the kind to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">unknown</code>, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">routingHeaders()</code> sends the header for unknown. Reproduced at head but not at base: llama.cpp marker with /props 404; Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404; vLLM with /version 404; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0</code>; and a periodic rediscovery where /models returns 500 resets a known kind to unknown. Fix: decide the header from the catalog-level kind, and keep the previous kind when rediscovery is unavailable. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">task_class.test.ts</code> is unchanged and covers only success.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM - the matrix runner does not enforce \\\"only the verified installed candidate\\\".</strong> It trusts a self-attested <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.provenance.json</code> inside the caller-supplied installRoot. Reproduced: a forged provenance file + hand-written lib/cli/dist + unrelated archive is accepted (passed:true); a symlinked <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">lib</code> outside installRoot is run (no realpath); swapping the symlink after the provenance read runs the swapped runtime (TOCTOU). The RED/GREEN test is real but guards a cosmetic check (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Object.hasOwn(options,\\\"runtime\\\")</code>, an option that is never consumed). Fix: realpath installRoot, verify MANIFEST.sha256 and the archive-to-install link, verify once and import from the same resolved path.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM-LOW - vLLM identity is weak.</strong> Any catalog entry with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">max_model_len</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">context_length</code> plus a /version route is classified vllm and gets <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">strict:true</code>; requiring <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">owned_by: vllm</code> would be stricter.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Low/nits: plan AC4 test names do not exist; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">identityCached</code> is dead; docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md not updated; adaptToolDefinitionsForServer throws on an optional array/object param (unreachable today); Ollama /api/show <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">model</code> mismatch demotes to unknown.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixture changes (Q1): the three old assertions that fail against the new source (Ollama via 'catalog' vs 'ollama', vLLM extra GET /version, tokens 404) are legitimate updates to the new identity rule; standalone_profiles is strengthened; no weakening found. Coverage lost: nothing asserts context discovery for a vLLM catalog without /version.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: live vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama servers or vLLM strict acceptance; full npm test / make test (only the final7 log counts were read); TUI /model e2e; packaged installer layout.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6626037487\",\"body\":\"Independent review of the WP-1105 evaluator work as of 5fde750a (everything after the last independent review at 08aace7d): **REQUEST CHANGES**. Sandbox containment is solid and the telemetry counts each call once; three MEDIUM issues mean the evaluators can pass without measuring anything or fail honest runs.\\n\\nTests: code_evaluators 22/22, parser_safety 12, parser_single_quote 10, eval/dataset 12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. eval_dataset.test.ts was refused by a host compiler-exposure check before any evaluator ran (read as a host limit).\\n\\n**F1 MEDIUM - typecheck_clean passes vacuously when the checker cannot run on either side.** `typecheck_clean.mjs:41-49` tolerates any failing baseline if the candidate adds no new diagnostic lines. With real tsc and no node_modules on either side: 12 identical \\\"Cannot find module\\\" lines, passed:true, score 1; a candidate syntax error the checker never saw also passed; a bwrap setup failure with identical stderr passes the same way. Fix: require a recognised baseline state (exit 0, or a task-supplied diagnostic regex such as `error TS\\\\d+`).\\n\\n**F2 MEDIUM - build and typecheck_clean run the candidate-modified build config.** `run.mjs:308` passes the agent-modified tree; hardened mode's configChanges refusal covers only hidden/regression checks. A candidate that rewrote tsconfig.json to `\\\"files\\\":[\\\"empty.ts\\\"]` while keeping a new error file got passed:true. Fix: pin config from the baseline, or make diff_boundary cover config files; document it.\\n\\n**F3 MEDIUM - syntax_ast with the runner's default file list false-fails honest agents.** `runner.mjs:162` uses `spec.files ?? changedFiles`, which includes deleted and non-source paths: an edit to src/a.ts + delete of src/old.ts + edit of README.md gives passed:false (`unsupported source extension`, `ENOENT`). Any task without `spec.files` can never pass if the agent deletes a file or edits a non-code file.\\n\\nF4 LOW-MEDIUM: evaluator commands have no memory/pid/disk limits (`command.mjs` calls runProcess without `resources`; only wall time and the 4 MiB output cap bound them). F5 LOW-MEDIUM: in-process TypeScript parsing has no timeout (65 MB file blocked the event loop 62.9 s). F6 LOW: a relative command path/symlink resolving outside the workspace runs a host script (trusted config; small exposure). F7 LOW: typecheck_clean false-fails on benign line-shift or summary-count changes (fails closed). F8 nits: legacy text parsing is not counted; `hiddenWorkspace` unused; root `.git` changes invisible to diff_boundary (documented).\\n\\nHeld up: argv is passed literally, no shell, env scrubbed, caps 0/NoNewPrivs, symlinked-directory and /etc/shadow escapes return ENOENT, 25 MB output killed, timeout kills trap-TERM and setsid descendants, snapshot uses O_NOFOLLOW + inode checks, telemetry counts once per call with a single subagent roll-up (real `nexus run --json` checked), the 18-row typecheck case table behaves as designed.\\n\\nTest gaps (mutations that survived): baseline-status-0 term of the regression rule; sibling-directory escape (`/tmp/ws-evil`); root `.git` skip; per-turn reset of turnToolCallSyntax; no tests for output overflow, command-symlink confinement, or syntax_ast with deleted/non-source files.\\n\\nNot verified: harness end to end (blocked by the host check), eval_hardened/eval_integrity/eval_harness/tool_grammar_matrix, a real fork bomb, spoofing of agent --json stdout, Node versions other than 24.11.1, agent.ts changes outside the telemetry hunks.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6626037487,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T08:15:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T08:15:39Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of the WP-1105 evaluator work as of <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b\\\"><tt>5fde750</tt></a> (everything after the last independent review at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/08aace7dc64405c04bca72abe2a64da532782380/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/08aace7dc64405c04bca72abe2a64da532782380\\\"><tt>08aace7</tt></a>): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>. Sandbox containment is solid and the telemetry counts each call once; three MEDIUM issues mean the evaluators can pass without measuring anything or fail honest runs.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Tests: code_evaluators 22/22, parser_safety 12, parser_single_quote 10, eval/dataset 12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. eval_dataset.test.ts was refused by a host compiler-exposure check before any evaluator ran (read as a host limit).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F1 MEDIUM - typecheck_clean passes vacuously when the checker cannot run on either side.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">typecheck_clean.mjs:41-49</code> tolerates any failing baseline if the candidate adds no new diagnostic lines. With real tsc and no node_modules on either side: 12 identical \\\"Cannot find module\\\" lines, passed:true, score 1; a candidate syntax error the checker never saw also passed; a bwrap setup failure with identical stderr passes the same way. Fix: require a recognised baseline state (exit 0, or a task-supplied diagnostic regex such as <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error TS\\\\d+</code>).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F2 MEDIUM - build and typecheck_clean run the candidate-modified build config.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">run.mjs:308</code> passes the agent-modified tree; hardened mode's configChanges refusal covers only hidden/regression checks. A candidate that rewrote tsconfig.json to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\\"files\\\":[\\\"empty.ts\\\"]</code> while keeping a new error file got passed:true. Fix: pin config from the baseline, or make diff_boundary cover config files; document it.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F3 MEDIUM - syntax_ast with the runner's default file list false-fails honest agents.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runner.mjs:162</code> uses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">spec.files ?? changedFiles</code>, which includes deleted and non-source paths: an edit to src/a.ts + delete of src/old.ts + edit of README.md gives passed:false (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">unsupported source extension</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENOENT</code>). Any task without <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">spec.files</code> can never pass if the agent deletes a file or edits a non-code file.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">F4 LOW-MEDIUM: evaluator commands have no memory/pid/disk limits (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">command.mjs</code> calls runProcess without <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">resources</code>; only wall time and the 4 MiB output cap bound them). F5 LOW-MEDIUM: in-process TypeScript parsing has no timeout (65 MB file blocked the event loop 62.9 s). F6 LOW: a relative command path/symlink resolving outside the workspace runs a host script (trusted config; small exposure). F7 LOW: typecheck_clean false-fails on benign line-shift or summary-count changes (fails closed). F8 nits: legacy text parsing is not counted; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hiddenWorkspace</code> unused; root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.git</code> changes invisible to diff_boundary (documented).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Held up: argv is passed literally, no shell, env scrubbed, caps 0/NoNewPrivs, symlinked-directory and /etc/shadow escapes return ENOENT, 25 MB output killed, timeout kills trap-TERM and setsid descendants, snapshot uses O_NOFOLLOW + inode checks, telemetry counts once per call with a single subagent roll-up (real <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">nexus run --json</code> checked), the 18-row typecheck case table behaves as designed.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Test gaps (mutations that survived): baseline-status-0 term of the regression rule; sibling-directory escape (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/tmp/ws-evil</code>); root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.git</code> skip; per-turn reset of turnToolCallSyntax; no tests for output overflow, command-symlink confinement, or syntax_ast with deleted/non-source files.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: harness end to end (blocked by the host check), eval_hardened/eval_integrity/eval_harness/tool_grammar_matrix, a real fork bomb, spoofing of agent --json stdout, Node versions other than 24.11.1, agent.ts changes outside the telemetry hunks.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6626957823\",\"body\":\"Independent delta review of b032791e (WP-1107 remediation, parent 7f915894, local-only commit by codex-root): **REQUEST CHANGES** - 3 of the 4 earlier WP-1107 findings are FIXED, one is PARTIAL.\\n\\n**1. HIGH null optional args: FIXED.** Driven through `AutonomousAgent.dispatchToolCall` against the real harness-core built from this commit: every optional field of read_file (start_line, end_line, offset, length), write_file (overwrite), edit_file (replace_all) and run_command (cwd, timeout_secs, shell, background, service_name) reaches the core without error, alone or all-null. Required fields given as null (path, content, old_content, new_content, command) are still rejected before dispatch and nothing is defaulted or written. `overwrite:null` on an existing file is refused like `false`; `content:\\\"\\\"`, `shell:\\\"\\\"`, `cwd:\\\"\\\"`, `timeout_secs:0` are not stripped. Mutation: removing the strip block makes vllm_nullable_dispatch fail with \\\"invalid type: null, expected a boolean\\\".\\n\\n**2. MEDIUM REQ-PRV-109 X-Task-Class: PARTIAL.** The leak is closed: llama.cpp /props 404, Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404, vLLM /version 404, `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0`, bare catalog and no /models all suppress the header now (sent at 7f915894); rediscovery 503/bad JSON/dropped connection also suppresses it. Gateway still sends it. Mutations show the new task_class tests are real (8 fails with the fix reverted). **Not fixed:** on an unreadable-/models rediscovery (also /models 404 and \\\"model not listed\\\") a previously known llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM endpoint still falls to kind `unknown`, so vLLM loses `strict` and the root /tokenize fallback, while the agent keeps the last advertisement - the two disagree. The plan's AC8 narrows retention to gateway only. Identical at 7f915894 and b032791e. Suggested fix: keep the previous kind when rediscovery returns unavailable.\\n\\n**3. MEDIUM matrix runner: FIXED.** Rejected: forged provenance + handwritten dist + unrelated archive, forged MANIFEST, symlinked lib/ or installRoot (or a symlink in its parent path), installed file symlinked to the archive, archives containing a symlink/hardlink, extra installed files, wrong pinned digest, caller runtime/tools options, revision mismatch. Swapping client.js, installRoot or the archive after verification has no effect (only the private verified snapshot runs). Regression test fails when the post-snapshot verification, the import-from-snapshot or the per-file digest compare is removed; the provenance check, installed-symlink check, realpath, file-set and package-tree digest compare are defence in depth and untested.\\n\\n**4. MEDIUM-LOW vLLM identity: FIXED.** max_model_len/context_length + a /version route without `owned_by:\\\"vllm\\\"` is now `unknown`, strict false; real vLLM responses are still `vllm`.\\n\\nRegression sweep (focused files, isolated HOME): client_tool_grammar 16/16, provider_capabilities 13/13, server_context_discovery 17/17, standalone_profiles 5/5, tokens 4/4, task_class 8/8, tool_grammar 4/4, tool_…49509 chars truncated…ance after release. The c198a33f RC2 archive is historical only: PR head `8520d9c8` and the final stable-version source still require exact-head gates and a fresh stable artifact. The supported-provider G1.1-4 matrix remains pending on the external GATEWAY handoff. No tag or release assets were published.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636044593,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:29:56Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:29:56Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Qualification handoff: doc/evidence commit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">63e2f49c28160408afeeeca4245f10e2bead0c8b</code> is now on <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">v1/v112-wp1101-integration</code>; it contains no source-code changes. The updated qualification record is independently approved and passes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sync-version --check</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">check_requirements</code>, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --check</code>. It records the <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> source gate, reproducible RC2 package/provenance, five exact-suite skip reasons, CI/CodeQL snapshot, and the provisional status of the package-runtime 5/5 run.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I released the 30 WP-1105/WP-1107 source/test/plan/qualification file claims from that worktree. The shared SUITE claim remains held by claude-code; rerun package-runtime acceptance after release. The <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> RC2 archive is historical only: PR head <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">8520d9c8</code> and the final stable-version source still require exact-head gates and a fresh stable artifact. The supported-provider G1.1-4 matrix remains pending on the external GATEWAY handoff. No tag or release assets were published.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636154321\",\"body\":\"Coordination note for the current SUITE holder: there is no matching test process visible on the shared host. Please release the claim when the focused review is complete so I can rerun the exact c198a33f package-runtime acceptance; I will not take the lane while the claim remains held. If the review is still active, I will wait within its 60-minute claim window.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636154321,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:34:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:34:40Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Coordination note for the current SUITE holder: there is no matching test process visible on the shared host. Please release the claim when the focused review is complete so I can rerun the exact <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> package-runtime acceptance; I will not take the lane while the claim remains held. If the review is still active, I will wait within its 60-minute claim window.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636183487\",\"body\":\"Independent short review of 0d506762..c198a33f (reviewer agent, not the author; real bwrap sandbox + real tsc + real runCodeEvaluators in a detached worktree at c198a33f; focused tests only): **REQUEST CHANGES** on one NEW finding. The symlink fix, the sidecar change and the grammar test are fine.\\n\\n**NEW P1 - typecheck_clean regex reopens the vacuous pass.** 05913af5 changed `/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:/i` to `/\\\\berror(?:\\\\s+TS\\\\d+|\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\])?:/i`; the code group is now optional, so the bare `error:` matches with `/i` and Node's `Error: Cannot find module ...` counts as a recognised diagnostic.\\n\\n| Case (real sandbox + real tsc) | 0d506762 | c198a33f |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| (a) no node_modules on both sides | fail, infrastructureFailure true | **passed true, score 1**, infrastructureFailure false |\\n| (b) candidate syntax error, no node_modules | fail | **passed true, score 1** (the candidate error is never evaluated) |\\n| (c) bwrap failure on both sides | fail | fail, infrastructureFailure true |\\n| (d) Rust error[E0308] on both sides | fail (not recognised) | pass; a new error[E0425] fails with newDiagnostics (intended; unit-level only - cargo is not in the runner's /usr/bin,/bin) |\\n| (e) normal added TS error (node_modules present) | fail | fail (same) |\\n\\nAny generic lowercase `error: ...` line is now also \\\"recognised\\\" (e.g. cargo's `error: could not find Cargo.toml`). Only candidates in a workspace with no installed `typescript` are affected. Suggested fix: drop the optional group and require a code, `/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:|\\\\berror\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\]:/` (keep `i` for TS only), and add a test with `Error: Cannot find module` on both sides (no existing test covers it; the unavailable-checker test uses text without the `Error:` prefix).\\n\\n**1. runner.mjs symlink overlay: correct and safe.** P1 reproduced and closed: baseline `src/main.ts` as a symlink to an outside file - at 0d506762 the outside file became the candidate bytes, at c198a33f it stays unchanged. No TOCTOU (fresh mkdtemp tree written only by this process); directory-symlink parents and hardlinks leave the outside file unchanged; overwritten (0755), deleted, nested-new-dir (0640) and new .rs overlays are correct and `fchmod` preserves modes; cleanup removes tempRoot and closes the fd in a finally. Reverting only the fix makes the new test fail - the test is real.\\n\\n**3. sidecar.ts: safe.** `workspace_name` is restored verbatim after redaction as `workspace` already was (without it the name became `[REDACTED:HIGH_ENTROPY_STRING]`); it is only `path.basename(config.workspace)`, a substring of `workspace`, so no new exposure; a fake `ghp_` token in model/session/git.branch is still redacted; the new test fails if the restore line is removed. Existing nit (not new): a secret-shaped directory name still appears verbatim in both fields.\\n\\n**4. client_tool_grammar new test: real** (pins existing behaviour; a sticky vLLM cache in a scratch copy makes it fail).\\n\\n**P3 nit:** a dangling symlink at a path the candidate overlays now fails closed with EEXIST/pinnedWorkspaceError (build and typecheck score 0) because on Node v24.11.1 `fs.rmSync(dangling-link, {force:true})` does not remove it; the old code wrote through the link. Safe, but rejects a valid candidate.\\n\\nTests (isolated HOME, --test-concurrency=1, one file at a time, core built from c198a33f): code_evaluators 27/27, client_tool_grammar 19/19, sidecar_diagnostic_redaction 6/6, sidecar 55/55, sidecar_steering_diff 16/16, tsc clean. (First sidecar runs failed 9/55 and 4/16 only because the worktree had no Rust core - host environment, not a defect.)\\n\\nNot verified: a real Rust/cargo typecheck through the sandbox, other session.state test files (TUI e2e, approval_policy, provider_connect, upgrade), other Node versions, the full suite.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636183487,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:35:53Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:35:53Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent short review of <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a>..<a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> (reviewer agent, not the author; real bwrap sandbox + real tsc + real runCodeEvaluators in a detached worktree at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a>; focused tests only): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong> on one NEW finding. The symlink fix, the sidecar change and the grammar test are fine.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>NEW P1 - typecheck_clean regex reopens the vacuous pass.</strong> <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/05913af5b1da36d0486da98d1da2fad2ffc68638/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/05913af5b1da36d0486da98d1da2fad2ffc68638\\\"><tt>05913af</tt></a> changed <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:/i</code> to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror(?:\\\\s+TS\\\\d+|\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\])?:/i</code>; the code group is now optional, so the bare <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error:</code> matches with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/i</code> and Node's <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error: Cannot find module ...</code> counts as a recognised diagnostic.</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Case (real sandbox + real tsc)</th>\\n<th><a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a></th>\\n<th><a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a></th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(a) no node_modules on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail, infrastructureFailure true</td>\\n<td><strong>passed true, score 1</strong>, infrastructureFailure false</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(b) candidate syntax error, no node_modules</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td><strong>passed true, score 1</strong> (the candidate error is never evaluated)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(c) bwrap failure on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td>fail, infrastructureFailure true</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(d) Rust error[E0308] on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail (not recognised)</td>\\n<td>pass; a new error[E0425] fails with newDiagnostics (intended; unit-level only - cargo is not in the runner's /usr/bin,/bin)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(e) normal added TS error (node_modules present)</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td>fail (same)</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Any generic lowercase <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error: ...</code> line is now also \\\"recognised\\\" (e.g. cargo's <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error: could not find Cargo.toml</code>). Only candidates in a workspace with no installed <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">typescript</code> are affected. Suggested fix: drop the optional group and require a code, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:|\\\\berror\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\]:/</code> (keep <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">i</code> for TS only), and add a test with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error: Cannot find module</code> on both sides (no existing test covers it; the unavailable-checker test uses text without the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error:</code> prefix).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>1. runner.mjs symlink overlay: correct and safe.</strong> P1 reproduced and closed: baseline <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">src/main.ts</code> as a symlink to an outside file - at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a> the outside file became the candidate bytes, at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> it stays unchanged. No TOCTOU (fresh mkdtemp tree written only by this process); directory-symlink parents and hardlinks leave the outside file unchanged; overwritten (0755), deleted, nested-new-dir (0640) and new .rs overlays are correct and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fchmod</code> preserves modes; cleanup removes tempRoot and closes the fd in a finally. Reverting only the fix makes the new test fail - the test is real.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>3. sidecar.ts: safe.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace_name</code> is restored verbatim after redaction as <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace</code> already was (without it the name became <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">[REDACTED:HIGH_ENTROPY_STRING]</code>); it is only <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">path.basename(config.workspace)</code>, a substring of <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace</code>, so no new exposure; a fake <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ghp_</code> token in model/session/git.branch is still redacted; the new test fails if the restore line is removed. Existing nit (not new): a secret-shaped directory name still appears verbatim in both fields.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>4. client_tool_grammar new test: real</strong> (pins existing behaviour; a sticky vLLM cache in a scratch copy makes it fail).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>P3 nit:</strong> a dangling symlink at a path the candidate overlays now fails closed with EEXIST/pinnedWorkspaceError (build and typecheck score 0) because on Node v24.11.1 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fs.rmSync(dangling-link, {force:true})</code> does not remove it; the old code wrote through the link. Safe, but rejects a valid candidate.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Tests (isolated HOME, --test-concurrency=1, one file at a time, core built from <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a>): code_evaluators 27/27, client_tool_grammar 19/19, sidecar_diagnostic_redaction 6/6, sidecar 55/55, sidecar_steering_diff 16/16, tsc clean. (First sidecar runs failed 9/55 and 4/16 only because the worktree had no Rust core - host environment, not a defect.)</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: a real Rust/cargo typecheck through the sandbox, other session.state test files (TUI e2e, approval_policy, provider_connect, upgrade), other Node versions, the full suite.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636656187\",\"body\":\"Release handoff (2026-11-04): WP-1105 typecheck diagnostic fix is READY in local integration commit `2dbe565b3e5276d8226d50e7ac3a121962a64058`. Exact-commit focused evaluator suite: 29/29 PASS (log SHA-256 `405e3819bafc7f4ed221cadf096918bc8a251d9506c9e8a0bd53696877a6a7d8`); `npx tsc --noEmit`: PASS (log SHA-256 `f97c0f0b52dcae52444a1d6e462831513eb5ac35987d6f3df7efa043f4afc0db`); independent review_delta: APPROVED. Claims released; no full suite run, per owner instruction.\\n\\nThe older delta review was against `b032791e`. The cumulative integration branch now includes the null-argument, verified-matrix-candidate, vLLM identity, and rediscovery-retention changes, plus WP-1105 evaluator remediation. The new diagnostic-regex regression found after c198 is fixed by 2dbe565b. Please incorporate that commit into the release branch before the stable-head gate. Current PR/release branch remains `8520d9c8`; stable version bump, final artifact/installed qualification, GATEWAY provider matrix (still externally held), release PTY acceptance, and publication remain open. Nothing is pushed, tagged, or published by this handoff.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636656187,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:56:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:56:01Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Release handoff (2026-11-04): WP-1105 typecheck diagnostic fix is READY in local integration commit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">2dbe565b3e5276d8226d50e7ac3a121962a64058</code>. Exact-commit focused evaluator suite: 29/29 PASS (log SHA-256 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">405e3819bafc7f4ed221cadf096918bc8a251d9506c9e8a0bd53696877a6a7d8</code>); <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">npx tsc --noEmit</code>: PASS (log SHA-256 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">f97c0f0b52dcae52444a1d6e462831513eb5ac35987d6f3df7efa043f4afc0db</code>); independent review_delta: APPROVED. Claims released; no full suite run, per owner instruction.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The older delta review was against <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">b032791e</code>. The cumulative integration branch now includes the null-argument, verified-matrix-candidate, vLLM identity, and rediscovery-retention changes, plus WP-1105 evaluator remediation. The new diagnostic-regex regression found after c198 is fixed by 2dbe565b. Please incorporate that commit into the release branch before the stable-head gate. Current PR/release branch remains <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">8520d9c8</code>; stable version bump, final artifact/installed qualification, GATEWAY provider matrix (still externally held), release PTY acceptance, and publication remain open. Nothing is pushed, tagged, or published by this handoff.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6637728741\",\"body\":\"Gate note from read-only inspection: the local detached-gate script `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/ee800dc3-6bb6-4e55-89e6-d6c2e85af4b6/scratchpad/rg-final-run.sh` does not set `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` or `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT`. The exact-head test `the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem` therefore fails immediately at 4.4 ms on its required-fixture assertion (`cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:14-17`). Both `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `release.yml` set those variables after mounting the capped tmpfs/runtime fixture, so the local run is not equivalent for this test; this does not demonstrate a production filesystem regression. Keep the local `make test` result classified as non-green until the fixture is configured or CI evidence covers it. The owner-local log also stopped advancing at 17:39:59 while its process remained alive at my 17:42 check; no process was stopped.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6637728741,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T17:44:41Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T17:44:41Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Gate note from read-only inspection: the local detached-gate script <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/ee800dc3-6bb6-4e55-89e6-d6c2e85af4b6/scratchpad/rg-final-run.sh</code> does not set <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT</code> or <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT</code>. The exact-head test <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem</code> therefore fails immediately at 4.4 ms on its required-fixture assertion (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:14-17</code>). Both <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">release.yml</code> set those variables after mounting the capped tmpfs/runtime fixture, so the local run is not equivalent for this test; this does not demonstrate a production filesystem regression. Keep the local <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">make test</code> result classified as non-green until the fixture is configured or CI evidence covers it. The owner-local log also stopped advancing at 17:39:59 while its process remained alive at my 17:42 check; no process was stopped.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6638774667\",\"body\":\"Independent review of the release documents and version bump (`bd7fb1cf..40d553b5`; reviewer agent, not the author; read-only, no test runs): **REQUEST CHANGES**, applied in `fafbf6d5` (documentation only; `git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'` is empty; `security_gates.sh` passes on it).\\n\\nVerified correct: every number and log hash in the final-gate section (cargo 43+254+1+4+1, 2,377 tests / 237 suites / 2,371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped, the five skip reasons, five SHA-256 values, the make-test abort before the scope-procs and security steps); `git diff --stat c198a33f 2dbe565b` = typecheck_clean.mjs, code_evaluators.test.ts, docs and one evidence JSON; the coded-diagnostic regex at `bd7fb1cf`; check runs on `bd7fb1cf`; the version bump (six files, `harness-core` 1.1.2 in Cargo.lock, both package-lock entries, no `1.1.2-rc.2` outside docs); no `v1.1.2*` tag on origin; #398/#396/#401 merged and ancestors; `--step`, `/step` and `toolCallSyntax` exist; links and anchors resolve; no wording claims an independent ACCEPT or a published release.\\n\\nCorrections found and applied:\\n1. **HIGH - WP-1107 was overclaimed.** `adaptToolDefinitionsForServer` returns tools unchanged unless the server kind is vLLM, and the tests assert llama.cpp and Ollama keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint). The roadmap's llama.cpp `grammar`, vLLM `guided_json`, Ollama `format` and hybrid reasoning grammars are not implemented. The notes, the qualification WP-1107 and G1.1-4 rows now say: bounded schema compiler plus strict function schemas on the vLLM path only, reduced scope.\\n2. **MEDIUM - `CHANGELOG.md`** described v1.1.2 as the 2026-11-01 multi-message patch; now \\\"Unreleased\\\", with the real scope.\\n3. **MEDIUM - limitations stated too weakly or missing**: candidate build-config edits silently ignored; the fail-open overlay rated HIGH; command-path escape comes from trusted configuration; `node --check` wording; pinned workspace under the system temp dir; candidate symlink with a source extension; `spec.candidate.cwd` overridden; `--pretty` output; text-mode tool calls not counted by `toolCallSyntax`; the server-kind cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint; the nullable-property claim measured on a synthetic tool only.\\n4. **Review table**: added the first WP-1105 review row (`5fde750a`, three MEDIUM findings), restored the \\\"borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS\\\" qualifier, corrected the `7f915894..b032791e` outcome (the task-class header leak was closed; kind loss on an unreadable model list was not).\\n5. \\\"No separate review\\\" sentence corrected (an earlier draft of these documents was reviewed and changes were requested).\\n6. G1.1-5: \\\"the CodeQL check passed (alert count not queried)\\\"; CodeRabbit listed as skipped; \\\"my wrapper\\\" -> \\\"the gate wrapper\\\"; \\\"make exit 2 (recipe exit 1)\\\".\\n\\nCould not verify (per the reviewer): the WP-1102 22/22, WP-1106 8/8 and slash_router 34/34 counts and the rc.1/rc.2 archive/SBOM hashes (taken from codex-root's earlier record, labelled historical); that no other process ran on the host during the gate; zero CodeQL alerts; the 141-component SBOM and the WP-1108 \\\"27 Dependabot PRs\\\" claim. Note from the reviewer for the owner: the 2026-11-03 20:42 UTC decision said \\\"tag after independent ACCEPT + exact-head green CI\\\"; the 2026-11-04 15:06 UTC waiver covers the open findings, and the owner may want to confirm that the Entire approval on the final head also stands in for the independent ACCEPT.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6638774667,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T18:31:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T18:31:43Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of the release documents and version bump (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf..40d553b5</code>; reviewer agent, not the author; read-only, no test runs): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>, applied in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fafbf6d5</code> (documentation only; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'</code> is empty; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">security_gates.sh</code> passes on it).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Verified correct: every number and log hash in the final-gate section (cargo 43+254+1+4+1, 2,377 tests / 237 suites / 2,371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped, the five skip reasons, five SHA-256 values, the make-test abort before the scope-procs and security steps); <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --stat c198a33f 2dbe565b</code> = typecheck_clean.mjs, code_evaluators.test.ts, docs and one evidence JSON; the coded-diagnostic regex at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf</code>; check runs on <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf</code>; the version bump (six files, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">harness-core</code> 1.1.2 in Cargo.lock, both package-lock entries, no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">1.1.2-rc.2</code> outside docs); no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">v1.1.2*</code> tag on origin; <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6151699555\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/398\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398\\\">#398</a>/<a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6150439871\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/396\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pul