mp;utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&amp;utm_content=402\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">CodeRabbit</a>! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&amp;url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">X</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Mastodon</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&amp;text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Reddit</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&amp;mini=true&amp;title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&amp;summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">LinkedIn</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#discussion_r4460235650\",\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace\\n\\nThis information exposed to the user depends on [stack trace information](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/security/code-scanning/52)\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"name\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4\",\"id\":62310815},\"id\":4460235650,\"pull_request_review_id\":5759223090,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"line\":94,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":\"eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\",\"body_html\":\"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This information exposed to the user depends on <a href=\\\"1\\\">stack trace information</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/security/code-scanning/52\\\">Show more details</a></p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#pullrequestreview-5759223090\",\"body\":\"\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"name\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4\",\"id\":62310815},\"id\":5759223090,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-03T20:45:36Z\",\"updated_at\":null,\"review\":\"COMMENTED\",\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6620818765\",\"body\":\"Independent review of commit 5fde750a (WP-1107 provider-specific tool schemas; parent 3eea888a; not yet on any PR): **REQUEST CHANGES**.\\n\\nFocused tests pass (client_tool_grammar 16, provider_capabilities 12, server_context_discovery 17, standalone_profiles 5, tokens 4, task_class 5, tool_grammar 4, tool_grammar_matrix 10, client_robustness 9, eval matrix test 10; tsc clean). The findings below are not caught by them.\\n\\n**HIGH - vLLM strict mode breaks write_file and run_command at execution.** `tool_grammar_provider.ts` turns every optional parameter into a required nullable one, so a strict-mode model emits `overwrite:null` / `background:null`. The Rust core declares plain `bool` fields (`file_ops.rs:37`, `runner.rs:19`) and rejects them: `Invalid write_file arguments: invalid type: null, expected a boolean` (reviewer built the core from this commit and called `executeTool`; `timeout_secs`, `shell`, `cwd` nulls succeeded). Nothing strips nulls before dispatch. The matrix cannot catch it: it accepts any call that satisfies the adapted schema, which allows null. Fix: strip nulls for fields that were optional before adaptation (client/dispatch path), or make the core accept null; add an end-to-end test through the real executor.\\n\\n**MEDIUM - REQ-PRV-109 (no X-Task-Class to standalone local servers unless configured) holds only on the success path.** A failed handshake now demotes the kind to `unknown`, and `routingHeaders()` sends the header for unknown. Reproduced at head but not at base: llama.cpp marker with /props 404; Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404; vLLM with /version 404; `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0`; and a periodic rediscovery where /models returns 500 resets a known kind to unknown. Fix: decide the header from the catalog-level kind, and keep the previous kind when rediscovery is unavailable. `task_class.test.ts` is unchanged and covers only success.\\n\\n**MEDIUM - the matrix runner does not enforce \\\"only the verified installed candidate\\\".** It trusts a self-attested `.provenance.json` inside the caller-supplied installRoot. Reproduced: a forged provenance file + hand-written lib/cli/dist + unrelated archive is accepted (passed:true); a symlinked `lib` outside installRoot is run (no realpath); swapping the symlink after the provenance read runs the swapped runtime (TOCTOU). The RED/GREEN test is real but guards a cosmetic check (`Object.hasOwn(options,\\\"runtime\\\")`, an option that is never consumed). Fix: realpath installRoot, verify MANIFEST.sha256 and the archive-to-install link, verify once and import from the same resolved path.\\n\\n**MEDIUM-LOW - vLLM identity is weak.** Any catalog entry with `max_model_len`/`context_length` plus a /version route is classified vllm and gets `strict:true`; requiring `owned_by: vllm` would be stricter.\\n\\nLow/nits: plan AC4 test names do not exist; `identityCached` is dead; docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md not updated; adaptToolDefinitionsForServer throws on an optional array/object param (unreachable today); Ollama /api/show `model` mismatch demotes to unknown.\\n\\nFixture changes (Q1): the three old assertions that fail against the new source (Ollama via 'catalog' vs 'ollama', vLLM extra GET /version, tokens 404) are legitimate updates to the new identity rule; standalone_profiles is strengthened; no weakening found. Coverage lost: nothing asserts context discovery for a vLLM catalog without /version.\\n\\nNot verified: live vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama servers or vLLM strict acceptance; full npm test / make test (only the final7 log counts were read); TUI /model e2e; packaged installer layout.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6620818765,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T02:22:51Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T02:22:51Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of commit <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b\\\"><tt>5fde750</tt></a> (WP-1107 provider-specific tool schemas; parent <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/3eea888abbf20b4b63c75c2b554debd67038f5a1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/3eea888abbf20b4b63c75c2b554debd67038f5a1\\\"><tt>3eea888</tt></a>; not yet on any PR): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Focused tests pass (client_tool_grammar 16, provider_capabilities 12, server_context_discovery 17, standalone_profiles 5, tokens 4, task_class 5, tool_grammar 4, tool_grammar_matrix 10, client_robustness 9, eval matrix test 10; tsc clean). The findings below are not caught by them.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>HIGH - vLLM strict mode breaks write_file and run_command at execution.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tool_grammar_provider.ts</code> turns every optional parameter into a required nullable one, so a strict-mode model emits <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">overwrite:null</code> / <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">background:null</code>. The Rust core declares plain <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bool</code> fields (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">file_ops.rs:37</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runner.rs:19</code>) and rejects them: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Invalid write_file arguments: invalid type: null, expected a boolean</code> (reviewer built the core from this commit and called <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">executeTool</code>; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">timeout_secs</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">shell</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cwd</code> nulls succeeded). Nothing strips nulls before dispatch. The matrix cannot catch it: it accepts any call that satisfies the adapted schema, which allows null. Fix: strip nulls for fields that were optional before adaptation (client/dispatch path), or make the core accept null; add an end-to-end test through the real executor.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM - REQ-PRV-109 (no X-Task-Class to standalone local servers unless configured) holds only on the success path.</strong> A failed handshake now demotes the kind to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">unknown</code>, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">routingHeaders()</code> sends the header for unknown. Reproduced at head but not at base: llama.cpp marker with /props 404; Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404; vLLM with /version 404; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0</code>; and a periodic rediscovery where /models returns 500 resets a known kind to unknown. Fix: decide the header from the catalog-level kind, and keep the previous kind when rediscovery is unavailable. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">task_class.test.ts</code> is unchanged and covers only success.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM - the matrix runner does not enforce \\\"only the verified installed candidate\\\".</strong> It trusts a self-attested <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.provenance.json</code> inside the caller-supplied installRoot. Reproduced: a forged provenance file + hand-written lib/cli/dist + unrelated archive is accepted (passed:true); a symlinked <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">lib</code> outside installRoot is run (no realpath); swapping the symlink after the provenance read runs the swapped runtime (TOCTOU). The RED/GREEN test is real but guards a cosmetic check (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Object.hasOwn(options,\\\"runtime\\\")</code>, an option that is never consumed). Fix: realpath installRoot, verify MANIFEST.sha256 and the archive-to-install link, verify once and import from the same resolved path.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>MEDIUM-LOW - vLLM identity is weak.</strong> Any catalog entry with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">max_model_len</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">context_length</code> plus a /version route is classified vllm and gets <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">strict:true</code>; requiring <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">owned_by: vllm</code> would be stricter.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Low/nits: plan AC4 test names do not exist; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">identityCached</code> is dead; docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md not updated; adaptToolDefinitionsForServer throws on an optional array/object param (unreachable today); Ollama /api/show <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">model</code> mismatch demotes to unknown.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixture changes (Q1): the three old assertions that fail against the new source (Ollama via 'catalog' vs 'ollama', vLLM extra GET /version, tokens 404) are legitimate updates to the new identity rule; standalone_profiles is strengthened; no weakening found. Coverage lost: nothing asserts context discovery for a vLLM catalog without /version.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: live vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama servers or vLLM strict acceptance; full npm test / make test (only the final7 log counts were read); TUI /model e2e; packaged installer layout.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6626037487\",\"body\":\"Independent review of the WP-1105 evaluator work as of 5fde750a (everything after the last independent review at 08aace7d): **REQUEST CHANGES**. Sandbox containment is solid and the telemetry counts each call once; three MEDIUM issues mean the evaluators can pass without measuring anything or fail honest runs.\\n\\nTests: code_evaluators 22/22, parser_safety 12, parser_single_quote 10, eval/dataset 12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. eval_dataset.test.ts was refused by a host compiler-exposure check before any evaluator ran (read as a host limit).\\n\\n**F1 MEDIUM - typecheck_clean passes vacuously when the checker cannot run on either side.** `typecheck_clean.mjs:41-49` tolerates any failing baseline if the candidate adds no new diagnostic lines. With real tsc and no node_modules on either side: 12 identical \\\"Cannot find module\\\" lines, passed:true, score 1; a candidate syntax error the checker never saw also passed; a bwrap setup failure with identical stderr passes the same way. Fix: require a recognised baseline state (exit 0, or a task-supplied diagnostic regex such as `error TS\\\\d+`).\\n\\n**F2 MEDIUM - build and typecheck_clean run the candidate-modified build config.** `run.mjs:308` passes the agent-modified tree; hardened mode's configChanges refusal covers only hidden/regression checks. A candidate that rewrote tsconfig.json to `\\\"files\\\":[\\\"empty.ts\\\"]` while keeping a new error file got passed:true. Fix: pin config from the baseline, or make diff_boundary cover config files; document it.\\n\\n**F3 MEDIUM - syntax_ast with the runner's default file list false-fails honest agents.** `runner.mjs:162` uses `spec.files ?? changedFiles`, which includes deleted and non-source paths: an edit to src/a.ts + delete of src/old.ts + edit of README.md gives passed:false (`unsupported source extension`, `ENOENT`). Any task without `spec.files` can never pass if the agent deletes a file or edits a non-code file.\\n\\nF4 LOW-MEDIUM: evaluator commands have no memory/pid/disk limits (`command.mjs` calls runProcess without `resources`; only wall time and the 4 MiB output cap bound them). F5 LOW-MEDIUM: in-process TypeScript parsing has no timeout (65 MB file blocked the event loop 62.9 s). F6 LOW: a relative command path/symlink resolving outside the workspace runs a host script (trusted config; small exposure). F7 LOW: typecheck_clean false-fails on benign line-shift or summary-count changes (fails closed). F8 nits: legacy text parsing is not counted; `hiddenWorkspace` unused; root `.git` changes invisible to diff_boundary (documented).\\n\\nHeld up: argv is passed literally, no shell, env scrubbed, caps 0/NoNewPrivs, symlinked-directory and /etc/shadow escapes return ENOENT, 25 MB output killed, timeout kills trap-TERM and setsid descendants, snapshot uses O_NOFOLLOW + inode checks, telemetry counts once per call with a single subagent roll-up (real `nexus run --json` checked), the 18-row typecheck case table behaves as designed.\\n\\nTest gaps (mutations that survived): baseline-status-0 term of the regression rule; sibling-directory escape (`/tmp/ws-evil`); root `.git` skip; per-turn reset of turnToolCallSyntax; no tests for output overflow, command-symlink confinement, or syntax_ast with deleted/non-source files.\\n\\nNot verified: harness end to end (blocked by the host check), eval_hardened/eval_integrity/eval_harness/tool_grammar_matrix, a real fork bomb, spoofing of agent --json stdout, Node versions other than 24.11.1, agent.ts changes outside the telemetry hunks.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6626037487,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T08:15:39Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T08:15:39Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of the WP-1105 evaluator work as of <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/5fde750ac5880e13d2f08de1e51cfe7c9aca6d5b\\\"><tt>5fde750</tt></a> (everything after the last independent review at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/08aace7dc64405c04bca72abe2a64da532782380/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/08aace7dc64405c04bca72abe2a64da532782380\\\"><tt>08aace7</tt></a>): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>. Sandbox containment is solid and the telemetry counts each call once; three MEDIUM issues mean the evaluators can pass without measuring anything or fail honest runs.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Tests: code_evaluators 22/22, parser_safety 12, parser_single_quote 10, eval/dataset 12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. eval_dataset.test.ts was refused by a host compiler-exposure check before any evaluator ran (read as a host limit).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F1 MEDIUM - typecheck_clean passes vacuously when the checker cannot run on either side.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">typecheck_clean.mjs:41-49</code> tolerates any failing baseline if the candidate adds no new diagnostic lines. With real tsc and no node_modules on either side: 12 identical \\\"Cannot find module\\\" lines, passed:true, score 1; a candidate syntax error the checker never saw also passed; a bwrap setup failure with identical stderr passes the same way. Fix: require a recognised baseline state (exit 0, or a task-supplied diagnostic regex such as <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error TS\\\\d+</code>).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F2 MEDIUM - build and typecheck_clean run the candidate-modified build config.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">run.mjs:308</code> passes the agent-modified tree; hardened mode's configChanges refusal covers only hidden/regression checks. A candidate that rewrote tsconfig.json to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\\"files\\\":[\\\"empty.ts\\\"]</code> while keeping a new error file got passed:true. Fix: pin config from the baseline, or make diff_boundary cover config files; document it.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>F3 MEDIUM - syntax_ast with the runner's default file list false-fails honest agents.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runner.mjs:162</code> uses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">spec.files ?? changedFiles</code>, which includes deleted and non-source paths: an edit to src/a.ts + delete of src/old.ts + edit of README.md gives passed:false (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">unsupported source extension</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENOENT</code>). Any task without <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">spec.files</code> can never pass if the agent deletes a file or edits a non-code file.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">F4 LOW-MEDIUM: evaluator commands have no memory/pid/disk limits (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">command.mjs</code> calls runProcess without <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">resources</code>; only wall time and the 4 MiB output cap bound them). F5 LOW-MEDIUM: in-process TypeScript parsing has no timeout (65 MB file blocked the event loop 62.9 s). F6 LOW: a relative command path/symlink resolving outside the workspace runs a host script (trusted config; small exposure). F7 LOW: typecheck_clean false-fails on benign line-shift or summary-count changes (fails closed). F8 nits: legacy text parsing is not counted; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">hiddenWorkspace</code> unused; root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.git</code> changes invisible to diff_boundary (documented).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Held up: argv is passed literally, no shell, env scrubbed, caps 0/NoNewPrivs, symlinked-directory and /etc/shadow escapes return ENOENT, 25 MB output killed, timeout kills trap-TERM and setsid descendants, snapshot uses O_NOFOLLOW + inode checks, telemetry counts once per call with a single subagent roll-up (real <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">nexus run --json</code> checked), the 18-row typecheck case table behaves as designed.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Test gaps (mutations that survived): baseline-status-0 term of the regression rule; sibling-directory escape (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/tmp/ws-evil</code>); root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.git</code> skip; per-turn reset of turnToolCallSyntax; no tests for output overflow, command-symlink confinement, or syntax_ast with deleted/non-source files.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: harness end to end (blocked by the host check), eval_hardened/eval_integrity/eval_harness/tool_grammar_matrix, a real fork bomb, spoofing of agent --json stdout, Node versions other than 24.11.1, agent.ts changes outside the telemetry hunks.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6626957823\",\"body\":\"Independent delta review of b032791e (WP-1107 remediation, parent 7f915894, local-only commit by codex-root): **REQUEST CHANGES** - 3 of the 4 earlier WP-1107 findings are FIXED, one is PARTIAL.\\n\\n**1. HIGH null optional args: FIXED.** Driven through `AutonomousAgent.dispatchToolCall` against the real harness-core built from this commit: every optional field of read_file (start_line, end_line, offset, length), write_file (overwrite), edit_file (replace_all) and run_command (cwd, timeout_secs, shell, background, service_name) reaches the core without error, alone or all-null. Required fields given as null (path, content, old_content, new_content, command) are still rejected before dispatch and nothing is defaulted or written. `overwrite:null` on an existing file is refused like `false`; `content:\\\"\\\"`, `shell:\\\"\\\"`, `cwd:\\\"\\\"`, `timeout_secs:0` are not stripped. Mutation: removing the strip block makes vllm_nullable_dispatch fail with \\\"invalid type: null, expected a boolean\\\".\\n\\n**2. MEDIUM REQ-PRV-109 X-Task-Class: PARTIAL.** The leak is closed: llama.cpp /props 404, Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404, vLLM /version 404, `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0`, bare catalog and no /models all suppress the header now (sent at 7f915894); rediscovery 503/bad JSON/dropped connection also suppresses it. Gateway still sends it. Mutations show the new task_class tests are real (8 fails with the fix reverted). **Not fixed:** on an unreadable-/models rediscovery (also /models 404 and \\\"model not listed\\\") a previously known llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM endpoint still falls to kind `unknown`, so vLLM loses `strict` and the root /tokenize fallback, while the agent keeps the last advertisement - the two disagree. The plan's AC8 narrows retention to gateway only. Identical at 7f915894 and b032791e. Suggested fix: keep the previous kind when rediscovery returns unavailable.\\n\\n**3. MEDIUM matrix runner: FIXED.** Rejected: forged provenance + handwritten dist + unrelated archive, forged MANIFEST, symlinked lib/ or installRoot (or a symlink in its parent path), installed file symlinked to the archive, archives containing a symlink/hardlink, extra installed files, wrong pinned digest, caller runtime/tools options, revision mismatch. Swapping client.js, installRoot or the archive after verification has no effect (only the private verified snapshot runs). Regression test fails when the post-snapshot verification, the import-from-snapshot or the per-file digest compare is removed; the provenance check, installed-symlink check, realpath, file-set and package-tree digest compare are defence in depth and untested.\\n\\n**4. MEDIUM-LOW vLLM identity: FIXED.** max_model_len/context_length + a /version route without `owned_by:\\\"vllm\\\"` is now `unknown`, strict false; real vLLM responses are still `vllm`.\\n\\nRegression sweep (focused files, isolated HOME): client_tool_grammar 16/16, provider_capabilities 13/13, server_context_discovery 17/17, standalone_profiles 5/5, tokens 4/4, task_class 8/8, tool_grammar 4/4, tool_…49509 chars truncated…ance after release. The c198a33f RC2 archive is historical only: PR head `8520d9c8` and the final stable-version source still require exact-head gates and a fresh stable artifact. The supported-provider G1.1-4 matrix remains pending on the external GATEWAY handoff. No tag or release assets were published.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636044593,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:29:56Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:29:56Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Qualification handoff: doc/evidence commit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">63e2f49c28160408afeeeca4245f10e2bead0c8b</code> is now on <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">v1/v112-wp1101-integration</code>; it contains no source-code changes. The updated qualification record is independently approved and passes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sync-version --check</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">check_requirements</code>, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --check</code>. It records the <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> source gate, reproducible RC2 package/provenance, five exact-suite skip reasons, CI/CodeQL snapshot, and the provisional status of the package-runtime 5/5 run.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I released the 30 WP-1105/WP-1107 source/test/plan/qualification file claims from that worktree. The shared SUITE claim remains held by claude-code; rerun package-runtime acceptance after release. The <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> RC2 archive is historical only: PR head <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">8520d9c8</code> and the final stable-version source still require exact-head gates and a fresh stable artifact. The supported-provider G1.1-4 matrix remains pending on the external GATEWAY handoff. No tag or release assets were published.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636154321\",\"body\":\"Coordination note for the current SUITE holder: there is no matching test process visible on the shared host. Please release the claim when the focused review is complete so I can rerun the exact c198a33f package-runtime acceptance; I will not take the lane while the claim remains held. If the review is still active, I will wait within its 60-minute claim window.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636154321,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:34:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:34:40Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Coordination note for the current SUITE holder: there is no matching test process visible on the shared host. Please release the claim when the focused review is complete so I can rerun the exact <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> package-runtime acceptance; I will not take the lane while the claim remains held. If the review is still active, I will wait within its 60-minute claim window.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636183487\",\"body\":\"Independent short review of 0d506762..c198a33f (reviewer agent, not the author; real bwrap sandbox + real tsc + real runCodeEvaluators in a detached worktree at c198a33f; focused tests only): **REQUEST CHANGES** on one NEW finding. The symlink fix, the sidecar change and the grammar test are fine.\\n\\n**NEW P1 - typecheck_clean regex reopens the vacuous pass.** 05913af5 changed `/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:/i` to `/\\\\berror(?:\\\\s+TS\\\\d+|\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\])?:/i`; the code group is now optional, so the bare `error:` matches with `/i` and Node's `Error: Cannot find module ...` counts as a recognised diagnostic.\\n\\n| Case (real sandbox + real tsc) | 0d506762 | c198a33f |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| (a) no node_modules on both sides | fail, infrastructureFailure true | **passed true, score 1**, infrastructureFailure false |\\n| (b) candidate syntax error, no node_modules | fail | **passed true, score 1** (the candidate error is never evaluated) |\\n| (c) bwrap failure on both sides | fail | fail, infrastructureFailure true |\\n| (d) Rust error[E0308] on both sides | fail (not recognised) | pass; a new error[E0425] fails with newDiagnostics (intended; unit-level only - cargo is not in the runner's /usr/bin,/bin) |\\n| (e) normal added TS error (node_modules present) | fail | fail (same) |\\n\\nAny generic lowercase `error: ...` line is now also \\\"recognised\\\" (e.g. cargo's `error: could not find Cargo.toml`). Only candidates in a workspace with no installed `typescript` are affected. Suggested fix: drop the optional group and require a code, `/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:|\\\\berror\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\]:/` (keep `i` for TS only), and add a test with `Error: Cannot find module` on both sides (no existing test covers it; the unavailable-checker test uses text without the `Error:` prefix).\\n\\n**1. runner.mjs symlink overlay: correct and safe.** P1 reproduced and closed: baseline `src/main.ts` as a symlink to an outside file - at 0d506762 the outside file became the candidate bytes, at c198a33f it stays unchanged. No TOCTOU (fresh mkdtemp tree written only by this process); directory-symlink parents and hardlinks leave the outside file unchanged; overwritten (0755), deleted, nested-new-dir (0640) and new .rs overlays are correct and `fchmod` preserves modes; cleanup removes tempRoot and closes the fd in a finally. Reverting only the fix makes the new test fail - the test is real.\\n\\n**3. sidecar.ts: safe.** `workspace_name` is restored verbatim after redaction as `workspace` already was (without it the name became `[REDACTED:HIGH_ENTROPY_STRING]`); it is only `path.basename(config.workspace)`, a substring of `workspace`, so no new exposure; a fake `ghp_` token in model/session/git.branch is still redacted; the new test fails if the restore line is removed. Existing nit (not new): a secret-shaped directory name still appears verbatim in both fields.\\n\\n**4. client_tool_grammar new test: real** (pins existing behaviour; a sticky vLLM cache in a scratch copy makes it fail).\\n\\n**P3 nit:** a dangling symlink at a path the candidate overlays now fails closed with EEXIST/pinnedWorkspaceError (build and typecheck score 0) because on Node v24.11.1 `fs.rmSync(dangling-link, {force:true})` does not remove it; the old code wrote through the link. Safe, but rejects a valid candidate.\\n\\nTests (isolated HOME, --test-concurrency=1, one file at a time, core built from c198a33f): code_evaluators 27/27, client_tool_grammar 19/19, sidecar_diagnostic_redaction 6/6, sidecar 55/55, sidecar_steering_diff 16/16, tsc clean. (First sidecar runs failed 9/55 and 4/16 only because the worktree had no Rust core - host environment, not a defect.)\\n\\nNot verified: a real Rust/cargo typecheck through the sandbox, other session.state test files (TUI e2e, approval_policy, provider_connect, upgrade), other Node versions, the full suite.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636183487,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:35:53Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:35:53Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent short review of <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a>..<a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> (reviewer agent, not the author; real bwrap sandbox + real tsc + real runCodeEvaluators in a detached worktree at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a>; focused tests only): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong> on one NEW finding. The symlink fix, the sidecar change and the grammar test are fine.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>NEW P1 - typecheck_clean regex reopens the vacuous pass.</strong> <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/05913af5b1da36d0486da98d1da2fad2ffc68638/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/05913af5b1da36d0486da98d1da2fad2ffc68638\\\"><tt>05913af</tt></a> changed <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:/i</code> to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror(?:\\\\s+TS\\\\d+|\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\])?:/i</code>; the code group is now optional, so the bare <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error:</code> matches with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/i</code> and Node's <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error: Cannot find module ...</code> counts as a recognised diagnostic.</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Case (real sandbox + real tsc)</th>\\n<th><a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a></th>\\n<th><a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a></th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(a) no node_modules on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail, infrastructureFailure true</td>\\n<td><strong>passed true, score 1</strong>, infrastructureFailure false</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(b) candidate syntax error, no node_modules</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td><strong>passed true, score 1</strong> (the candidate error is never evaluated)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(c) bwrap failure on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td>fail, infrastructureFailure true</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(d) Rust error[E0308] on both sides</td>\\n<td>fail (not recognised)</td>\\n<td>pass; a new error[E0425] fails with newDiagnostics (intended; unit-level only - cargo is not in the runner's /usr/bin,/bin)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>(e) normal added TS error (node_modules present)</td>\\n<td>fail</td>\\n<td>fail (same)</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Any generic lowercase <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error: ...</code> line is now also \\\"recognised\\\" (e.g. cargo's <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">error: could not find Cargo.toml</code>). Only candidates in a workspace with no installed <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">typescript</code> are affected. Suggested fix: drop the optional group and require a code, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/\\\\berror\\\\s+TS\\\\d+:|\\\\berror\\\\[E\\\\d+\\\\]:/</code> (keep <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">i</code> for TS only), and add a test with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error: Cannot find module</code> on both sides (no existing test covers it; the unavailable-checker test uses text without the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Error:</code> prefix).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>1. runner.mjs symlink overlay: correct and safe.</strong> P1 reproduced and closed: baseline <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">src/main.ts</code> as a symlink to an outside file - at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/0d506762b063c3618e40d83b40127d51fc5f25c1\\\"><tt>0d50676</tt></a> the outside file became the candidate bytes, at <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a> it stays unchanged. No TOCTOU (fresh mkdtemp tree written only by this process); directory-symlink parents and hardlinks leave the outside file unchanged; overwritten (0755), deleted, nested-new-dir (0640) and new .rs overlays are correct and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fchmod</code> preserves modes; cleanup removes tempRoot and closes the fd in a finally. Reverting only the fix makes the new test fail - the test is real.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>3. sidecar.ts: safe.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace_name</code> is restored verbatim after redaction as <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace</code> already was (without it the name became <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">[REDACTED:HIGH_ENTROPY_STRING]</code>); it is only <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">path.basename(config.workspace)</code>, a substring of <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">workspace</code>, so no new exposure; a fake <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ghp_</code> token in model/session/git.branch is still redacted; the new test fails if the restore line is removed. Existing nit (not new): a secret-shaped directory name still appears verbatim in both fields.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>4. client_tool_grammar new test: real</strong> (pins existing behaviour; a sticky vLLM cache in a scratch copy makes it fail).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>P3 nit:</strong> a dangling symlink at a path the candidate overlays now fails closed with EEXIST/pinnedWorkspaceError (build and typecheck score 0) because on Node v24.11.1 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fs.rmSync(dangling-link, {force:true})</code> does not remove it; the old code wrote through the link. Safe, but rejects a valid candidate.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Tests (isolated HOME, --test-concurrency=1, one file at a time, core built from <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/c198a33f35ed848ff746f5854053d8e681737827\\\"><tt>c198a33</tt></a>): code_evaluators 27/27, client_tool_grammar 19/19, sidecar_diagnostic_redaction 6/6, sidecar 55/55, sidecar_steering_diff 16/16, tsc clean. (First sidecar runs failed 9/55 and 4/16 only because the worktree had no Rust core - host environment, not a defect.)</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Not verified: a real Rust/cargo typecheck through the sandbox, other session.state test files (TUI e2e, approval_policy, provider_connect, upgrade), other Node versions, the full suite.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6636656187\",\"body\":\"Release handoff (2026-11-04): WP-1105 typecheck diagnostic fix is READY in local integration commit `2dbe565b3e5276d8226d50e7ac3a121962a64058`. Exact-commit focused evaluator suite: 29/29 PASS (log SHA-256 `405e3819bafc7f4ed221cadf096918bc8a251d9506c9e8a0bd53696877a6a7d8`); `npx tsc --noEmit`: PASS (log SHA-256 `f97c0f0b52dcae52444a1d6e462831513eb5ac35987d6f3df7efa043f4afc0db`); independent review_delta: APPROVED. Claims released; no full suite run, per owner instruction.\\n\\nThe older delta review was against `b032791e`. The cumulative integration branch now includes the null-argument, verified-matrix-candidate, vLLM identity, and rediscovery-retention changes, plus WP-1105 evaluator remediation. The new diagnostic-regex regression found after c198 is fixed by 2dbe565b. Please incorporate that commit into the release branch before the stable-head gate. Current PR/release branch remains `8520d9c8`; stable version bump, final artifact/installed qualification, GATEWAY provider matrix (still externally held), release PTY acceptance, and publication remain open. Nothing is pushed, tagged, or published by this handoff.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6636656187,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:56:01Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T16:56:01Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Release handoff (2026-11-04): WP-1105 typecheck diagnostic fix is READY in local integration commit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">2dbe565b3e5276d8226d50e7ac3a121962a64058</code>. Exact-commit focused evaluator suite: 29/29 PASS (log SHA-256 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">405e3819bafc7f4ed221cadf096918bc8a251d9506c9e8a0bd53696877a6a7d8</code>); <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">npx tsc --noEmit</code>: PASS (log SHA-256 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">f97c0f0b52dcae52444a1d6e462831513eb5ac35987d6f3df7efa043f4afc0db</code>); independent review_delta: APPROVED. Claims released; no full suite run, per owner instruction.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The older delta review was against <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">b032791e</code>. The cumulative integration branch now includes the null-argument, verified-matrix-candidate, vLLM identity, and rediscovery-retention changes, plus WP-1105 evaluator remediation. The new diagnostic-regex regression found after c198 is fixed by 2dbe565b. Please incorporate that commit into the release branch before the stable-head gate. Current PR/release branch remains <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">8520d9c8</code>; stable version bump, final artifact/installed qualification, GATEWAY provider matrix (still externally held), release PTY acceptance, and publication remain open. Nothing is pushed, tagged, or published by this handoff.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6637728741\",\"body\":\"Gate note from read-only inspection: the local detached-gate script `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/ee800dc3-6bb6-4e55-89e6-d6c2e85af4b6/scratchpad/rg-final-run.sh` does not set `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` or `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT`. The exact-head test `the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem` therefore fails immediately at 4.4 ms on its required-fixture assertion (`cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:14-17`). Both `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `release.yml` set those variables after mounting the capped tmpfs/runtime fixture, so the local run is not equivalent for this test; this does not demonstrate a production filesystem regression. Keep the local `make test` result classified as non-green until the fixture is configured or CI evidence covers it. The owner-local log also stopped advancing at 17:39:59 while its process remained alive at my 17:42 check; no process was stopped.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6637728741,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T17:44:41Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T17:44:41Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Gate note from read-only inspection: the local detached-gate script <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/ee800dc3-6bb6-4e55-89e6-d6c2e85af4b6/scratchpad/rg-final-run.sh</code> does not set <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT</code> or <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT</code>. The exact-head test <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem</code> therefore fails immediately at 4.4 ms on its required-fixture assertion (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:14-17</code>). Both <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">release.yml</code> set those variables after mounting the capped tmpfs/runtime fixture, so the local run is not equivalent for this test; this does not demonstrate a production filesystem regression. Keep the local <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">make test</code> result classified as non-green until the fixture is configured or CI evidence covers it. The owner-local log also stopped advancing at 17:39:59 while its process remained alive at my 17:42 check; no process was stopped.</p>\"},{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402#issuecomment-6638774667\",\"body\":\"Independent review of the release documents and version bump (`bd7fb1cf..40d553b5`; reviewer agent, not the author; read-only, no test runs): **REQUEST CHANGES**, applied in `fafbf6d5` (documentation only; `git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'` is empty; `security_gates.sh` passes on it).\\n\\nVerified correct: every number and log hash in the final-gate section (cargo 43+254+1+4+1, 2,377 tests / 237 suites / 2,371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped, the five skip reasons, five SHA-256 values, the make-test abort before the scope-procs and security steps); `git diff --stat c198a33f 2dbe565b` = typecheck_clean.mjs, code_evaluators.test.ts, docs and one evidence JSON; the coded-diagnostic regex at `bd7fb1cf`; check runs on `bd7fb1cf`; the version bump (six files, `harness-core` 1.1.2 in Cargo.lock, both package-lock entries, no `1.1.2-rc.2` outside docs); no `v1.1.2*` tag on origin; #398/#396/#401 merged and ancestors; `--step`, `/step` and `toolCallSyntax` exist; links and anchors resolve; no wording claims an independent ACCEPT or a published release.\\n\\nCorrections found and applied:\\n1. **HIGH - WP-1107 was overclaimed.** `adaptToolDefinitionsForServer` returns tools unchanged unless the server kind is vLLM, and the tests assert llama.cpp and Ollama keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint). The roadmap's llama.cpp `grammar`, vLLM `guided_json`, Ollama `format` and hybrid reasoning grammars are not implemented. The notes, the qualification WP-1107 and G1.1-4 rows now say: bounded schema compiler plus strict function schemas on the vLLM path only, reduced scope.\\n2. **MEDIUM - `CHANGELOG.md`** described v1.1.2 as the 2026-11-01 multi-message patch; now \\\"Unreleased\\\", with the real scope.\\n3. **MEDIUM - limitations stated too weakly or missing**: candidate build-config edits silently ignored; the fail-open overlay rated HIGH; command-path escape comes from trusted configuration; `node --check` wording; pinned workspace under the system temp dir; candidate symlink with a source extension; `spec.candidate.cwd` overridden; `--pretty` output; text-mode tool calls not counted by `toolCallSyntax`; the server-kind cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint; the nullable-property claim measured on a synthetic tool only.\\n4. **Review table**: added the first WP-1105 review row (`5fde750a`, three MEDIUM findings), restored the \\\"borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS\\\" qualifier, corrected the `7f915894..b032791e` outcome (the task-class header leak was closed; kind loss on an unreadable model list was not).\\n5. \\\"No separate review\\\" sentence corrected (an earlier draft of these documents was reviewed and changes were requested).\\n6. G1.1-5: \\\"the CodeQL check passed (alert count not queried)\\\"; CodeRabbit listed as skipped; \\\"my wrapper\\\" -> \\\"the gate wrapper\\\"; \\\"make exit 2 (recipe exit 1)\\\".\\n\\nCould not verify (per the reviewer): the WP-1102 22/22, WP-1106 8/8 and slash_router 34/34 counts and the rc.1/rc.2 archive/SBOM hashes (taken from codex-root's earlier record, labelled historical); that no other process ran on the host during the gate; zero CodeQL alerts; the 141-component SBOM and the WP-1108 \\\"27 Dependabot PRs\\\" claim. Note from the reviewer for the owner: the 2026-11-03 20:42 UTC decision said \\\"tag after independent ACCEPT + exact-head green CI\\\"; the 2026-11-04 15:06 UTC waiver covers the open findings, and the owner may want to confirm that the Entire approval on the final head also stands in for the independent ACCEPT.\\n\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"id\":6638774667,\"pull_request_review_id\":null,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T18:31:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-04T18:31:43Z\",\"review\":null,\"side\":null,\"line\":null,\"start_line\":null,\"path\":null,\"body_html\":\"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Independent review of the release documents and version bump (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf..40d553b5</code>; reviewer agent, not the author; read-only, no test runs): <strong>REQUEST CHANGES</strong>, applied in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">fafbf6d5</code> (documentation only; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'</code> is empty; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">security_gates.sh</code> passes on it).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Verified correct: every number and log hash in the final-gate section (cargo 43+254+1+4+1, 2,377 tests / 237 suites / 2,371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped, the five skip reasons, five SHA-256 values, the make-test abort before the scope-procs and security steps); <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff --stat c198a33f 2dbe565b</code> = typecheck_clean.mjs, code_evaluators.test.ts, docs and one evidence JSON; the coded-diagnostic regex at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf</code>; check runs on <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bd7fb1cf</code>; the version bump (six files, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">harness-core</code> 1.1.2 in Cargo.lock, both package-lock entries, no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">1.1.2-rc.2</code> outside docs); no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">v1.1.2*</code> tag on origin; <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6151699555\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/398\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/398\\\">#398</a>/<a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6150439871\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/396\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/396/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/396\\\">#396</a>/<a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6170113661\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/401\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/401/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/401\\\">#401</a> merged and ancestors; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--step</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/step</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">toolCallSyntax</code> exist; links and anchors resolve; no wording claims an independent ACCEPT or a published release.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Corrections found and applied:</p>\\n<ol dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><strong>HIGH - WP-1107 was overclaimed.</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">adaptToolDefinitionsForServer</code> returns tools unchanged unless the server kind is vLLM, and the tests assert llama.cpp and Ollama keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint). The roadmap's llama.cpp <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">grammar</code>, vLLM <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">guided_json</code>, Ollama <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">format</code> and hybrid reasoning grammars are not implemented. The notes, the qualification WP-1107 and G1.1-4 rows now say: bounded schema compiler plus strict function schemas on the vLLM path only, reduced scope.</li>\\n<li><strong>MEDIUM - <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">CHANGELOG.md</code></strong> described v1.1.2 as the 2026-11-01 multi-message patch; now \\\"Unreleased\\\", with the real scope.</li>\\n<li><strong>MEDIUM - limitations stated too weakly or missing</strong>: candidate build-config edits silently ignored; the fail-open overlay rated HIGH; command-path escape comes from trusted configuration; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">node --check</code> wording; pinned workspace under the system temp dir; candidate symlink with a source extension; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">spec.candidate.cwd</code> overridden; <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--pretty</code> output; text-mode tool calls not counted by <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">toolCallSyntax</code>; the server-kind cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint; the nullable-property claim measured on a synthetic tool only.</li>\\n<li><strong>Review table</strong>: added the first WP-1105 review row (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">5fde750a</code>, three MEDIUM findings), restored the \\\"borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS\\\" qualifier, corrected the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">7f915894..b032791e</code> outcome (the task-class header leak was closed; kind loss on an unreadable model list was not).</li>\\n<li>\\\"No separate review\\\" sentence corrected (an earlier draft of these documents was reviewed and changes were requested).</li>\\n<li>G1.1-5: \\\"the CodeQL check passed (alert count not queried)\\\"; CodeRabbit listed as skipped; \\\"my wrapper\\\" -&gt; \\\"the gate wrapper\\\"; \\\"make exit 2 (recipe exit 1)\\\".</li>\\n</ol>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Could not verify (per the reviewer): the WP-1102 22/22, WP-1106 8/8 and slash_router 34/34 counts and the rc.1/rc.2 archive/SBOM hashes (taken from codex-root's earlier record, labelled historical); that no other process ran on the host during the gate; zero CodeQL alerts; the 141-component SBOM and the WP-1108 \\\"27 Dependabot PRs\\\" claim. Note from the reviewer for the owner: the 2026-11-03 20:42 UTC decision said \\\"tag after independent ACCEPT + exact-head green CI\\\"; the 2026-11-04 15:06 UTC waiver covers the open findings, and the owner may want to confirm that the Entire approval on the final head also stands in for the independent ACCEPT.</p>\"}],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402\",\"title\":\"mikeholownych/nexus-code PR #402 comments\",\"display_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/402\",\"display_title\":\"mikeholownych/nexus-code PR #402 comments\"},\"isError\":false}"}],"isError":false},"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":58845923}},"started_at_ms":1793828440536,"completed_at_ms":1793828441595}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:40:42.083Z","ordinal":114666,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a881-cfe2-7123-90ab-450781ad740d","call_id":"call_a1aab71e9a1642c4838a318cedbf51d2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6614964594 2026-11-03T20:43:07Z by coderabbitai[bot]\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\"} --> Trigger review\n> \n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> - **Source mode**: Auto\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\n> - **Layers**: defaults\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\n> - **Run ID**: `07231aaa-61c5-47af-9206-845746424f20`\n> \n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=402)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Share</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6626037487 2026-11-04T08:15:39Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent review of the WP-1105 evaluator work as of 5fde750a (everything after the last independent review at 08aace7d): **REQUEST CHANGES**. Sandbox containment is solid and the telemetry counts each call once; three MEDIUM issues mean the evaluators can pass without measuring anything or fail honest runs.\n\nTests: code_evaluators 22/22, parser_safety 12, parser_single_quote 10, eval/dataset 12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. eval_dataset.test.ts was refused by a host compiler-exposure check before any evaluator ran (read as a host limit).\n\n**F1 MEDIUM - typecheck_clean passes vacuously when the checker cannot run on either side.** `typecheck_clean.mjs:41-49` tolerates any failing baseline if the candidate adds no new diagnostic lines. With real tsc and no node_modules on either side: 12 identical \"Cannot find module\" lines, passed:true, score 1; a candidate syntax error the checker never saw also passed; a bwrap setup failure with identical stderr passes the same way. Fix: require a recognised baseline state (exit 0, or a task-supplied diagnostic regex such as `error TS\\d+`).\n\n**F2 MEDIUM - build and typecheck_clean run the candidate-modified build config.** `run.mjs:308` passes the agent-modified tree; hardened mode's configChanges refusal covers only hidden/regression checks. A candidate that rewrote tsconfig.json to `\"files\":[\"empty.ts\"]` while keeping a new error file got passed:true. Fix: pin config from the baseline, or make diff_boundary cover config files; document it.\n\n**F3 MEDIUM - syntax_ast with the runner's default file list false-fails honest agents.** `runner.mjs:162` uses `spec.files ?? changedFiles`, which includes deleted and non-source paths: an edit to src/a.ts + delete of src/old.ts + edit of README.md gives passed:false (`unsupported source extension`, `ENOENT`). Any task without `spec.files` can never pass if the agent deletes a file or edits a non-code file.\n\nF4 LOW-MEDIUM: evaluator commands have no memory/pid/disk limits (`command.mjs` calls runProcess without `resources`; only wall time and the 4 MiB output cap bound them). F5 LOW-MEDIUM: in-process TypeScript parsing has no timeout (65 MB file blocked the event loop 62.9 s). F6 LOW: a relative command path/symlink resolving outside the workspace runs a host script (trusted config; small exposure). F7 LOW: typecheck_clean false-fails on benign line-shift or summary-count changes (fails closed). F8 nits: legacy text parsing is not counted; `hiddenWorkspace` unused; root `.git` changes invisible to diff_boundary (documented).\n\nHeld up: argv is passed literally, no shell, env scrubbed, caps 0/NoNewPrivs, symlinked-directory and /etc/shadow escapes return ENOENT, 25 MB output killed, timeout kills trap-TERM and setsid descendants, snapshot uses O_NOFOLLOW + inode checks, telemetry counts once per call with a single subagent roll-up (real `nexus run --json` checked), the 18-row typecheck case table behaves as designed.\n\nTest gaps (mutations that survived): baseline-status-0 term of the regression rule; sibling-directory escape (`/tmp/ws-evil`); root `.git` skip; per-turn reset of turnToolCallSyntax; no tests for output overflow, command-symlink confinement, or syntax_ast with deleted/non-source files.\n\nNot verified: harness end to end (blocked by the host check), eval_hardened/eval_integrity/eval_harness/tool_grammar_matrix, a real fork bomb, spoofing of agent --json stdout, Node versions other than 24.11.1, agent.ts changes outside the telemetry hunks.\n\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6626957823 2026-11-04T09:04:38Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent delta review of b032791e (WP-1107 remediation, parent 7f915894, local-only commit by codex-root): **REQUEST CHANGES** - 3 of the 4 earlier WP-1107 findings are FIXED, one is PARTIAL.\n\n**1. HIGH null optional args: FIXED.** Driven through `AutonomousAgent.dispatchToolCall` against the real harness-core built from this commit: every optional field of read_file (start_line, end_line, offset, length), write_file (overwrite), edit_file (replace_all) and run_command (cwd, timeout_secs, shell, background, service_name) reaches the core without error, alone or all-null. Required fields given as null (path, content, old_content, new_content, command) are still rejected before dispatch and nothing is defaulted or written. `overwrite:null` on an existing file is refused like `false`; `content:\"\"`, `shell:\"\"`, `cwd:\"\"`, `timeout_secs:0` are not stripped. Mutation: removing the strip block makes vllm_nullable_dispatch fail with \"invalid type: null, expected a boolean\".\n\n**2. MEDIUM REQ-PRV-109 X-Task-Class: PARTIAL.** The leak is closed: llama.cpp /props 404, Ollama without /api/version or with /api/show 404, vLLM /version 404, `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0`, bare catalog and no /models all suppress the header now (sent at 7f915894); rediscovery 503/bad JSON/dropped connection also suppresses it. Gateway still sends it. Mutations show the new task_class tests are real (8 fails with the fix reverted). **Not fixed:** on an unreadable-/models rediscovery (also /models 404 and \"model not listed\") a previously known llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM endpoint still falls to kind `unknown`, so vLLM loses `strict` and the root /tokenize fallback, while the agent keeps the last advertisement - the two disagree. The plan's AC8 narrows retention to gateway only. Identical at 7f915894 and b032791e. Suggested fix: keep the previous kind when rediscovery returns unavailable.\n\n**3. MEDIUM matrix runner: FIXED.** Rejected: forged provenance + handwritten dist + unrelated archive, forged MANIFEST, symlinked lib/ or installRoot (or a symlink in its parent path), installed file symlinked to the archive, archives containing a symlink/hardlink, extra installed files, wrong pinned digest, caller runtime/tools options, revision mismatch. Swapping client.js, installRoot or the archive after verification has no effect (only the private verified snapshot runs). Regression test fails when the post-snapshot verification, the import-from-snapshot or the per-file digest compare is removed; the provenance check, installed-symlink check, realpath, file-set and package-tree digest compare are defence in depth and untested.\n\n**4. MEDIUM-LOW vLLM identity: FIXED.** max_model_len/context_length + a /version route without `owned_by:\"vllm\"` is now `unknown`, strict false; real vLLM responses are still `vllm`.\n\nRegression sweep (focused files, isolated HOME): client_tool_grammar 16/16, provider_capabilities 13/13, server_context_discovery 17/17, standalone_profiles 5/5, tokens 4/4, task_class 8/8, tool_grammar 4/4, tool_grammar_matrix 13/13, client_robustness 9/9, vllm_nullable_dispatch 4/4, eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs 13/13; tsc clean. No assertion weakened silently; the reversed expectations match the stated behaviour change.\n\nNew findings: (MEDIUM) the rediscovery kind loss above; (LOW-MEDIUM) null stripping applies only to the dispatch copy, so read-coverage and observation tracking still see raw nulls under vLLM strict (`readRequests(\"read_file\", {path, offset:null, length:null})` returns undefined; observationKey differs) - normalising at the parse step would fix it and remove the hardcoded per-tool list; (LOW) a transient /version failure on a successful rediscovery downgrades vLLM to unknown; (LOW) matrix `sourceCommit` is checked only against .provenance.json and archiveSha256 pinning is optional - the downstream gate must pin it; (NIT) vllm_nullable_dispatch covers only write_file.overwrite and run_command fields.\n\nNot verified: full test suite/make test, live vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama (mocks only), real install.sh output through the runner, first-request header behaviour on a real gateway, approval behaviour with null cwd in restrictive modes, same-uid attacker with write access to the snapshot dir.\n\nOut of scope here and still open: the WP-1105 evaluator findings F1-F3 (separate review).\n\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6633861635 2026-11-04T14:55:20Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent delta review of the WP-1105 evaluator half of 0d506762 (reviewer agent, not the author; run on 0d506762 in a detached worktree and scratch copies; 05913af5 was read but not run): **REQUEST CHANGES**.\n\n**F1 (typecheck_clean vacuous pass): FIXED at 0d506762, probably reopened by 05913af5.** At 0d506762: no node_modules on either side now gives infrastructureFailure/passed:false (real sandbox + real tsc); a candidate syntax error with no node_modules fails; identical \"Cannot find module\" lines and identical bwrap setup failures on both sides fail. The gate is a hard-coded `error TS\\d+:` regex, not a task-supplied one, so non-TS checkers (eslint, mypy, cargo check) fail closed whenever the baseline already has errors - undocumented; README/SPEC-EVALUATION still describe the old rule. Residual: identical recognised config errors (TS5057) on both sides still pass. **05913af5 changes the regex to `\\berror(?:\\s+TS\\d+|\\[E\\d+\\])?:` with /i - the code group is optional, so any `error:` line (incl. Node's `Error: Cannot find module '...'`) counts as recognised and F1 scenario 1 probably goes back to passed:true (read from the diff, NOT verified). Fix: require a TS or Rust code; add a test with `Error: Cannot find module` on both sides.**\n\n**F2 (candidate-modified build config): PARTIAL.** Now blocked (real tsc): tsconfig rewritten to files:[\"empty.ts\"]; include:[\"nothing\"]; tsconfig.build.json; extends chain; package.json scripts; scripts/build.js; .tsbuildinfo; a patched node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc (no extension). Still open: **node_modules shadowing** (rewriting node_modules/typescript/lib/tsc.js to exit(0) with a type error kept gave build and typecheck_clean passed:true - the overlay copies every candidate-changed .ts/.js/.rs/.py incl. node_modules) and **any in-repo build helper** (tools/check.js rewritten to exit(0) made build pass; same for build.rs, setup.py, conftest.py; only *.config.* and scripts/{build,compile,typecheck}.* are excluded). Honest candidates editing tsconfig/package.json are not wrongly failed, but the edited config is silently ignored (not reported, not documented).\n\n**F3 (syntax_ast default list): FIXED** (edit src/a.ts + delete src/old.ts + edit README.md passes; broken .ts/.TS, broken .ts with another file renamed .txt, symlink to /etc/passwd, dangling .ts symlink all still fail). Pre-existing, not this commit: `node --check` exits 0 on ESM-syntax .js such as `export const a = ;` under Node v24.11.1, a false pass in parsers.mjs.\n\n**F4 (memory/pid/disk limits), F5 (parser timeout), F6 (command-path symlink/.. escape), F7 (line-shift false failures): untouched** (no diff in command.mjs, isolate.mjs, parsers.mjs; resolveCommand unchanged).\n\n**New findings.**\n1. **HIGH, fail-open:** build/typecheck_clean now run in baseline + an overlay of only .ts/.mts/.cts/.tsx/.js/.mjs/.cjs/.jsx/.rs/.py candidate files. Edits to any other file are invisible to the build: a .go edit that breaks the build and a new .c file that breaks it both gave build passed:true (a .ts control failed correctly). The same cause fails honest candidates: a new src/data.json with resolveJsonModule gave a false TS2307. This regresses the previous behaviour (build ran in the candidate workspace). Fix: fail closed for unsupported changed files, or use a deny-list overlay.\n2. MEDIUM: the node_modules / build-helper overlay vectors above.\n3. MEDIUM (05913af5): the optional-code regex above.\n4. MEDIUM, honest-run failure: two full workspace snapshots (baseline + candidate) even for build-only tasks; a ~54k-file node_modules gave \"workspace snapshot refused: traversal deadline exceeded\" after 5 s, and the 50,000-entry cap would also refuse it, so build failed.\n5. LOW: pinned workspace is created under os.tmpdir(), not config.resources.workspaceRoot; a candidate symlink with a source extension fails build and typecheck_clean (\"not a stable regular file\"); spec.candidate.cwd is silently overridden by the pinned root; an explicit baseline without typecheckBaselineWorkspace now errors; README stale; --pretty ANSI output defeats the TS regex (fails closed).\n\nTypecheck rule table (18 rows): all listed rules hold; three rows changed from pass to fail (identical non-TS failures, identical bwrap failures, non-TS baseline errors). `statusRegression` is now effectively dead.\n\nTests at 0d506762: code_evaluators 25/25, parser_safety 12/12, parser_single_quote 10/10, eval/dataset 12/12, eval/package_runtime 2 pass/3 skipped, tsc clean. Existing assertions changed (3) were not weakened. Mutations that survived: dropping the .config.*/scripts/build.* exclusions; making an empty default syntax_ast list fail. No tests cover node_modules, non-source build inputs, or a broken edited source file in the default list; the unavailable-checker test uses status 127 with no `error:` text so it would not catch the 05913af5 regex.\n\n05913af5 (read only): the runner change recreates the target with O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW, closing the baseline-symlink overlay hole - sound from reading, not run. Its tests were not reviewed. Not verified: anything run from 05913af5, the cargo check/Rust path, Go/make toolchains in the sandbox, non-TS checkers, workspaceRoot on tmpfs. Context: no task in eval/tasks or the datasets currently uses `evaluators`.\n\nDisclosure: the reviewer ran focused tests (code_evaluators, scenarios, mutations, parser suites, dataset, package_runtime, tsc) inside its own worktree and scratch copies before the stop message arrived; it ran nothing from ~/nexus-code/cli or v112-*, but its node_modules was a symlink into ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules and the runs used real bwrap, so they may have overlapped codex-root's gate.\n\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6633876272 2026-11-04T14:55:57Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent delta review of the WP-1107 half of 0d506762 (reviewer agent, not the author; parent b032791e; focused tests only, scenario tables at both commits, mutations on scratch copies, matrix runner read-only): **REQUEST CHANGES** (borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS). 05913af5 was read but not run.\n\n**A. REQ-PRV-109 retention: PARTIAL.** Fixed: 4 kinds x 8 rediscovery modes - at b032791e a 503, bad JSON, dropped connection, 404 or missing model dropped llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM to `unknown` (vLLM lost strict and the root /tokenize fallback); at 0d506762 all keep the kind, vLLM keeps strict:true and /tokenize, and X-Task-Class stays absent for standalone servers; a readable generic catalog correctly clears the kind. **Not fixed: retention has no bound.** `serverKindCache` is a process-wide map keyed only by endpoint string with no TTL, failure counter or invalidation (the commit removed every `delete`): a vLLM kind survived 3 further 503s and a swap to a llama.cpp server that did not list the model; a fresh client for the same endpoint inherits the old kind (true before the commit too); no invalidation on endpoint, /model provider or account switch. A replaced server answering 404/503/without the model leaks the old `strict` flag. **Gateway behaviour is not unchanged:** at b032791e a gateway whose /models 404'd or lacked the model went to unknown and the header was suppressed; at 0d506762 it stays `gateway` and the header is sent - in the scenario \"gateway replaced by a standalone server returning 404 on /models\" the header was `subagent`, i.e. it leaks to a non-gateway server (503 and dropped connection behave the same in both commits).\n\n**B. Null normalisation: PARTIAL.** Fixed: the per-tool strip list is gone from agent.ts, replaced by schema-driven `normalizeNullableOptionalToolArguments` applied in the client on streamed and non-streamed paths and again at dispatch (idempotent). Every optional property of the four harness tools (read_file start_line/end_line/offset/length; write_file overwrite; edit_file replace_all; run_command cwd/timeout_secs/shell/background/service_name) is stripped when null; required nulls are kept (still rejected); false/0/\"\" not stripped; for a well-formed native call the observation key is `{\"path\":\"a.txt\"}` and read coverage is recorded. **Not fixed:** calls that bypass the client normaliser (arguments needing JSON repair, text-mode tool calls) still reach observationKey/readRequests with nulls - coverage was NOCOVERAGE for repairable null arguments and COVERAGE for clean ones, keys differ; the dispatch-time strip changes only the local `args`, not the call object. Narrow (vLLM strict normally emits valid JSON) but real. **Over-broad:** the normaliser strips null from every optional property of every tool for all providers; a property whose schema explicitly allows null (e.g. an MCP tool taking `[\"string\",\"null\"]`) loses a meaningful null (measured on a synthetic tool; real MCP tools not checked).\n\n**C. Transient /version failure on a successful rediscovery: PARTIAL.** vLLM kind and strict are retained, but the returned advertisement has `via:\"catalog\"` not `\"vllm\"`; agent.ts `measureAdmission` allows tokenizing only for via llamacpp/vllm or tokenize:true, so the agent probably reports \"no request counting\" while the client holds the vLLM kind (the same after a 404/missing-model rediscovery, where refreshCapabilities drops the advertisement). tokens.test.ts calls countRequestTokens directly and bypasses that gate. Read from code, not run end to end.\n\n**D. Matrix runner: FIXED, with a residual.** sourceCommit is now checked against Git HEAD of a caller-named candidateCheckoutRoot (must be a real directory, the worktree top level, clean with --untracked-files=all); archiveSha256 is required (sha256: prefix and uppercase accepted; empty/missing/wrong rejected). Symlinked installRoot/checkout root/lib, a subdirectory of the checkout and a post-verify swap are rejected or irrelevant (the runtime is imported from the private verified archive snapshot). Residual LOW-MEDIUM: the checkout is not bound to the archive contents - a handwritten dist with a matching manifest, forged provenance and any unrelated clean repo whose HEAD equals the claimed commit still passes verification (the author's own fixture does this).\n\n**E. Test quality: PARTIAL.** Mutations: client normaliser no-op -> only the client_tool_grammar streamed/non-streamed test fails; dispatch normaliser no-op -> only vllm_nullable_dispatch; both removed -> agent_observer finally fails; retention reverted for 503 -> 4 tests fail (task_class, tokens); missing-model reverted -> task_class; /version retention reverted -> client_tool_grammar; generic-clears reverted -> task_class; matrix HEAD check, clean check and pin requirement each fail exactly their own test; whole commit reverted -> 3 fail. **Survivors/gaps:** 404 reverted to unknown, and a thrown exception (bad JSON, dropped connection) changed to delete the kind - nothing fails; the new agent_observer test passes with either normaliser removed alone (it checks post-dispatch args, not call.function.arguments); \"required null is rejected\" in vllm_nullable_dispatch also passes if required nulls are stripped (the error text matches either way). No assertion weakened.\n\n**F. Regression sweep (focused files, 0d506762, isolated HOME, built core in the worktree): PASS.** client_tool_grammar 18/18, provider_capabilities 13/13, server_context_discovery 17/17, standalone_profiles 5/5, tokens 5/5, task_class 10/10, tool_grammar 4/4, tool_grammar_matrix (cli) 16/16, client_robustness 9/9, vllm_nullable_dispatch 4/4, agent_observer 12/12 on rerun (one load-flaky failure in the first run: \"subagent model requests are nested under the parent turn\", 116 s under load 16), eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs 16/16; tsc clean by output only.\n\n**New findings, ranked.** (1) MEDIUM: retained kind has no expiry/invalidation, and gateway retention on 404/missing model now leaks X\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6635599479 2026-11-04T16:09:25Z by mikeholownych\ncodex-root release update (2026-11-04): c198a33f is committed and its exact source gate passed (make test 2,369 pass, 0 fail, 5 skipped; security lifecycle and terminal process-scope gates passed; make build passed). Independent review_delta approved the cumulative WP-1107/WP-1105 remediation diff through c198a33f.\n\nTwo digest-pinned RC2 builds from c198a33f matched byte-for-byte across archive, checksums, SBOMs, notices, compatibility metadata, and installer. Archive SHA-256: `ddaa6915da0808b8a95ac115c54a076411351c45229af7538ffc0236e59dad7c`. The production installer installed that archive and its `.provenance.json` binds the exact archive SHA and source revision. `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` reported 5/5, with six benchmark requests and prompt-boundary checks; however, this test run overlapped the active shared SUITE claim, so I am treating it as provisional and will rerun after the reviewer releases the claim.\n\nThis is RC2 qualification for c198a33f only. PR head `8520d9c8` also merges a `main` change in `cli/src/config.ts`; it still needs exact-head gate and a package built from the final stable-version source. No tag or release files have been published.\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6636044593 2026-11-04T16:29:56Z by mikeholownych\nQualification handoff: doc/evidence commit `63e2f49c28160408afeeeca4245f10e2bead0c8b` is now on `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`; it contains no source-code changes. The updated qualification record is independently approved and passes `sync-version --check`, `check_requirements`, and `git diff --check`. It records the c198a33f source gate, reproducible RC2 package/provenance, five exact-suite skip reasons, CI/CodeQL snapshot, and the provisional status of the package-runtime 5/5 run.\n\nI released the 30 WP-1105/WP-1107 source/test/plan/qualification file claims from that worktree. The shared SUITE claim remains held by claude-code; rerun package-runtime acceptance after release. The c198a33f RC2 archive is historical only: PR head `8520d9c8` and the final stable-version source still require exact-head gates and a fresh stable artifact. The supported-provider G1.1-4 matrix remains pending on the external GATEWAY handoff. No tag or release assets were published.\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6636183487 2026-11-04T16:35:53Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent short review of 0d506762..c198a33f (reviewer agent, not the author; real bwrap sandbox + real tsc + real runCodeEvaluators in a detached worktree at c198a33f; focused tests only): **REQUEST CHANGES** on one NEW finding. The symlink fix, the sidecar change and the grammar test are fine.\n\n**NEW P1 - typecheck_clean regex reopens the vacuous pass.** 05913af5 changed `/\\berror\\s+TS\\d+:/i` to `/\\berror(?:\\s+TS\\d+|\\[E\\d+\\])?:/i`; the code group is now optional, so the bare `error:` matches with `/i` and Node's `Error: Cannot find module ...` counts as a recognised diagnostic.\n\n| Case (real sandbox + real tsc) | 0d506762 | c198a33f |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) no node_modules on both sides | fail, infrastructureFailure true | **passed true, score 1**, infrastructureFailure false |\n| (b) candidate syntax error, no node_modules | fail | **passed true, score 1** (the candidate error is never evaluated) |\n| (c) bwrap failure on both sides | fail | fail, infrastructureFailure true |\n| (d) Rust error[E0308] on both sides | fail (not recognised) | pass; a new error[E0425] fails with newDiagnostics (intended; unit-level only - cargo is not in the runner's /usr/bin,/bin) |\n| (e) normal added TS error (node_modules present) | fail | fail (same) |\n\nAny generic lowercase `error: ...` line is now also \"recognised\" (e.g. cargo's `error: could not find Cargo.toml`). Only candidates in a workspace with no installed `typescript` are affected. Suggested fix: drop the optional group and require a code, `/\\berror\\s+TS\\d+:|\\berror\\[E\\d+\\]:/` (keep `i` for TS only), and add a test with `Error: Cannot find module` on both sides (no existing test covers it; the unavailable-checker test uses text without the `Error:` prefix).\n\n**1. runner.mjs symlink overlay: correct and safe.** P1 reproduced and closed: baseline `src/main.ts` as a symlink to an outside file - at 0d506762 the outside file became the candidate bytes, at c198a33f it stays unchanged. No TOCTOU (fresh mkdtemp tree written only by this process); directory-symlink parents and hardlinks leave the outside file unchanged; overwritten (0755), deleted, nested-new-dir (0640) and new .rs overlays are correct and `fchmod` preserves modes; cleanup removes tempRoot and closes the fd in a finally. Reverting only the fix makes the new test fail - the test is real.\n\n**3. sidecar.ts: safe.** `workspace_name` is restored verbatim after redaction as `workspace` already was (without it the name became `[REDACTED:HIGH_ENTROPY_STRING]`); it is only `path.basename(config.workspace)`, a substring of `workspace`, so no new exposure; a fake `ghp_` token in model/session/git.branch is still redacted; the new test fails if the restore line is removed. Existing nit (not new): a secret-shaped directory name still appears verbatim in both fields.\n\n**4. client_tool_grammar new test: real** (pins existing behaviour; a sticky vLLM cache in a scratch copy makes it fail).\n\n**P3 nit:** a dangling symlink at a path the candidate overlays now fails closed with EEXIST/pinnedWorkspaceError (build and typecheck score 0) because on Node v24.11.1 `fs.rmSync(dangling-link, {force:true})` does not remove it; the old code wrote through the link. Safe, but rejects a valid candidate.\n\nTests (isolated HOME, --test-concurrency=1, one file at a time, core built from c198a33f): code_evaluators 27/27, client_tool_grammar 19/19, sidecar_diagnostic_redaction 6/6, sidecar 55/55, sidecar_steering_diff 16/16, tsc clean. (First sidecar runs failed 9/55 and 4/16 only because the worktree had no Rust core - host environment, not a defect.)\n\nNot verified: a real Rust/cargo typecheck through the sandbox, other session.state test files (TUI e2e, approval_policy, provider_connect, upgrade), other Node versions, the full suite.\n\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6636656187 2026-11-04T16:56:01Z by mikeholownych\nRelease handoff (2026-11-04): WP-1105 typecheck diagnostic fix is READY in local integration commit `2dbe565b3e5276d8226d50e7ac3a121962a64058`. Exact-commit focused evaluator suite: 29/29 PASS (log SHA-256 `405e3819bafc7f4ed221cadf096918bc8a251d9506c9e8a0bd53696877a6a7d8`); `npx tsc --noEmit`: PASS (log SHA-256 `f97c0f0b52dcae52444a1d6e462831513eb5ac35987d6f3df7efa043f4afc0db`); independent review_delta: APPROVED. Claims released; no full suite run, per owner instruction.\n\nThe older delta review was against `b032791e`. The cumulative integration branch now includes the null-argument, verified-matrix-candidate, vLLM identity, and rediscovery-retention changes, plus WP-1105 evaluator remediation. The new diagnostic-regex regression found after c198 is fixed by 2dbe565b. Please incorporate that commit into the release branch before the stable-head gate. Current PR/release branch remains `8520d9c8`; stable version bump, final artifact/installed qualification, GATEWAY provider matrix (still externally held), release PTY acceptance, and publication remain open. Nothing is pushed, tagged, or published by this handoff.\n---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ID 6638774667 2026-11-04T18:31:43Z by mikeholownych\nIndependent review of the release documents and version bump (`bd7fb1cf..40d553b5`; reviewer agent, not the author; read-only, no test runs): **REQUEST CHANGES**, applied in `fafbf6d5` (documentation only; `git diff --stat bd7fb1cf HEAD -- ':!docs' ':!CHANGELOG.md'` is empty; `security_gates.sh` passes on it).\n\nVerified correct: every number and log hash in the final-gate section (cargo 43+254+1+4+1, 2,377 tests / 237 suites / 2,371 pass / 1 fail / 5 skipped, the five skip reasons, five SHA-256 values, the make-test abort before the scope-procs and security steps); `git diff --stat c198a33f 2dbe565b` = typecheck_clean.mjs, code_evaluators.test.ts, docs and one evidence JSON; the coded-diagnostic regex at `bd7fb1cf`; check runs on `bd7fb1cf`; the version bump (six files, `harness-core` 1.1.2 in Cargo.lock, both package-lock entries, no `1.1.2-rc.2` outside docs); no `v1.1.2*` tag on origin; #398/#396/#401 merged and ancestors; `--step`, `/step` and `toolCallSyntax` exist; links and anchors resolve; no wording claims an independent ACCEPT or a published release.\n\nCorrections found and applied:\n1. **HIGH - WP-1107 was overclaimed.** `adaptToolDefinitionsForServer` returns tools unchanged unless the server kind is vLLM, and the tests assert llama.cpp and Ollama keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint). The roadmap's llama.cpp `grammar`, vLLM `guided_json`, Ollama `format` and hybrid reasoning grammars are not implemented. The notes, the qualification WP-1107 and G1.1-4 rows now say: bounded schema compiler plus strict function schemas on the vLLM path only, reduced scope.\n2. **MEDIUM - `CHANGELOG.md`** described v1.1.2 as the 2026-11-01 multi-message patch; now \"Unreleased\", with the real scope.\n3. **MEDIUM - limitations stated too weakly or missing**: candidate build-config edits silently ignored; the fail-open overlay rated HIGH; command-path escape comes from trusted configuration; `node --check` wording; pinned workspace under the system temp dir; candidate symlink with a source extension; `spec.candidate.cwd` overridden; `--pretty` output; text-mode tool calls not counted by `toolCallSyntax`; the server-kind cache is process-wide and keyed only by endpoint; the nullable-property claim measured on a synthetic tool only.\n4. **Review table**: added the first WP-1105 review row (`5fde750a`, three MEDIUM findings), restored the \"borderline with ACCEPT WITH NITS\" qualifier, corrected the `7f915894..b032791e` outcome (the task-class header leak was closed; kind loss on an unreadable model list was not).\n5. \"No separate review\" sentence corrected (an earlier draft of these documents was reviewed and changes were requested).\n6. G1.1-5: \"the CodeQL check passed (alert count not queried)\"; CodeRabbit listed as skipped; \"my wrapper\" -> \"the gate wrapper\"; \"make exit 2 (recipe exit 1)\".\n\nCould not verify (per the reviewer): the WP-1102 22/22, WP-1106 8/8 and slash_router 34/34 counts and the rc.1/rc.2 archive/SBOM hashes (taken from codex-root's earlier record, labelled historical); that no other process ran on the host during the gate; zero CodeQL alerts; the 141-component SBOM and the WP-1108 \"27 Dependabot PRs\" claim. Note from the reviewer for the owner: the 2026-11-03 20:42 UTC decision said \"tag after independent ACCEPT + exact-head green CI\"; the 2026-11-04 15:06 UTC waiver covers the open findings, and the owner may want to confirm that the Entire approval on the final head also stands in for the independent ACCEPT.\n\n---"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828442.0829678}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
