A deterministic substitution of the installed runtime after snapshot verification and before import cannot affect the measured code. Test: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`.\n- **AC10:** vLLM identity requires a model catalog entry whose `owned_by` is exactly `vllm` (case-insensitive) and a non-empty `version` from `/version`; generic `context_length` or `max_model_len` fields and a generic `/version` route alone do not identify vLLM or enable strict adaptation. Tests: `generic catalog metadata does not identify vLLM`; `vLLM adaptation requires owned_by vllm and a version handshake`.\n- **AC11:** The vLLM strict-mode compatibility normalization also omits explicit `null` for optional `run_command.shell`, allowing the Rust RPC executor to apply its platform default, while preserving a non-null shell value. Test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge` (extended shell cases).\n- **AC12:** Unknown tool names including `toString` and `constructor` follow ordinary unknown-tool handling through terminal reporting and cannot trigger an exception during optional-argument normalization or label lookup. Test `unknown special-name tools do not enter nullable argument normalization` asserts the same ordinary unknown-tool receipt/result as a plain unknown name.\n- **AC13:** Before matrix inference, every installed package file (apart from the installer-owned provenance record) must match the verified archive snapshot's exact file set and SHA-256 digests; a matching but forged provenance record cannot make a modified installed runtime qualify. Test `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance` asserts rejection before any provider/client call and before evidence output is written.\n\n**Out of scope:** Live provider inference and the G1.1-4 99.5% metric remain gated on GATEWAY ownership; these source corrections do not satisfy that metric. Installer provenance remains an installer claim, and the matrix independently checks installed package bytes against the archive it measures.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1107 base commit `5fde750a`; exact-source and archive evidence at `7f915894` is historical for the pre-correction source and must be regenerated after the fixes.\n\n**Files:** `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`, and this plan. Existing context, token-counting, and standalone-profile tests already use the exact vLLM owner marker and a successful version route; they remain part of the final regression run without source edits. Atomically acquire an owner claim for every listed file before writing the first RED test; include any additional fixture/helper file in the claims before editing it.\n\n### Plan for review remediation\n\n**Chunks (each independently testable):**\n\n1. Normalize strict-mode optional nulls — files: `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n2. Preserve endpoint identity and gate task-class headers — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`; tests: all three AC8 tests.\n3. Require positive vLLM identity — files: `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`; tests: both AC10 tests plus existing context/token-counting and standalone-profile regressions in the full suite.\n4. Snapshot, verify, and bind matrix runtime bytes — files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`; tests: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`; `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance`.\n5. Complete optional and unknown-name dispatch boundaries — files: `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`; tests: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge` (shell cases); `unknown special-name tools do not enter nullable argument normalization` (ordinary unknown receipt/result through terminal reporting).\n\n**Reference corpora to query:** `nexus-core` for executor argument deserialization and defaults; `nexus-cli` for agent dispatch, routing-header policy, provider capability discovery, safe archive extraction, and manifest verification.\n\n**Risks / unknowns:**\n\n- Tool dispatch must prove real Rust RPC behavior — retrieval query: `dispatchToolCall parses arguments then invokes real tool executor`.\n- Archive verification must bind imported bytes across a deterministic installed-file substitution — retrieval query: `package MANIFEST.sha256 exact file set safe extraction and runtime import`.\n- Identity freshness is endpoint-keyed: transient `/models` failure keeps a same-URL positive gateway identity; a successful generic catalog or changed endpoint clears it — retrieval query: `parseAdvertisement serverKind positive identity vLLM owned_by version`.\n- `RunCommandArgs.shell` is a required Rust string with a serde default, so explicit JSON null must be omitted to reach that default — retrieved `nexus-core` `runner.rs:7-30`.\n- Optional-argument metadata must use own-key-safe lookup for model-controlled tool names — retrieved `nexus-cli` dispatch passage in `agent.ts` establishes the dispatch boundary; regression will pin prototype-name handling.\n- Terminal tool labels use a normal object keyed by model-controlled tool names; retrieved `nexus-cli` `ui.ts:144-151` shows the direct label lookup that also needs prototype-safe fallback behavior.\n- Archive snapshot verification alone does not prove the installed tree matches the archive — retrieved `nexus-cli` `upgrade.ts:1153-1172` verifies package manifests after extraction; the matrix must compare its installed files to that verified package manifest before measuring the snapshot runtime.\n  }\n  for (const [relative, expectedDigest] of expectedPackageFiles) {\n    if (installedFiles.get(relative) !== expectedDigest) {\n      throw new TypeError(`installed candidate file does not match the verified archive manifest: ${relative}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction verifyCandidateCheckout(checkoutRoot, sourceCommit) {\n  if (typeof checkoutRoot !== \"string\" || !checkoutRoot) throw new TypeError(\"explicit candidate Git checkout root is required\");\n  const resolvedRoot = path.resolve(checkoutRoot);\n  const stat = fs.lstatSync(resolvedRoot);\n  if (!stat.isDirectory() || stat.isSymbolicLink() || fs.realpathSync(resolvedRoot) !== resolvedRoot) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"candidate checkout root must be a real directory\");\n  }\n  const git = (args) => execFileSync(\"git\", args, { cwd: resolvedRoot, encoding: \"utf8\", stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] }).trim();\n  let gitRoot;\n  let head;\n  let status;\n  try {\n    gitRoot = git([\"rev-parse\", \"--show-toplevel\"]);\n    head = git([\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"]);\n    status = git([\"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=all\"]);\n  } catch {\n    throw new TypeError(\"candidate checkout root is not a readable Git worktree\");\n  }\n  if (path.resolve(gitRoot) !== resolvedRoot) throw new TypeError(\"candidate checkout root must be the Git worktree root\");\n  if (head !== sourceCommit) throw new TypeError(\"candidate source commit does not match Git HEAD\");\n  if (status) throw new TypeError(\"candidate checkout must be clean before matrix qualification\");\n  return head;\n}\n\n/** Invoke the exact installed candidate client for 50 attempts/tool and retain only non-secret aggregate evidence. */\nexport async function runToolGrammarMatrix(options) {\n  if (!options || typeof options.archivePath !== \"string\" || typeof options.installRoot !== \"string\") throw new TypeError(\"candidate archive and installed root are required\");\n  if (Object.hasOwn(options, \"runtime\")) throw new TypeError(\"caller-supplied runtime is not accepted; runtime must be loaded from the installed candidate\");\n  if (Object.hasOwn(options, \"tools\")) throw new TypeError(\"tool schemas must be loaded from the exact installed candidate\");\n  if (!commitPattern.test(options.sourceCommit)) throw new TypeError(\"full candidate source commit is required\");\n  verifyCandidateCheckout(options.candidateCheckoutRoot, options.sourceCommit);\n  if (typeof options.archiveSha256 !== \"string\" || !sha256Pattern.test(options.archiveSha256)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"pinned candidate archive SHA-256 is required\");\n  }\n  const archivePath = fs.realpathSync(options.archivePath);\n  const archiveSha256 = sha256(fs.readFileSync(archivePath));\n  if (options.archiveSha256.replace(/^sha256:/i, \"\").toLowerCase() !== archiveSha256) throw new TypeError(\"candidate archive SHA-256 does not match the pinned digest\");\n  const snapshot = createVerifiedArchiveSnapshot(archivePath, archiveSha256);\n  try {\n    verifyInstalledArchive(options.installRoot, archiveSha256, options.sourceCommit, snapshot.packageFiles);\n    if (!Array.isArray(options.providers) || options.providers.length !== 3) throw new TypeError(\"exactly one configuration per supported provider is required\");\n    const configuredProviders = options.providers.map((provider) => {\n      validProviderIdentity(provider);\n\n  /**\n   * This connection's `/models` entry for the selected model, read from the active endpoint only (never a fallback or\n   * another provider: capability discovery is scoped to the connection in use). Not content-bearing.\n   * `unsupported`: the provider has no catalog or does not list the model; `unavailable`: it could not be read now.\n   */\n  async discoverAdvertisement(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<{ state: \"supported\" | \"unsupported\" | \"unavailable\"; advertised?: Advertisement; detail?: string }> {\n    const ep = this.endpoint;\n    const previousKind = LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(ep);\n    if (this.conn.protocol !== \"openai-chat\") return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: `${this.conn.protocol} connection` };\n    const url = `${ep}/models`;\n    try {\n      await this.prepareCredential(ep);\n      const res = await fetch(url, {\n        // Marked so providers (and their logs) can tell a capability read from an availability probe.\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(10_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n      });\n      if (res.status === 404) {\n        // A catalog-less response does not contradict an identity verified earlier on this same endpoint.\n        if (previousKind) LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, previousKind);\n        return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: \"no /models catalog\" };\n      }\n      if (!res.ok) {\n        return { state: \"unavailable\", detail: `HTTP ${res.status}` };\n      }\n      const data = (await res.json()) as { data?: Array<Record<string, any>> };\n      const entry = Array.isArray(data?.data) ? data.data.find((e) => e?.id === this.model) : undefined;\n      // A catalog that cannot identify this model provides no contradictory identity evidence.\n      if (!entry) {\n        if (previousKind) LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, previousKind);\n        return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: `model ${this.model} not listed` };\n      }\n      let advertised = parseAdvertisement(entry);\n      let entryKind = advertised?.serverKind ?? serverKindOf(entry);\n      const vllmCatalogMarker = typeof entry.owned_by === \"string\" && entry.owned_by.toLowerCase() === \"vllm\";\n      if (!this.conn.providerId) {\n        if (entryKind === \"llamacpp\" && (process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE === \"0\" || !(await this.discoverServerContext(entry, signal))) ) {\n          entryKind = \"unknown\";\n        } else if (entryKind === \"ollama\" && (process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE === \"0\" || !(await this.discoverOllamaIdentity(signal))) ) {\n          entryKind = \"unknown\";\n        } else if (vllmCatalogMarker && entryKind === \"unknown\" && process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE !== \"0\") {\n          const version = await this.discoverVllmVersion(signal);\n          if (version) {\n            entryKind = \"vllm\";\n            if (advertised) advertised = { ...advertised, via: \"vllm\" };\n          } else if (previousKind === \"vllm\") {\n            // Keep strict mode and the /tokenize fallback through a transient version-route outage.\n            entryKind = \"vllm\";\n          }\n        }\n      }\n      // A readable generic entry clears a stale identity; only unavailable discovery, an absent model, or the\n      // specifically verified vLLM identity above may retain the previous kind.\n      if (!advertised || (advertised.contextLength === undefined && advertised.maxCompletionTokens === undefined)) {\n        // An OpenAI-style catalog without limits (llama.cpp, LM Studio, Ollama): ask the server itself what it loaded.\n        // Only for a plain endpoint: cloud provider connections have no such endpoints.\n        const local = this.conn.providerId || entryKind === \"unknown\" ? undefined : await this.discoverServerContext(entry, signal);\n        if (local) {\n          LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, local.serverKind ?? entryKind);\n          return { state: \"supported\", advertised: local };\n        }\n        LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, entryKind);\n        return { state: \"unsupported\", advertised, detail: \"catalog lists no limits\" };\n      }\n      LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, entryKind);\n      return { state: \"supported\", advertised };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return { state: \"unavailable\", detail: redactSecrets(String(err?.message ?? err)).slice(0, 160) };\n    }\n  }\n\n  private static serverContextCache = new Map<string, Advertisement>();\n  private static serverKindCache = new Map<string, ServerKind>();\n  private static serverShowCache = new Map<string, unknown>();\n\n  /** Provider identity detected for the active endpoint after capability discovery; unknown until a positive handshake. */\n  getDetectedServerKind(): ServerKind {\n    return LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(this.endpoint) ?? \"unknown\";\n  }\n\n  private async discoverVllmVersion(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<string | undefined> {\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828557.819885}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
