{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:44:36.751Z","ordinal":114736,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a885-648f-7c11-92e3-8252d200132f","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED — plan review.** Reviewed `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan` at `b032791e`; only `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md` is uncommitted. No tests or edits.\n\n- **AC8:** The separation is sound, but “fresh positive gateway handshake by that client” needs a defined freshness bound and explicit clearing on that client’s endpoint/model change. Also define what happens when a successful catalog omits the selected model; the current text says unavailable discovery retains identity, but does not clearly distinguish that case from a positive mismatch. The warm-vLLM test should assert both strict request adaptation and `/tokenize` routing. Add `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts` to chunk 2’s file list, or name a single test that demonstrably covers both behaviors.\n\n- **AC14:** The canonical-arguments criteria are strong and testable. However, `cli/src/parser.ts` and `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts` appear in chunk 1 at lines 95–96 but are absent from the claimed-files list at line 89. Add them before any RED work. Also name coverage for the subagent parse/dispatch path: `agent.ts` parses tool calls separately for the main agent and subagents, so the “same arguments” guarantee should cover both. Define that ambiguous or unsupported schema forms preserve `null` unless the schema proves it is disallowed.\n\n- **AC15:** The source-revision and archive-digest requirements are adequately testable if the revision is a trusted, out-of-band qualification input and is checked against a clean candidate checkout’s Git `HEAD`; the archive hash must be caller-pinned and checked against the exact private snapshot used for import. The plan’s tests cover mismatches and missing pins. Make the out-of-band trust boundary explicit so matrix evidence or installer provenance cannot supply the expected value.\n\n**WP-1105 F1–F3 status against the intended candidate:**\n\n- **F1, typecheck can pass without measuring anything — partly fixed, residual remains.** `2dbe565b` rejects generic missing-module failures, with coverage in [code_evaluators.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:190). But [typecheck_clean.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/evaluators/code/typecheck_clean.mjs:38) treats any `TS<number>` or Rust `E<number>` line as a recognized diagnostic; an identical recognized configuration failure can still pass. The release notes specifically identify TS5057 as an example ([v1.1.2.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md:62)). To close F1, add a regression for a recognized diagnostic that means the checker did not measure source, while retaining true TS/Rust diagnostic comparison.\n\n- **F2, candidate-controlled build configuration/checker inputs — partially fixed, still open.** Baseline configuration is now used and the test verifies candidate source errors remain visible ([code_evaluators.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:249)). But the allowlist silently ignores changed non-source inputs and overlays source-like files under `node_modules` or build helpers ([runner.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs:146), [runner.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs:187)). The run captures changed-path snapshots only for syntax/diff-boundary evaluators, not build-only tasks ([run.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/run.mjs:218)). Minimum closure: fail closed on changed paths outside an explicit source overlay, protect checker/config/dependency inputs during execution, and prove allowed source changes still reach the evaluator. Likely files: `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs`, `eval/evaluators/code/command.mjs` (or isolation code if mount policy changes), and `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts`.\n\n- **F3, syntax evaluation on deleted/non-source changes — fixed in the current source.** The default list filters to supported, existing source paths ([runner.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs:287)), with regression coverage ([code_evaluators.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release/cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:318)). Keep that test; no additional F3 source change is justified by this finding.\n\n**Claim/gate prerequisites:** The active `SUITE` claim is held by `claude-code` for the final gate in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/rg-final`; no validation should start until it is released. WP-1105’s earlier claim is released; reacquire all implementation and test files atomically before work. The current proposed test/implementation files do not show active claims, but that must be checked again at claim time."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828676.7514815,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3976}}
