{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:44:46.653Z","ordinal":114739,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba74d02b481a391c8336b52305ade","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The plan reviewer approved the core separation but requested tighter rules for gateway-auth freshness, successful catalogs that omit the selected model, and explicit parser/subagent file coverage. The reviewer also confirmed WP-1105 F3 is already fixed in the current candidate; F1 has a residual configuration-error false pass, and F2 still permits unsafe overlay inputs. I’m incorporating these comments before the next review."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793828685028,"completed_at_ms":1793828686653}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:44:46.656Z","ordinal":114740,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba74d02b481a391c8336b52305ade","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The plan reviewer approved the core separation but requested tighter rules for gateway-auth freshness, successful catalogs that omit the selected model, and explicit parser/subagent file coverage. The reviewer also confirmed WP-1105 F3 is already fixed in the current candidate; F1 has a residual configuration-error false pass, and F2 still permits unsafe overlay inputs. I’m incorporating these comments before the next review.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828685.0122948,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba74d02b481a391c8336b52305ade","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1a885-8b40-7a52-8045-ad3283b22026","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3977}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:45:19.562Z","ordinal":114741,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aeba74ea18081a388a7deb23afb3a4d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a123642b63de4cada247314a0afc1ebc","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a successful mismatching catalog clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` is sent only after a fresh positive gateway handshake by that client or an explicit operator override; unavailable/ambiguous refresh suppresses it until fresh verification. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation with matching model`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\\n+- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a readable catalog that omits or mismatches the selected model clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict request adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` authorization is per client and is valid for at most five minutes from a positive gateway handshake; endpoint/model change clears it, and any unavailable, ambiguous, or mismatching refresh suppresses it until that same client obtains a fresh positive gateway handshake. A new client cannot inherit header authorization from shared provider cache. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `successful catalog without selected model clears provider identity`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation and tokenize routing`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `gateway authorization expires and clears on endpoint or model change`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\\n@@\\n-- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema forbids null; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, while schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `native text and repaired tool calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\\n-- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted inputs: the declared source commit must equal the immutable candidate revision supplied by the qualification invocation, and archive SHA-256 must be required and match the exact archive copied into the private verified snapshot. A self-written provenance/source record cannot override either value. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\\n+- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation in both main-agent and subagent parse/dispatch paths. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema proves null is disallowed; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, and ambiguous or unsupported schema forms preserve null. Schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `main and subagent native text and repaired calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `ambiguous schema preserves explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\\n+- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted, out-of-band qualification inputs: the expected source commit is supplied independently of matrix evidence and installer provenance and must match the clean candidate checkout's Git HEAD; the expected archive SHA-256 is caller-pinned independently and must match the exact private archive snapshot used for verification and import. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\\n@@\\n-**Files:** `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`, and this plan. Existing context, token-counting, and standalone-profile tests already use the exact vLLM owner marker and a successful version route; they remain part of the final regression run without source edits. Atomically acquire an owner claim for every listed file before writing the first RED test; include any additional fixture/helper file in the claims before editing it.\\n+**Files:** `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`, and this plan. Existing context, token-counting, and standalone-profile tests remain part of the final regression run. Atomically acquire an owner claim for every listed file before writing the first RED test; include any additional fixture/helper file in the claims before editing it.\\n@@\\n-1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\\n-2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests.\\n+1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge` on both main-agent and subagent paths.\\n+2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests, including strict request adaptation and `/tokenize` routing after a warm `/version` outage.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828686.6332295}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:45:19.596Z","ordinal":114742,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-760154f6-b049-4f87-bcf0-a186d5a4c06b","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -75,3 +75,3 @@\n - **AC7:** In a real `write_file` and `run_command` dispatch through the Rust RPC bridge, vLLM strict-mode `null` values for originally optional `write_file.overwrite`, `run_command.background`, and `run_command.timeout_secs` are omitted before deserialization; required fields and non-null optional values are preserved, and both executors succeed. Test: `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n-- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a successful mismatching catalog clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` is sent only after a fresh positive gateway handshake by that client or an explicit operator override; unavailable/ambiguous refresh suppresses it until fresh verification. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation with matching model`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\n+- **AC8:** Provider adaptation/counting cache and task-class authorization are independent. Adaptation/counting may retain a positively identified kind for at most five minutes only for the same normalized endpoint and selected model; unavailable discovery retains that kind, while endpoint/model changes, expiry, or a readable catalog that omits or mismatches the selected model clear it. A warm vLLM `/version` failure retains strict request adaptation and `/tokenize` routing only when the prior owner-plus-version handshake is still within that bound and the current catalog still contains the matching vLLM model entry. `X-Task-Class` authorization is per client and is valid for at most five minutes from a positive gateway handshake; endpoint/model change clears it, and any unavailable, ambiguous, or mismatching refresh suppresses it until that same client obtains a fresh positive gateway handshake. A new client cannot inherit header authorization from shared provider cache. Tests: `provider adaptation cache is bounded by endpoint model and ttl`; `unavailable rediscovery retains prior provider kind`; `successful catalog without selected model clears provider identity`; `warm vllm version failure retains strict adaptation and tokenize routing`; `failed gateway refresh suppresses task class until reverified`; `gateway authorization expires and clears on endpoint or model change`; `new client cannot inherit gateway header authorization from shared cache`; `explicit task class override survives unavailable discovery`.\n - **AC9:** The matrix copies the archive into a private snapshot, verifies archive digest, installer provenance, manifest contents, exact file set and every file digest without following symlinks, then imports only from that same verified snapshot. A deterministic substitution of the installed runtime after snapshot verification and before import cannot affect the measured code. Test: `tool grammar matrix binds imported runtime to the verified archive snapshot`.\n@@ -81,4 +81,4 @@\n - **AC13:** Before matrix inference, every installed package file (apart from the installer-owned provenance record) must match the verified archive snapshot's exact file set and SHA-256 digests; a matching but forged provenance record cannot make a modified installed runtime qualify. Test `tool grammar matrix rejects installed runtime substitution with matching provenance` asserts rejection before any provider/client call and before evidence output is written.\n-- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema forbids null; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, while schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `native text and repaired tool calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\n-- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted inputs: the declared source commit must equal the immutable candidate revision supplied by the qualification invocation, and archive SHA-256 must be required and match the exact archive copied into the private verified snapshot. A self-written provenance/source record cannot override either value. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\n+- **AC14:** Each parsed tool call is normalized once into a canonical record before dispatch or observation in both main-agent and subagent parse/dispatch paths. The same canonical arguments drive executor dispatch, read tracking, observer classification, observation identity, and persisted assistant history for native, text-mode, and structurally repaired calls. Optional `null` is removed only when the active tool schema proves null is disallowed; nullable union/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`enum`/`const` values are preserved, and ambiguous or unsupported schema forms preserve null. Schema-invalid required null is rejected before dispatch. Raw syntax/repair classification remains available, and structurally repaired writes/exec calls remain fail-closed. Tests: `main and subagent native text and repaired calls share canonical arguments across dispatch tracking and history`; `nullable schema fields preserve explicit null`; `ambiguous schema preserves explicit null`; `required null fails before tool dispatch`; `repaired write and exec calls remain denied`.\n+- **AC15:** Matrix evidence binds the tested source revision and archive to trusted, out-of-band qualification inputs: the expected source commit is supplied independently of matrix evidence and installer provenance and must match the clean candidate checkout's Git HEAD; the expected archive SHA-256 is caller-pinned independently and must match the exact private archive snapshot used for verification and import. Tests: `tool grammar matrix rejects source commit mismatch before provider calls`; `tool grammar matrix requires pinned archive digest`; `tool grammar matrix rejects archive digest mismatch before provider calls`.\n \n@@ -88,3 +88,3 @@\n \n-**Files:** `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`, and this plan. Existing context, token-counting, and standalone-profile tests already use the exact vLLM owner marker and a successful version route; they remain part of the final regression run without source edits. Atomically acquire an owner claim for every listed file before writing the first RED test; include any additional fixture/helper file in the claims before editing it.\n+**Files:** `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/ui.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs`, `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`, and this plan. Existing context, token-counting, and standalone-profile tests remain part of the final regression run. Atomically acquire an owner claim for every listed file before writing the first RED test; include any additional fixture/helper file in the claims before editing it.\n \n@@ -94,4 +94,4 @@\n \n-1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge`.\n-2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests.\n+1. Normalize parsed calls once and schema-aware — files: `cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/parser_safety.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts`, `cli/test/vllm_nullable_dispatch.test.ts`; tests: all AC14 tests and `vllm nullable optional tool arguments execute through the Rust RPC bridge` on both main-agent and subagent paths.\n+2. Separate provider adaptation cache from header authorization — files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/task_class.test.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`; tests: all AC8 tests, including strict request adaptation and `/tokenize` routing after a warm `/version` outage.\n 3. Require positive vLLM identity — files: `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md`; tests: both AC10 tests plus existing context/token-counting and standalone-profile regressions in the full suite.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793828719594,"completed_at_ms":1793828719595}}
