{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:46:01.394Z","ordinal":114771,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a886-af31-7582-a62c-534941ebf07e","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED.** AC8 now separates the five-minute, endpoint-and-model keyed adaptation/counting cache from per-client gateway-header authorization. AC14 covers main-agent and subagent paths, schema-aware null handling, and its files are now listed in both the plan and chunks. AC15 identifies trusted out-of-band commit and archive inputs and names tests for mismatch and pin failures. The claimed files cover the planned chunks.\n\nOne stale statement remains in the risk section: [WP-1107-PLAN.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-plan/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:107) says an unavailable `/models` refresh keeps a same-URL gateway identity. That conflicts with AC8’s rule to suppress `X-Task-Class` after an unavailable or ambiguous refresh. Update the risk text to distinguish temporary adaptation-cache retention from per-client header authorization; then the plan is ready to approve. No tests or edits were made."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a879-e2d7-72f2-87a2-e9ee9357fdf7","create_time":1793828761.3937657,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":3980}}
