-af 'make test|npm test|node .*run_tests|test-gate|rg-final' | head -20"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"284:scope: Evidence-bounded Cloudflare Artifacts research, agent-native collaboration design, and a minimal Workers/Artifacts/Git contest path for `/home/mike/nexus-code`; use for proof sequencing and claim boundaries, not as a general production-integration claim.\n340:- when researching platform capability, the user required consequential claims to be labeled `DOCUMENTED`, `OBSERVED`, `INFERRED`, `HYPOTHESIS`, or `UNKNOWN` -> never turn documentation into observed behavior, and retain authoritative-source discrepancies. [Task 1]\n353:- CTX-001, CTX-002, and EXT-004 remain Issue #12 closure blockers even when bounded for a demo; do not claim broad prompt provenance or production readiness. [Task 4]\n389:- CAP (7), AUTH (12), CTX (11), DATA (9), and UI (7) are explicit requirements. The claimed total of 59 includes `EXEC-001..013` traceability rows, which lack independent normative requirement statements. [Task 1]\n486:- when evaluating claimed fixes or model safety, the user rejected cosmetic diffs and a single successful run -> require failing-before/passing-after behavioral evidence and independent validation; preserve uncertainty where boundary evidence is incomplete. [Task 1][Task 2]\n499:- Symptom: an isolated run does not prove the intended claim. Cause: a narrow allowlist denied generic fixture Python commands and the model wrote only an ad-hoc print script. Fix: allow only explicit safe test-command patterns while retaining destructive-Git denies; stop and report the reproduction incomplete if it lacks a failing assertion. [Task 2]\n518:- do not claim qualification from configuration or historical reports alone; reconcile declared state against live evidence and preserve unresolved gaps. [Task 1]\n532:- Stop rule: the required five reports and final decision portfolio were not produced. Do not claim completion or qualification; continue only within the read-only boundary unless authorization changes. [Task 1]\n536:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (worktree used: /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration); reuse_rule=claim the source/test slice, use a temporary HOME, and revalidate against the current branch because this records an isolated focused success.\n564:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code and isolated Nexus release worktrees; reuse_rule=recheck live claims, exact heads/tags/artifacts, CI, acceptance documents, and release state; heads, PRs, and incomplete gates here are time-specific.\n566:## Task 1: Integrate CI prerequisite and record claimed readiness handoff, integration succeeded; qualification blocked\n584:- power-failure, recovery, dirty checkout, PR #66, v1/security-terminal-summary, c2f6d2a58f8b2c20d7702556b54a5b3699518cf1, nexus-claims, boot ID, PR #56, PR #60, PR #61, exact-head CI, CONCURRENCY.md\n614:- RC14, v1/integration, requirements-enforce, nexus-claims, held-out-custody, SHA256SUMS, provider-qualification, OpenRouter, ChatGPT sign-in, PR #354, 4de9d398\n618:- when recovering Nexus release state, the user said “Do not edit the shared dirty checkout” and “Preserve all uncommitted and unrelated work” -> inspect read-only and make changes only in a claimed worktree. [Task 2]\n619:- when deciding whether a claim is live, verify host identity, boot identity, process start time, command, and working directory; a stale PID/claim record is not ownership. [Task 2]\n624:- PR #10 exact head `bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0` passed CI `39085388798` and merged to `v1/integration` as `2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2`; this was source/CI acceptance, not release qualification. Its claimed readiness artifacts and held-out payload remained out of bounds. [Task 1]\n625:- Recovery concurrency procedure: first read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, work state, claims, PRs, and worktrees; use one claimed slice/worktree, isolated HOME/XDG, snapshot-based full suites, `GATEWAY` claims for inference, no `pkill -f`/`killall`, and owner-only push/tag/publish. [Task 2][Task 3]\n626:- Boot evidence proves reboot only, not application power-loss recovery. Verify durable post-reboot state directly; a WSL path in a claim and a newly recreated tmpfs do not prove retained state. [Task 2]\n633:- Related skill: skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md. [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n637:- Do not take PR #56, PR #60, PR #61, evaluator, or qualification-host claims without explicit handoff. Green checks on a stale remote head do not validate an independently reviewed replacement; reconcile the exact reviewed head and rerun exact-head CI. [Task 2]\n## v1/v112-release...origin/v1/v112-release [ahead 2]\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\n822c08fb (HEAD -> v1/v112-release) fix(step): --step pauses after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\nc5ceb2e5 test(step): --step must pause after a cycle of parallel read_file calls\nfafbf6d5 (origin/v1/v112-release) docs(release): correct WP-1107 scope and the review record\n40d553b5 docs(release): v1.1.2 release notes and qualification record\nfafbf6d598372f12c045cd08ab623b0c95f884ae\trefs/heads/v1/v112-release\n--- .git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json\n{\"agent\": \"claude-code\", \"host\": \"mike-dev\", \"branch\": \"detached-822c08fb\", \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rg-final\", \"since\": \"2026-11-04T20:27:30Z\", \"heartbeat\": \"2026-11-04T21:23:29Z\", \"scope\": \"v1.1.2 SECOND final exact-head gate on 822c08fb (worktree rg-final): make build, make test (cargo + npm test incl. terminal scope + security gates) with the CI fixture env vars set; reason: owner-approved fix of the --step parallel-read pause (Entire HIGH)\"}--- .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_agent.ts/owner.json\n{\"agent\":\"claude-code\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/v112-release\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release\",\"since\":\"2026-11-04