{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:49:23.520Z","ordinal":114890,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a888-863c-7650-846b-5ba747dc86a9","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aeba85bfe0c81a386ace5aacd44da0e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I rechecked the live state. The `822c08fb` exact-head gate is green, but PR #402 still points to `fafbf6d5`; the local release branch is two commits ahead, and I found no v1.1.2 tag. PR #402’s body still says the findings are waived, which conflicts with your direction to fix them in v1.1.2.\n\nThe WP-1107 remediation plan is independently approved. I logged a handoff request for WP-1107 and WP-1105 in the shared claims log. The `SUITE` and `agent.ts` claims remain with `claude-code`, so I have not started tests or overlapping edits. The release target remains v1.1.2; v1.1.0 is not being republished.\n\nNEXUS-STATUS\n- agent: Nexus-Release-Agent\n- item: WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\n- phase: PLAN approved; implementation awaiting handoff\n- claim: WP-1107 plan held; `SUITE` and `agent.ts` still owner-held\n- heartbeat: 2026-11-04 21:49 UTC\n- gate: test=PASS, types=PASS, lint=PASS on local `822c08fb` only\n- retrieval: `nexus-cli`, `agent.ts:2905` and `agent.ts:3053`\n- next: Begin RED-first implementation after explicit claim handoff.\n- friction: Owner-held claims block tests and overlapping edits.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":562,"lineEnd":564,"note":"rechecked live release claims and exact heads"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"started_at_ms":1793828956022,"completed_at_ms":1793828963520}}
