{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:50:14.043Z","ordinal":114914,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a88a-3a3a-7d70-b8fc-9383df12dec7","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a88a-3a3a-7d70-b8fc-9383df12dec7","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aeba88e74d081a38fcaaadb7b43f18b","usage":{"input_tokens":160902,"cached_input_tokens":158848,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":395,"reasoning_output_tokens":247,"total_tokens":161297},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":319882,"cached_input_tokens":314880,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":981,"reasoning_output_tokens":468,"total_tokens":320863},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2358360841,"cached_input_tokens":2340639744,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4316918,"reasoning_output_tokens":2080392,"total_tokens":2362677759}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:50:14.267Z","ordinal":114915,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a88a-3a3a-7d70-b8fc-9383df12dec7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32f74b35-8876-41dd-9939-eca03c193f0c","process_id":"95788","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"---\nname: nexus-release-qualification\ndescription: Coordinate or verify a Nexus RC/release lane when claims, exact-head CI, artifact integrity, reproducibility, or installed-PTY qualification are in scope.\nargument-hint: \"[rc-version or release lane]\"\nuser-invocable: false\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n\n# Nexus Release Qualification\n\n## When to use\n\n- The task concerns a Nexus v1 RC/release lane, recovery after an interrupted run, or an exact-artifact qualification claim.\n- The task needs to distinguish source/CI acceptance, artifact evidence, installed-RC qualification, and publication.\n- Do not use this to bypass another owner's claim, access held-out material, or publish/tag/push without explicit ownership.\n\n## Inputs / context to gather\n\n1. Read `/home/mike/nexus-code/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md`, current work state, `.git/nexus-claims`, worktrees, and relevant PR/CI exact heads.\n2. Snapshot the shared checkout's branch, HEAD, porcelain state, and ownership before any mutation. Treat a dirty shared checkout as read-only.\n3. For `$ARGUMENTS`, identify the exact tag, source commit, archive digest, installed artifact path, claims, and gate(s) requested.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Establish ownership. Verify host identity, boot identity if recovery is involved, process start time, command, working directory, and claim age. Obtain explicit handoff before touching another lane.\n2. Work only in a claimed isolated worktree with isolated `HOME`/XDG state. Claim `SUITE` before a full matrix and `GATEWAY` before synthetic gateway work. Never use `pkill -f` or `killall`.\n3. Separate status: source test/CI, independent review, artifact integrity, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC scripted PTY, held-out/provider/standalone acceptance, and publication. Report each gate separately.\n4. For artifact integrity, verify tag object -> source commit -> archive digest; compare release metadata, `SHA256SUMS`, provenance/SBOM/manifests, installer/version/help, and evidence packet checksum index. Preserve byte-faithful API captures.\n5. For reproducibility, build the exact RC on distinct runners, compare runner outputs to each other and public assets byte-for-byte, then retain checksum evidence. Avoid overlapping full CI matrices.\n6. For installed PTY qualification, rerun every required scripted scenario against the freshly installed exact artifact using isolated HOME/workspace and process-cleanup evidence. Do not substitute historic notes or source-level tests.\n7. For cancellation remediation, confirm child liveness before cancel; assert `INTERRUPTED`, settled outstanding tool state, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Compare only with an exact archived RC core.\n\n## Efficiency plan\n\n- Read claims/topology once and cache exact head/tag/digest plus gate status in the work-state update.\n- Run focused gate-specific checks before any serialized full suite. Cancel only an identified duplicate suite, never a different owner’s run.\n- Stop a readiness claim immediately when an exact-artifact or ownership invariant is missing; record the unresolved gate rather than broadening scope.\n\n## Pitfalls and fixes\n\n- Green CI or an accepted source review is not RC/product qualification -> require the exact installed artifact and documented acceptance gates.\n- Reboot, tmpfs recreation, or an inaccessible WSL path is not durable recovery evidence -> inspect durable state on the actual host/filesystem.\n- `release-assets.json` is an object -> enumerate `.assets`.\n- A dirty checkout can make `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` fail on cleanliness -> use a clean committed snapshot for that gate.\n- Sidecar tests do not prove TUI Escape behavior -> rerun the exact-artifact scripted PTY scenario.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n- Shared checkout was preserved; worktree, claims, and isolated HOME/XDG are recorded.\n- Exact head/tag/artifact digest and CI state are recorded.\n- Every stated gate has a separate pass/fail/unverified disposition.\n- Artifact and reproducibility evidence includes retained checksums.\n- Installed-RC PTY evidence is fresh, exact-artifact, and includes process cleanup.\n- Held-out, owner-only, and publication boundaries were preserved.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":38613}},"started_at_ms":1793829014267,"completed_at_ms":1793829014267}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T21:50:14.475Z","ordinal":114916,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a88a-8bcb-7090-9f91-605fd45513db","call_id":"call_48502a8701a44861acbe73364569ca4f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: nexus-release-qualification\ndescription: Coordinate or verify a Nexus RC/release lane when claims, exact-head CI, artifact integrity, reproducibility, or installed-PTY qualification are in scope.\nargument-hint: \"[rc-version or release lane]\"\nuser-invocable: false\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n\n# Nexus Release Qualification\n\n## When to use\n\n- The task concerns a Nexus v1 RC/release lane, recovery after an interrupted run, or an exact-artifact qualification claim.\n- The task needs to distinguish source/CI acceptance, artifact evidence, installed-RC qualification, and publication.\n- Do not use this to bypass another owner's claim, access held-out material, or publish/tag/push without explicit ownership.\n\n## Inputs / context to gather\n\n1. Read `/home/mike/nexus-code/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md`, current work state, `.git/nexus-claims`, worktrees, and relevant PR/CI exact heads.\n2. Snapshot the shared checkout's branch, HEAD, porcelain state, and ownership before any mutation. Treat a dirty shared checkout as read-only.\n3. For `$ARGUMENTS`, identify the exact tag, source commit, archive digest, installed artifact path, claims, and gate(s) requested.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Establish ownership. Verify host identity, boot identity if recovery is involved, process start time, command, working directory, and claim age. Obtain explicit handoff before touching another lane.\n2. Work only in a claimed isolated worktree with isolated `HOME`/XDG state. Claim `SUITE` before a full matrix and `GATEWAY` before synthetic gateway work. Never use `pkill -f` or `killall`.\n3. Separate status: source test/CI, independent review, artifact integrity, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC scripted PTY, held-out/provider/standalone acceptance, and publication. Report each gate separately.\n4. For artifact integrity, verify tag object -> source commit -> archive digest; compare release metadata, `SHA256SUMS`, provenance/SBOM/manifests, installer/version/help, and evidence packet checksum index. Preserve byte-faithful API captures.\n5. For reproducibility, build the exact RC on distinct runners, compare runner outputs to each other and public assets byte-for-byte, then retain checksum evidence. Avoid overlapping full CI matrices.\n6. For installed PTY qualification, rerun every required scripted scenario against the freshly installed exact artifact using isolated HOME/workspace and process-cleanup evidence. Do not substitute historic notes or source-level tests.\n7. For cancellation remediation, confirm child liveness before cancel; assert `INTERRUPTED`, settled outstanding tool state, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Compare only with an exact archived RC core.\n\n## Efficiency plan\n\n- Read claims/topology once and cache exact head/tag/digest plus gate status in the work-state update.\n- Run focused gate-specific checks before any serialized full suite. Cancel only an identified duplicate suite, never a different owner’s run.\n- Stop a readiness claim immediately when an exact-artifact or ownership invariant is missing; record the unresolved gate rather than broadening scope.\n\n## Pitfalls and fixes\n\n- Green CI or an accepted source review is not RC/product qualification -> require the exact installed artifact and documented acceptance gates.\n- Reboot, tmpfs recreation, or an inaccessible WSL path is not durable recovery evidence -> inspect durable state on the actual host/filesystem.\n- `release-assets.json` is an object -> enumerate `.assets`.\n- A dirty checkout can make `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` fail on cleanliness -> use a clean committed snapshot for that gate.\n- Sidecar tests do not prove TUI Escape behavior -> rerun the exact-artifact scripted PTY scenario.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n- Shared checkout was preserved; worktree, claims, and isolated HOME/XDG are recorded.\n- Exact head/tag/artifact digest and CI state are recorded.\n- Every stated gate has a separate pass/fail/unverified disposition.\n- Artifact and reproducibility evidence includes retained checksums.\n- Installed-RC PTY evidence is fresh, exact-artifact, and includes process cleanup.\n- Held-out, owner-only, and publication boundaries were preserved.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a88a-3a3a-7d70-b8fc-9383df12dec7","create_time":1793829014.4754663}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
